[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The Fibonacci sequence is the sequence 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, $\ldots$ where each term is the sum of the previous two terms. What is the remainder when the $100^{\mathrm{th}}$ term of the sequence is divided by 4?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the remainder when the 100th term of the Fibonacci sequence is divided by 4, we can use the property of the Fibonacci sequence that it repeats every 30 terms. This is because the sequence is periodic with a period of 30. Therefore, we can find the remainder of the 100th term by finding the remainder of 100 divided by 30.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 100 \div 30 = 3 \text{ remainder } 10
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This means that 100 is 30 more than a multiple of 30. Therefore, the remainder when 100 is divided by 30 is 10. So, the remainder when the 100th term of the Fibonacci sequence is divided by 4 is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{10}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Model Response]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>system
