[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m What is the remainder when $13^{51}$ is divided by 5?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the remainder when 13^51 is divided by 5, we need to understand the pattern of the remainders when dividing by 5. Notice that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[13 \equiv 3 \pmod{5}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[13^2 \equiv 3^2 \equiv 9 \equiv 4 \pmod{5}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[13^3 \equiv 3^3 \equiv 27 \equiv 2 \pmod{5}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[13^4 \equiv 3^4 \equiv 81 \equiv 1 \pmod{5}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From this pattern, we can observe that for any power of 13 modulo 5, the remainder will always be 3 modulo 5. This is because each time we multiply by 13 and divide by 5, we take the remainder and multiply by 4 if the power is even, or by 1 if the power is odd.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, for 13^51, the following calculations give us the remainders:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[13^1 \equiv 3 \pmod{5}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[13^2 \equiv 4 \pmod{5}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[13^3 \equiv 2 \pmod{5}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[13^4 \equiv 1 \pmod{5}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[13^5 \equiv 4 \cdot 13^4 \equiv 4 \cdot 1 \equiv 4 \pmod{5}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[13^6 \equiv 4 \cdot 13^5 \equiv 4 \cdot 4 \equiv 16 \equiv 1 \pmod{5}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[13^7 \equiv 13^3 \equiv 2 \pmod{5}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[13^8 \equiv 13^6 \equiv 1 \pmod{5}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In general, we see that for any power \( n \), the pattern is that \( n \equiv 3 \pmod{5} \). Therefore, for \( n = 51 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[13^{51} \equiv 3^{51} \pmod{5}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We simplify further by reducing modulo 5:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[3^{51} \mod 5\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(3^4 \equiv 1 \pmod{5}\), we can write:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[3^{51} = (3^4)^{12} \cdot 3^3 \equiv 1^{12} \cdot 3^3 \equiv 3^3 \equiv 27 \equiv 2 \pmod{5}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the remainder when \(13^{51}\) is divided by 5 is \(\boxed{2}\).<|endoftext|>
