[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Compute $\sin 210^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute \(\sin 210^\circ\), we can use the sine subtraction formula. The formula for the sine of the angle \(\theta = 210^\circ\) is \(\sin(\theta) = \sin(180^\circ + \theta) = -\sin(\theta)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, note that \(210^\circ\) is equivalent to \(210^\circ - 180^\circ = 30^\circ\). So, \(\sin 210^\circ = \sin(30^\circ)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We know from trigonometry that \(\sin 30^\circ = \frac{1}{2}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, \(\sin 210^\circ = -\sin 30^\circ = -\frac{1}{2}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Putting this answer in the required format, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \(\boxed{-\frac{1}{2}}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Ground Truth]
