[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute \(\cos 30^\circ\), we will use the angle addition formula for cosine, which is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos(a + b) = \cos a \cos b - \sin a \sin b
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we need the values of \(\cos 30^\circ\) and \(\sin 30^\circ\). The value of \(\sin 30^\circ\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \sin 30^\circ = \frac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The value of \(\cos 30^\circ\) can be found using the half-angle formula. For an angle \(\frac{\theta}{2}\), the cosine is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos \left(\frac{\theta}{2}\right) = \sqrt{\frac{1 + \cos \theta}{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In this case, \(\theta = 60^\circ\), so we need to find \(\cos 60^\circ\). The cosine of 60 degrees is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 60^\circ = \frac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substituting \(\theta = 60^\circ\) into the half-angle formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 30^\circ = \sqrt{\frac{1 + \frac{1}{2}}{2}} = \sqrt{\frac{\frac{3}{2}}{2}} = \sqrt{\frac{3}{4}} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 30^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Putting this final answer in the required format, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}}
