[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(AB = 7\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(AC = 10\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Let \(AX = 4\) and \(AY = 6\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Let \(BC = z\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Use the coordinates of the points:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Place \(C\) at \((0, 0)\) and \(B\) at \((7, 0)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Place \(A\) at \((x, y)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Determine \(x\) and \(y\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Since \(AX = 4\) and \(AY = 6\), \(A\) is 12 units away from \(B\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Using the distance formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \sqrt{x^2 + y^2} = 12
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      x^2 + y^2 = 144
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Since \(AB = 7\), \(A\) is on the y-axis.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      |x| = 7 \quad \text{so} \quad x = 7 \quad (\text{since } y \geq 0)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Substitute \(x = 7\) into the distance equation:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    7^2 + y^2 = 144
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    49 + y^2 = 144
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    y^2 = 95
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    y = \pm \sqrt{95}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. **Determine \(z\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Since \(AC = 10\), the length of \(BC\) is \(z\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(z\) is the distance between \(C\) and \(B\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Using the distance formula again:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      |z - 7| = 10
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      z = 17 \quad (\text{since } z \geq -3)
