[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 7. **Calculate the coordinates of point \(A\) and \(B\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Point \(A\) is at \((7, 0)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Point \(B\) is at \((7, 0)\) (since \(A\) and \(B\) are symmetrically placed on the y-axis).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 8. **Determine the area of triangle \(ABC\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times AB \times AC = \frac{1}{2} \times 7 \times 10 = 35
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 9. **Calculate the area of triangle \(AXY\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Point \(A\) is at \((7, 0)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Point \(Y\) is at \((6, 0)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Point \(X\) is at \((4, 6)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Using the formula for the area of a triangle given vertices \((x_1, y_1)\), \((x_2, y_2)\), and \((x_3, y_3)\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| 7(0 - 6) + 6(6 - 0) + 4(0 - 0) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| 7(-6) + 6(6) + 4(0) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| -42 + 36 + 0 \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| -6 + 36 \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| 30 \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times 30 = 15
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 10. **Calculate the ratio of the areas:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     \text{Ratio} = \frac{\text{Area of } \triangle AXY}{\text{Area of } \triangle ABC} = \frac{15}{35}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 11. **Simplify the ratio:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     \text{Ratio} = \frac{15 \div 5}{35 \div 5} = \frac{3}{7}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the ratio of the area of triangle \(AXY\) to the area of triangle \(ABC\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\frac{3}{7}}
