[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The mean of one set of five numbers is 13, and the mean of a separate set of six numbers is 24. What is the mean of the set of all eleven numbers?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The mean of one set of five numbers is 13, so the sum of all numbers in the first set is $13*5 = 65$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Similarly, the mean of the other set of six numbers is 24, so the sum of all numbers in the second set is $24*6 = 144$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, to find the mean of the set of all eleven numbers, we can sum the two means and divide by the sum of the two numbers (13+24).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the mean of the set of all eleven numbers is $\frac{(65+144)}{13+24} = \boxed{12.5}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ####
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The answer is 12.5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
