[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Divide the leading term**: Divide the leading term of the dividend \(7x^6\) by the leading term of the divisor \(x\), which gives \(7x^5\). Write \(7x^5\) above the division symbol.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Multiply and subtract**: Multiply \(7x^5\) by \(x + 2\) to get \(7x^6 + 14x^5\). Subtract this from the original polynomial:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    (7x^6 + 3x^5 - 3x^3 - 7x^2 - 6x - 2) - (7x^6 + 14x^5) = -11x^5 - 3x^3 - 7x^2 - 6x - 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Repeat the process**: Divide the new leading term \(-11x^5\) by \(x\) to get \(-11x^4\). Write \(-11x^4\) above the division symbol. Multiply \(-11x^4\) by \(x + 2\) to get \(-11x^5 - 22x^4\). Subtract this from the current polynomial:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    (-11x^5 - 3x^3 - 7x^2 - 6x - 2) - (-11x^5 - 22x^4) = 22x^4 - 7x^2 - 6x - 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. **Continue dividing**: Divide the new leading term \(22x^4\) by \(x\) to get \(22x^3\). Write \(22x^3\) above the division symbol. Multiply \(22x^3\) by \(x + 2\) to get \(22x^4 + 44x^3\). Subtract this from the current polynomial:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    (22x^4 - 7x^2 - 6x - 2) - (22x^4 + 44x^3) = -44x^3 - 7x^2 - 6x - 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6. **Repeat again**: Divide the new leading term \(-44x^3\) by \(x\) to get \(-44x^2\). Write \(-44x^2\) above the division symbol. Multiply \(-44x^2\) by \(x + 2\) to get \(-44x^3 - 88x^2\). Subtract this from the current polynomial:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    (-44x^3 - 7x^2 - 6x - 2) - (-44x^3 - 88x^2) = 81x^2 - 6x - 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 7. **Continue**: Divide the new leading term \(81x^2\) by \(x\) to get \(81x\). Write \(81x\) above the division symbol. Multiply \(81x\) by \(x + 2\) to get \(81x^2 + 162x\). Subtract this from the current polynomial:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
