[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The quotient is the polynomial above the division symbol, and the remainder is \(-334\). Therefore, the quotient of \(7x^6 + 3x^5 - 3x^3 - 7x^2 - 6x - 2\) when divided by \(x + 2\) is \(\boxed{7x^5 - 11x^4 + 22x^3 - 44x^2 + 81x - 168}\).<|endoftext|>
