[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 9 = x + y   (since their sum is 9)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 153 = x^2 + y^2   (since their squares sum to 153)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can substitute x in the second equation with 9 to simplify the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 153 = 9^2 + y^2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 153 = 81 + y^2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we can subtract 81 from both sides to isolate y:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
