[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve the expression $(-5)^3 + (-2)^3 + 2^3 + 5^3$, we first need to simplify the exponents part. The expression can be rearranged as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $(-5)^3 = -125$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $(-2)^3 = -8$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $2^3$ remains as $2^3 = 8$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $5^3 = 125$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we will add all the together step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $-125 + (-8) + 8 + 125$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's start with the addition of the negative terms:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $-125 - 8 = -133$
