[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's start by fixing the circular nature of the seating arrangement. In a circular arrangement, rotating the arrangement doesn't change the number of arrangements. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, let's assume there are 6 people seated in 7 seats. To find the number of ways to arrange them seated in a circular manner, we make use of the concept of circular permutations. Circular permutations of \(n\) distinct objects occur \(n-1\) times.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m That is, there are \(6-1=5\) circular permutations of the people in a round.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Hence the number of ways to arrange 6 people following the seating arrangement in a circle with 7 seats will be \(5\). 
