[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m What is $441_{10}$ in base $7$?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To convert $441_{10}$ to base $7$, we need to divide the decimal number by $7$ iteratively and keep track of the quotient and remainder. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. First, we divide $441$ by $7$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 441 \div 7 = 63 \text{ remainder } 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, $441_{10}$ in base $10$ is $63$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. We then take the quotient from the division process, which is $63$, and divide it by $7$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 63 \div 7 = 9 \text{ remainder } 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, $63$ in base $10$ is $90_7$ because $63_{10} = 9 \cdot 7^1 + 0 \cdot 7^0$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. We take the quotient from the previous step, $9$, and divide it by $7$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 9 \div 7 = 1 \text{ remainder } 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, $9$ in base $10$ is $12_7$ because $9_{10} = 1 \cdot 7^1 + 2 \cdot 7^0$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. Finally, we take the quotient from the previous step, $1$, and divide it by $7$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1 \div 7 = 0 \text{ remainder } 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, $1$ in base $10$ is $1_7$ because $1_{10} = 1 \cdot 7^0$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Putting it all together, $441_{10}$ in base $7$ is $120_{7}$, because $12_{10} = 2 \cdot 7^1 + 0 \cdot 7^0 = 12 \cdot 7^1 + 0 \cdot 7^0$. Therefore, the answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{120_7}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
