[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In a rectangular coordinate system, the line $3y = x$ intersects the line $2x + 5y = 11$ at point $A$. What is the sum of the coordinates of point $A$?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the coordinates of the intersection point, we need to solve the system of linear equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3y = x & 2x + 5y = 11
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [/pre]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can use the substitution method or elimination method. Here, I'll use the elimination method:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we can multiply the first equation by 2 to make the coefficients of x the same in both equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6y = 2x & 10x + 10y = 22
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we can subtract the second equation from the first:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6y - (10x + 10y) = 2x - 22
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6y - 10x - 10y = 2x - 22
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -4x - 10y = -22
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now we have two equations with two variables:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -4x - 10y = -22 & 2y = -4x + 11
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we can solve for x and y:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we can solve for y from the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2y = -4x + 11
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m y = -\frac{4}{2}x + \frac{11}{2} 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m y = -2x + \frac{11}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we can use the first equation to substitute x:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -4x - 10(-2x + \frac{11}{2}) = -22
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -4x + 20x - 55 = -22
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 16x - 55 = -22
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 16x = 33
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = \frac{33}{16}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now substitute x back into the second equation to find y:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{11}{2} = -2(\frac{33}{16}) + \frac{11}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{11}{2} = -\frac{66}{16} + \frac{11}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{11}{2} = -\frac{66}{16} + \frac{88}{16}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{11}{2} = \frac{22}{16}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 11 = 2.25
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 11 = 2.25
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the coordinates of the intersection are (3, 2).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
