[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In this passage, it seems there might be confusion regarding the unit of measure used in the equation representing the probability of Gimli having more heads than Legolas. The equation given (P(Gimli > Legolas) = 1 - 1/2) uses both the number of heads displayed on the flipped coins (2008H and 2009H) and the uniform distribution (both probability = 1/2). To determine the probability of Artem having more heads than Geordi, you would need to use the probabilities associated with each coin flip, which is typically given in terms of the product of the individual coin probabilities or in a different form whose sum is always equal to 1 (when the coins are fair). Without additional context, it's challenging to determine the exact wording or precise values of the specific coins or their respective probabilities. 
