[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Before attempting to identify the specific wording, consider if the equation used had to be understood accurately:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. The binomial distribution ($X \sim Bin(n,p)$) is the distribution of the number of successes in $n$ independent Bernoulli trials.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The term "else $X \sb q$" likely refers to the generalized binomial distribution ($X \sb q \sim Bin\left(n, q\right)$) or the hypergeometric distribution when the specific coins are known and either fair or not. 
