[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m I won a trip for four to the Super Bowl.  I can bring three of my friends.  I have 8 friends.  In how many ways can I form my Super Bowl party?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Certainly, let's break this down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Total number of ways to choose 3 out of 8 friends:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Totalitions = \(\binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In this case, \( n = 8 \) and \( k = 3 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Totalitions = \(\binom{8}{3}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This calculation involves the binomial coefficient, which typically is represented as \(\frac{8!}{3!(8-3)!} = \frac{8!}{3!5!}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Calculate \( 8! \) (8 factorial) as \(8 \times 7 \times 6 \times 5!\) and \(\binom{8}{3}\) is the number of combinations, which equals \( \frac{8!}{3!5!} \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This gives us the total number of ways to choose 3 out of 8 friends, which in terms of permutations is \(\binom{8}{3} = \frac{8!}{3!5!} = 56\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # meaning
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, you can choose 3 friends from 8 in \(\boxed{56}\) different ways.
