[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **One root costs one mineral.**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - We have three roots and five minerals.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - One root is incompatible with two minerals.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Order does not matter.**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - For example, using roots 1 and 2 for root A and minerals A and B is the same as using roots 2 and 1 for root B.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Same three roots can't be used in combination with three other roots.**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's consider each root separately before moving on to the other combinations.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Root Compatibility
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since one root is incompatible with two minerals, we first choose which two minerals are incompatible. There are \(\binom{5}{2} = 10\) ways to do this. 
