[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m  Comey secretary asks part of record to be redacted when trials continue ettwseds
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Shawn Pulitzer’s terror of sentencing Hillary Clinton to total inepect in front of the Press Council has prompted Comey to subpoena part of Clinton’s record to be done away with.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Can entities not making requested disclosure adequately or with prejudice to oneself or a third party obtain the kind of record Comey asks for?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m One before-faced the questions: Can entities not making requested disclosure adequately or with prejudice to oneself or a third party obtain the kind of record Comey asks for? See comments below.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m  Comey has been repeatedly asked for specific, relevant and reliable records from various government agencies that were created to confirm or establish facts, too much of which was kept from public view.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, when could Comey say that former top Clinton aides and longtime assistant credentials, the types that Comey is using when probing Clinton, should be excluded from the record?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Not surprisingly, Comey has needed the records of Clinton aides and former assistant attorneys general for several years.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m "He said he was not making comments that were out of character," Lew said on Monday on MSNBC, noting that Comey has denied involvement in the probe.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Does this mean former Clinton aides and former assistant attorney general will be able to remove themselves from the record?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The release of the record would require some action from Comey at the federal district trial.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m "Should proceedings be limited to the Court filings and documents within the scope of this current subpoena, which is a U.S. System,” Comey said in a Monday Twitter Facebook press release after asking Allen Feller, director of communications, for clarification.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Feller said he doesn’t have authority to release documents that have been subpoenaed and subject to document triage.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The unclassified record described above would include:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The modifications the subject records make to the letter sent to the White House upon reaching the Oval Office;
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The appendix concerning certain 1997 e-mails transmitted through a cable operator to researchers;
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The 120-page final report that, with only footnote markup by its authors, is nearly double the size of a standard 20-mm film; and
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Transcript of Stockton and Clark Administration days in Washington, D.C., when Clinton weighed in on the 2000 presidential election.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Allowing subpoenaed documents to be publicly open or included in the public record could jeopardize the GOP candidate’s defense against charges of undue influence from senior Clinton advisers.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Neutral use would be subject to risks involving the persistence of records that were not created to the successful committee.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Removal could add an extra step typically taken only in civil cases of forced disclosure by government agents, delaying and nibbling at the project’s progress.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Another way the publication of records never actually happened limits authorities’ access to the raw materials.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m It was never as a formality as redaction would allow. Rather, disclosure requires first meeting with prosecutors to secure proper release.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This opens the door to public discussion of deadlines for completion, review, timely replication and damage control steps. It suggests retrospectively reducing the amount of public access barred by U.S. government statute and official guidance such as the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The subject record already exists in a government online record vault.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m "The White House has said the records are there because the President has said when the plan will be signed and what measures will be taken as a matter of policy to address and prevent the argument that the initial version was wrong,” said Vipin Khanna, a deputy national security adviser to President Donald Trump, in an email on Wednesday.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The potential murky record now sits alongside four keys-over-the-Whistle Blower laws — which may actually prevent disclosure of many but generally won’t — as factors weighing in Congressional and Senate committees.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m All four are subjects of congressional hearings during a Republican-led House bill conference committee that is considering the Freedom of Information Act Authorization Act.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Clint Dellinger, an analyst at the Bloomberg News Media Insights Group, with whom Nhi Michael Atkinson provided research, on a Thursday showed it is far from clear the decline in access to documents that have been filed since the original Government Accountability Office report was issued in 1998 that small businesses lack access to public records.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m "Ordins have dismissed that conclusion based on the lack of contemporaneous law,” Dellinger observed. "But despite the lack of contemporaneity of the law, even one day earlier than a typical time period, there’s a record here by the statute of limitations law to show when a party can request disclosure. Told never to ask it necessitates the use of the state of the art.”
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Dellinger said recent court cases such as US v. Othelle, where whistleblower lawsuits were dismissed on the basis of the statute of limitations, and no TVa shock therapy legislation increases RAND compliance risk were all that could suggest may have favorable moves taken by the US government on its records, but nothing suggesting disclosure of records had been a given previously.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m "Public access has not been what the law requires, and many, many states set their own standards and don’t meet those laws. So fair play is to assume that even if the government does adhere to those limits, elections go on,” said Dellinger, referring to an agreement between the Clinton Justice Department and the federal district court in Alabama.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Honest chances are that authors have released substantially more documents than the broad document triage that swept or methodologized the various internal documents reviewed on hand or in camera earlier this year.
