[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m How many multiples of $17$ are greater than $-50$ and less than $50$?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let me think for a while.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Okay, I'll start.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To have "17" as a divisor,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m There exists = $x$ as a divisor so that $17x\ge -50\text{(so that X is larger)}$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m And, 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $17x<50$ (so that X is smaller).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m That is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $17\times \left(\dfrac{-50}{x}\right)\ge -50$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m And,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $17\times \left(\dfrac{50}{x}\right)<50$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can simplify the first inequality and the second inequality.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $17\times \left(\dfrac{-50}{x}\right)\ge -50$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Then, divide both sides by 17. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $-50\ge -50\times\left(\dfrac{17}{17}\right)$ 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $x\ge 50$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m And, 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $17\times \left(\dfrac{50}{x}\right)<50$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Then, divide both sides by 17. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $50\le 50\times\left(\dfrac{1}{17}\right)$ 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $x\le 50$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the answer is $50$.
