[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A line has a slope of $-7$ and contains the point $(3,0)$. The equation of this line can be written in the form $y = mx+b$. What is the value of $m+b$?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the equation of the line with the given slope and apoint (3,0), we can use the point-slope form of the equation of a line, which is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In this problem, we know:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - The slope \( m = -7 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - The point \((x_1, y_1) = (3, 0)\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substituting these values into the point-slope form, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m y - 0 = -7(x - 3)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplifying this, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m y = -7(x - 3)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we expand the right-hand side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m y = -7x + 21
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we need to convert this equation into the slope-intercept form, which is \( y = mx + b \). We do this by isolating \( y \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m y = -7x + 21
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From this, we can see that \( m = -7 \) and \( b = 21 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Finally, we add \( m \) and \( b \) to find \( m + b \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m + b = -7 + 21 = 14
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the value of \( m + b \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{14}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
