[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the value of $\cos 150^\circ$, we can use the angle addition formula: $\cos\theta = \cos(\theta - 90^\circ)$. So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 150^\circ = \cos(150^\circ - 90^\circ) = \cos150^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we need to find the value of $\cos (-60^\circ)$. We know that the cosine function is even, so:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos(-60^\circ) = \cos60^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We know that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos60^\circ = 0.5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, $\cos 150^\circ = \cos(-60^\circ) = 0.5$. Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 150^\circ = \boxed{0.5}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{}<|endoftext|>
