[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let $a_n = 4n^3 + 6n^2 + 4n + 1.$  Find
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[a_8 + a_9 + a_{10} + \dots + a_{23}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We know $a_n = 4 n^3 + 6 n^2 + 4 n + 1.$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find $a_8 + a_9 + a_{10} + \dots + a_{23},$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m we can use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic progression.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The terms of an arithmetic progression can be represented as $a_n + a_{n+1} + a_{n+2} + \dots + a_{n+k} = \frac{k}{2} (a_1 + a_{n+k})$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m For $a_8 + a_9 + a_{10} + \dots + a_{23},$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m the $k$ terms are $a_8 + a_{23}, a_9 + a_{22}, a_{10} + a_{21}, \dots, a_{23} + a_1,$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m which can be written as
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\frac{41}{2} ([a_1 + a_{23}] + [a_2 + a_{22}] + [a_3 + a_{21}] + \dots + [a_{23} + a_1]).\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The sum of the $41$ elements in the arithmetic progression is $41a_1.$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since we can choose $41$ terms at a time, we can calculate this sum by summing the numbers $[a_3 + a_{21}, a_4 + a_{20}, a_5 + a_{19}, \dots, a_{23} + a_1].$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since we can divide this sum by $4$ to find the sum of the $41$ numbers,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $[a_3 + a_{21}, a_4 + a_{20}, a_5 + a_{19}, \dots, a_{23} + a_1] = \frac{41 \cdot 4}{4} (a_1 + a_1) = 41(a_1 + a_1) = 41a_1.$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, we have
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\frac{41}{2} (41 a_1) = 41 a_1.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ####
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The answer is $41a_1.$<|endoftext|>
