[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the number of distinct three-digit positive integers with only odd digits, we need to consider all possible combinations of three digits where each digit can be 1, 3, 5, 7, or 9. Since we are dealing with positive integers, we only need to consider single-digit or two-digit numbers.
