[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 8. Three digits ([3, 7, 5]): No valid integer because they are all the same.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the only valid combination is ([1, 1, 7]) which forms the numbers 17, 37, and 17.5, but 17.5 is not a strictly positive integer. The only valid integers are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. 37
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. 17
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, there are 2 distinct three-digit positive integers with only odd digits.<|endoftext|>
