[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Compute $\cos 30^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute $\cos 30^\circ$, we can use the fact that $\cos 30^\circ$ is related to the values of $2$nd order trig functions.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 30^\circ &= \cos\left(2s + \frac{3}{2}t + 15^\circ\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using the angle identities for trigonometric functions and the sum-to-product identities, we can simplify the expression to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 30^\circ &= \cos\left(2s + \frac{3}{2}t + 15^\circ\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 30^\circ &= \cos(s - 15^\circ - t)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using the unit circle property, $cosx = \cos(90^\circ - x)$, we can simplify further:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 30^\circ &= \cos(90^\circ - (15^\circ + t))
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Which can be further reduced to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 30^\circ &= \sin(15^\circ + t)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Hence, using the angle identity for $\sin x$ given as $$\sin(x) = \sin(180^\circ - x)$$,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \sin(15^\circ + t) &= \sin(90^\circ - (t - 15^\circ)) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &= \sin(105^\circ - t)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplifying, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 30^\circ &= \sin(105^\circ - t)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align}<|endoftext|>
