[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine the number of five-digit zip codes that have a first digit greater than 4, we can use the following steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Identify the range of five-digit ZIP codes**: Five-digit zip codes start from 10000 to 99999.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Define the length of the zip code**: Each length of zip code has \(n - 2\) digits, where \(n\) is the number of digits (3 for ZIP codes like 09900 to 09999).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Count the possible combinations**: For each possible \(n\) (where \(n\) ranges from 3 to 9), we count the number of possibilities for each part.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Case 1: \(n = 3\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - We have 10 possible values for the first digit (1 through 10).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - For any other digit (from 2 to 9), there are \(9 \times 10 = 90\) possible values.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Possible lengths: } [10000, 10001, 10002, 10003, 10004, 10005, 10006, 10007, 10008, 10009]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Number of lengths: \(8\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Total combinations for } n = 3 : 8 \times 90 = 720
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Case 2: \(n = 4\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - We need 4 digits to subtract for the 10 possible hours.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - There are \(10\) possible numbers for the all-hours code (1 to 9).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - For each valid hour (five-digit code), there are \(9 \times 10 = 90\) possible combinations of two digits.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Possible lengths: } [10000, 10001, 10002, 10003, 10004, 10005, 10006, 10007, 10008, 10009]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Number of lengths: \(7\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Total combinations for } n = 4 : 7 \times 90 = 630
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Case 3: \(n = 5\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - We have 10 possible hours (1 to 9).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Each hour has 5 digits, and each digit has 10 possibilities for the second digit.
