[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [/asy]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the area of a regular pentagon (a pentagon with all sides and angles equal), we can use the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Area = (1/4) \* n \* s^2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m where n is the number of sides and s is the length of each side.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m For our pentagon:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - n = 5 (since it has 5 sides)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - s = 8' (since the side length is equivalent to 1 inch)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now we can plug these values into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Area = (1/4) \* 5 \* (8')^2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Area = 5 \* 64
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Area = 320 square inches
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
