[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs are consecutive whole numbers is 29 units. What is the sum of the lengths of the two legs?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let both legs from the right triangle be denoted as $x$ and $x+1$ [(because leg is scalar).]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The conditions we have for the right triangle are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $\begin{cases} x(x+1) & = 29~(\text {But }x~\text {and}~x+1 \text { are consecutive positive numbers.})~(29 = 29 & 29={28\text { }}+1.~~ \text{} ) \end{cases} $
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Then $x$ is either 5 or 7. It's impossible for us to have $x > x+1$, thus:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $x = 7$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Then $x+1 = 8$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m so the hypotenuse is, $h = \sqrt{x^2 + (x+1)^2} = \sqrt{25} = 5$. So the sum of the lengths of the two legs are $7+8 = 15~ . \square$. grateful for your input. createStackNavigatorsInit with result
