[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve for the angle \( x \), we need to use the fact that the external angle to angle \( x \) is equal to the sum of the two opposite interior angles. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Identify the known angles**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - We know the sum of the angle \( 108^\circ \) and \( 26^\circ \) is \( 134^\circ \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Understand the property of angles in a triangle**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - In any triangle, the sum of the angles is \( 180^\circ \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Express the property mathematically**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \angle x + \angle 108^\circ + \angle 26^\circ = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Substitute the known angle degrees**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \angle x + 108^\circ + 26^\circ = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. **Solve for \( \angle x \)**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \angle x + 134^\circ = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \angle x = 180^\circ - 134^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \angle x = 46^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the angle \( x \) is \( 46^\circ \). 
