[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $a^{lcm(b,c,lcm(a,b)))}-lcm(a,lcm(b,c))=n$ I'm trying to solve it by logical steps
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Could you help me to solve it?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $a^{lcm(b,c,lcm(a,b)))}-lcm(a,lcm(b,c))=n$ How to solve? To solve the equation \(a^{lcm(b,c,lcm(a,b)))} - lcm(a,lcm(b,c)) = n\), we will proceed step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 1: Understanding the LCM Function
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The least common multiple (LCM) of two numbers \(a\) and \(b\), denoted as \(lcm(a, b)\), is the smallest positive integer that is divisible by both \(a\) and \(b\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 2: Expressing \(lcm(a,lcm(b,c))\) in Terms of \(\text{lcm}(a,b)\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using the property of the LCM, we know:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{lcm}(a, b) = \text{lcm}\left(\text{lcm}(a, b), c\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This implies:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m lcm(a, b) \equiv c \pmod{\text{lcm}(a, b)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 3: Applying the \(\text{lcm}\) Function Step-by-Step
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We start with the expression \(lcm(a, lcm(b, c))\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{lcm}(a, \text{lcm}(b, c))
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using the property once more:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{lcm}\left(\text{lcm}(a, \text{lcm}(b, c)), c\right) \equiv \text{lcm}(a, c) \pmod{\text{lcm}(a, \text{lcm}(b, c))}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, reduce \(\text{lcm}\left(a, \text{lcm}(b, c)\right)\) from the right side:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{lcm}(a, \text{lcm}(b, c)) = \text{lcm}\left(\text{lcm}(a, c), \text{lcm}(b, c)\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{lcm}\left(\text{lcm}(a, c), \text{lcm}(b, c)\right) \equiv \text{lcm}(a, c \cdot \text{lcm}(b, c)) \pmod{\text{lcm}(a, \text{lcm}(b, c))}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substitute \(\text{lcm}(a, c) \equiv c \pmod{\text{lcm}(a, \text{lcm}(b, c))}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{lcm}\left(\text{lcm}(a, c), \text{lcm}(b, c)\right) \equiv c \pmod{\text{lcm}(a, \text{lcm}(b, c))}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 4: Simplifying the Exponentiation
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we express \(\text{lcm}(a, \text{lcm}(b, c))\) in terms of \(\text{lcm}(a, b)\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{lcm}(a, \text{lcm}(b, c)) = \text{lcm}\left(\text{lcm}(a, \text{lcm}(b, c)), c\right) \equiv \text{lcm}(a \cdot \text{lcm}(b, c), c) \pmod{\text{lcm}(a, b)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We need to simplify further:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{LCM}\left(a \cdot \text{lcm}(b, c), c\right) \equiv \text{LCM}(a, c, \text{lcm}(b, c)) \pmod{-\text{lcm}(a, b)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Subtract \(\text{lcm}(a, c)\) from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{LCM}(a \cdot \text{lcm}(b, c), c) + \text{lcm}(a, c) \equiv \text{LCM}(a, c, \text{lcm}(b, c)) \pmod{-\text{lcm}(a, b)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This is the final expression:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m a^{lcm(a, \text{lcm}(b, c), \text{lcm}(a, \text{lcm}(b, c)))} - lcm(a, \text{lcm}(b, c)) = n
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{a^{lcm(a, \text{lcm}(b, c), \text{lcm}(a, \text{lcm}(b, c)))} - lcm(a, \text{lcm}(b, c)) = n}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
