[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the total length of all the lines that make up the set \( S \), we need to first understand the given equation and then determine the length of each line. The equation given is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \Big|\big| |x|-2\big|-1\Big|+\Big|\big| |y|-2\big|-1\Big|=1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This equation describes a squared ellipse centered at \((1, 1)\) with semi-major and semi-minor axes of length 1. The equation represents all points within this ellipse. Since the ellipse is symmetric and centered at \((1, 1)\), we can consider only the vertical lines defining the ellipse.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The equation states that the distances between the point and the line, as well as between the line and the vertical axis, are all equal to 1. Let's denote the vertical coordinate of a point on the boundary of the ellipse by \( y = 7 - x^2 \). The value of \( x \) determines how far a point is from the line \( y = x^2 \) on both axes. Given that \( |x| \) ranges from \(-1\) to \( 1\), \( x \) can be any value from \( -1 \) to \( 1 \), and \( y \) can be any value from \( 7 - x^2 \) up to \( 1 + (1 - x^2) = 2 - x^2 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the length of a horizontal line segment (i.e., from point \((x, y)\) to \((x, 7 - x^2)\)), we calculate the vertical distance \( y - y^2 \) and then take the absolute value. The total length of all such line segments is the same for each vertical line segment because the ellipse is symmetric and centered at \((1, 1)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The length of the horizontal line segment from \((-1, (-1)^2 - (-1)^2)\) to \((1, 7 - 1^2 - 1^2) = (1, 5)\) is the same as the length of the line segment from \((-1, 1 - (-1)^2)\) to \((1, 5 - 1^2)\), which is 5.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since the equation described above describes all such line segments as the points on the ellipse, the total length of all the lines that make up the set \( S \) is the product of the total number of points (which is infinite if only vertical lines are considered) with the length of each line segment, which is 5.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the total length of all the lines that make up the set \( S \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{5}
