[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Sure, let's evaluate the determinant of a \(3 \times 3\) matrix using the values \(x\), \(\sin \theta\), and \(\cos \theta\) (which you haven't provided). The given matrix is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} x & \sin \theta & \cos \theta \\ -\sin \theta & -x & 1 \\ \cos \theta & 1 & x \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The determinant of a \(3 \times 3\) matrix \(\mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\ d & e & f \\ g & h & i \end{pmatrix} is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{Det}(\mathbf{A}) = a(ei - fh) - b(di - fg) + c(dh - eg)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m For our matrix \(\mathbf{A}\), the elements are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m a = x, \quad b = \sin \theta, \quad c = \cos \theta
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m d = -\sin \theta, \quad e = -x, \quad f = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m g = \cos \theta, \quad h = 1, \quad i = x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's calculate the determinant step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Compute the determinant coefficients using \(a = x\), \(b = \sin \theta\), \(c = \cos \theta\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{vmatrix} x & \sin \theta & \cos \theta \\ -\sin \theta & -x & 1 \\ \cos \theta & 1 & x \end{vmatrix} = x(x \cdot x - 1 \cdot 1) - \sin \theta(-\sin \theta \cdot x - 1 \cdot \cos \theta) + \cos \theta(-\sin \theta \cdot 1 - (-x) \cdot \cos \theta)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = x^3 - (\sin \theta)(-\sin \theta x + \cos \theta) + \cos \theta(-\sin \theta - \cos \theta x)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = x^3 + \sin^2 \theta x - \cos^2 \theta - \sin \theta \cos \theta x - \cos \theta \sin \theta x - \cos^2 \theta x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Simplify the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = x^3 + \sin^2 \theta x + \cos^2 \theta x - \sin \theta \cos \theta x - \cos \theta \sin \theta x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = x^3 + \sin^2 \theta + \cos^2 \theta - \sin \theta \cos \theta - \cos \theta \sin \theta x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(\sin \theta \cos \theta = \frac{\sin (2\theta)}{2}\) and \(\cos \theta \sin \theta = \frac{\sin (2\theta)}{2}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = x^3 + \frac{\sin^2 \theta}{2} + \frac{\cos^2 \theta}{2} - \frac{\sin (2\theta)}{2} - \frac{\cos (2\theta)}{2} x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = x^3 + \frac{\sin^2 \theta + \cos^2 \theta}{2} - \frac{\sin (2\theta)}{2} - \frac{\cos (2\theta)}{2} x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(\sin^2 \theta + \cos^2 \theta = 1\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = x^3 - \frac{\sin (2\theta)}{2} - \frac{\cos (2\theta)}{2} x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Recall the double-angle identities: \(\sin(2\theta) = 2 \sin \theta \cos \theta\) and \(\cos(2\theta) = \cos^2 \theta - \sin^2 \theta\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = x^3 - \frac{2 \sin \theta \cos \theta}{2} - \frac{\cos^2 \theta - \sin^2 \theta}{2} x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = x^3 - \sin \theta \cos \theta - \frac{(\cos^2 \theta - \sin^2 \theta)}{2} x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = x^3 - \sin \theta \cos \theta - \frac{\cos (2\theta)}{2} x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. The final determinant:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Det(\mathbf{A}) = x^3 - \frac{\sin^2 \theta + \cos^2 \theta}{2} - \frac{\sin (2\theta)}{2} - \frac{\cos (2\theta)}{2} x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(\sin^2 \theta + \cos^2 \theta = 1\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Det(\mathbf{A}) = x^3 - \frac{1}{2} - \frac{\sin (2\theta)}{2} - \frac{\cos (2\theta)}{2} x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Putting it all together:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Det(\mathbf{A}) = x^3 - \frac{1}{2} - \frac{\sin (2\theta)}{2} - \frac{\cos (2\theta)}{2} x = x^3 - \frac{1}{2} - \frac{\sin (2\theta) + \cos (2\theta) - \cos (2\theta)}{2} x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Det(\mathbf{A}) = x^3 - \frac{1}{2} - \frac{\sin (2\theta) + \cos (2\theta)}{2} x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{x^3 - \frac{1}{2} - \frac{\sin (2\theta) + \cos (2\theta)}{2} x}<|endoftext|>
