[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let $P(x)$ be a polynomial with integer coefficients that satisfies $P(17)=10$ and $P(24)=17.$ Given that $P(n)=n+3$ has two distinct integer solutions $n_1$ and $n_2,$ find $n_1$ and $n_2$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (Give your answer as a comma-separated list, in either order; for example, "2, 5" or "6, -3".)
