[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The product \[\frac{8}{4}\cdot\frac{12}{8}\cdot\frac{16}{12} \dotsm \frac{4n+4}{4n} \dotsm \frac{2008}{2004}\] is an infinite product of fractions. We can simplify it by finding a common denominator, which is \(4n+4\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\frac{8}{4}\cdot\frac{12}{8}\cdot\frac{16}{12} \dotsm \frac{4n+4}{4n} \dotsm \frac{2008}{2004}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This can be rewritten as:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\frac{2\cdot 6\cdot 12\cdot \dotsm \cdot (4n+4)}{1\cdot 4\cdot 8\cdot \dotsm \cdot 2n}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can cancel out pairs of terms, starting from \(\frac{2}{1}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\frac{2}{1} \cdot \frac{6}{1} \cdot \frac{12}{2} \cdot \dotsm \cdot \frac{4n+4}{2}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, the denominators are powers of 2:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[1 \cdot 2 \cdot 4 \cdot \dotsm \cdot 2n = \frac{2^{n+1}}{2} = 2^{n+1}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So the product simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[2 \cdot 6 \cdot 12 \cdot \dotsm \cdot \frac{2n+4}{2} \cdot 2^{n+1}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This can be split into two parts:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\frac{2n+4}{2} \cdot 2^{n+1} \cdot 6 \cdot 12 \cdot \dotsm \cdot 2^{n+1}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can separate the constant terms and the fractional terms:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[2^{n+1} + 2 \cdot 6 \cdot 12 \cdot \dotsm \cdot 2^{n+1}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can factor out \(2^{n+1}\) from the product inside the parentheses:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[2^{n+1} (1 + 6 \cdot 12 \cdot \dotsm \cdot 2^{n+1}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The product \(1 + 6 \cdot 12 \cdot \dotsm \cdot 2^{n+1}\) is a geometric series with the first term \(1\) and common ratio \(2^{n+1}\). The sum of the infinite geometric series is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[1 \cdot \frac{1}{1-2^{n+1}} = \frac{1}{2^{n+1}}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So the expression simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[2^{n+1} \cdot \frac{1}{2^{n+1}} = 1.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\boxed{1}.\]
