[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m At least how many students should be present at their tables that day?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In the original table of operations, there are 10 students being enrolled from two groups of 10 children and 20 teachers. We need to find the minimum number of students, \( n \), such that when they be collectively divided into groups, each group contains at least 4 students in total, and among all groups, both graduates and non-graders are present simultaneously.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The maximum number to be present from the table is the sum of those being active from both groups minus the smallest number of students making all groups impossible to have exactly one person.
