[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We need to find \( h \) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3(s + t) + h < 10n
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m For her row, 3 chairs are available. Hence, \( n = 3 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m For her column, as \( H = 10 - (3 - c) \), this implies \( H = c + 7 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we will use the rule that there are at least \( \left\lceil \frac{n}{6} \right\rceil \) and at most \( \left\lfloor \frac{n}{6} \right\rfloor \) subjects per row for row-division.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's compute the pertinent values for \( h \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. For household:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    h \le \left\lfloor \frac{h}{2} \right\rfloor + \left\{ \left\lfloor \frac{h}{3} \right\rfloor \right\}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substituting \( \nums{\h} = 3 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3 \le \left\lfloor \frac{3}{2} \right\rfloor + \left\{ \left\lfloor \frac{3}{9} \right\rfloor \right\}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m }\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \b[3] gives fair totals for each part: \( \left\lfloor \frac{3}{2} \right\rfloor = 2 \) and \( \left\lfloor \frac{3}{9} \right\rfloor = 0 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the minimal team \( l \) must include the possible available \(2n = 6\) and \(l \ge 3 \), including 3 in the party.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{10} \qquad \boxed{6} \qquad \boxed{3}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This step ensures there are sufficient students and is without constraints, thus meeting all conditions that both should be able to take the requirement with no head room.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{3}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \] Then, student numbers can be determined using the rule that the Group must have: \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m n \ge 6 \text{ + } k + \frac{3 \times -6 \log(k+ 3)}{\log(k+ 3)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
