[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The complement of an angle is 90 degrees minus the measure of the angle, so to find the double measure of complement, we simply multiply by 2: \(180^\circ - 2 \times \frac{\pi}{3}\). 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's solve this using Python.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m import math
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Calculate the complement
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m complement = math.pi / math.tan(0.5)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Double the measure of complement
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m angle = 2 * complement * 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m print(angle)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```
