[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Determine the number of integers $x$ such that $0\le x< 12$ and $x$ satisfies the following system of equations: \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &x-1\equiv 1-x\pmod {12},\\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &x-2\equiv 2-x\pmod{12}.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve the given system of congruences, we will use the given information and iterate through the integer values within the range \(0 \leq x < 12\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. First, we solve the first congruence for \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    x - 1 \equiv 1 - x \pmod{12}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Add \(x\) and \(1\) on one side to eliminate the \(x\) term:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    2x \equiv 2 \pmod{12}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Divide by 2:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    x \equiv 1 \pmod{6}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    This means \(x = 6k + 1\) for some integer \(k\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Next, we solve the second congruence for \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    x - 2 \equiv 2 - x \pmod{12}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Add \(x\) and \(2\) on one side:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    2x \equiv 4 \pmod{12}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Divide by 2:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    x \equiv 2 \pmod{6}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    This means \(x = 6k + 2\) for some integer \(k\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. We need to find the values of \(k\) such that \(6k + 1\) and \(6k + 2\) fall within the range \(0 \leq x < 12\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. For \(6k + 1\) to be in the range \(0 \leq x < 12\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    0 \leq 6k + 1 < 12
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Solving for \(k\):
