[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Finding the roots in terms of \( \tan x \):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Recall that \( \tan x = \frac{\sin x}{\cos x} \). We know that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \sin^2 x + \cos^2 x = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    So, if \( t = \tan x \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    t^2 = \frac{\sin^2 x + \cos^2 x}{\sin^2 t + \cos^2 t} = \frac{1}{\sin^2 t + \cos^2 t}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    1 + t^2 = \frac{1}{\sin^2 t + \cos^2 t}
