[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In a convex hexagon, no matter which two vertices correspond to, the remaining four vertices can only have three isolated edges. These vertices are the vertices of the hexagon that are not part of the diagonal you are choosing, and we want to find the number of distinct diagonals for these vertices. Since there are six vertices in total, three vertices will have two edges, and three vertices will have three edges, which means there are three edges shared among these three vertices. Therefore, there are 9 = 3 + 3 - 3 = 9 edges sharing sides, and each shared edge contributes two vertices. So, the number of distinct diagonals is 9 × 2 = 18.
