[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We have to find the value of the expression \[\sqrt{41+24\sqrt2}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To simplify it, we need to square both the radicals on the inside. We can write it as \[\sqrt{41+24\sqrt{2}}^2=\sqrt{41^2+2\cdot24\sqrt{2^2}+24^2}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can simplify further by completing the square on the first two terms, \[\sqrt{41^2+32}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The square root of $41^2$ is $41$ and the square root of $32$ is $\sqrt{16} = 4$. So, \[\sqrt{41^2+32}=\sqrt{169+32}=\sqrt{201}=\boxed{15.\,80627}.\]eousystem
