[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's rewrite $3x+5y=20$ in slope-intercept form, which is $y=mx+b$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{3}{5}x+0y&=20 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &\quad \iff \quad \frac{3}{5}x=20 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &\quad \iff x&=\frac{20\cdot 5}{3} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &\quad \iff x&=\frac{100}{3} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &\quad \iff y&=\frac{3\times 100}{5}\;,\;y=\frac{600}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the coordinates for the slope of the line $3x+5y=20$ are $left( frac {100}{3}, frac {600}{10} right)$
