[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To simplify the fraction \(\frac{27}{30}\), we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of the numerator (27) and the denominator (30) and then divide both the numerator and the denominator by this GCD.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 1: Find the prime factorization of both the numerator and the denominator.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - The prime factorization of 27:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \(\begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   27 & = 3 \times 3 \times 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m               & = 3^3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m           \end{align*}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - The prime factorization of 30:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \(\begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   30 & = 2 \times 3 \times 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m               & = 2 \times 3 \times 2 \times 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m               & = (2 \times 3) \times (2 \times 5)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m           \end{align*}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 2: Identify the common factors. In this case, both 2 and 3 are common factors.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - The common factor is 3.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 3: Write the simplified fraction using the GCD (which is 3) as the denominator.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \(\frac{27 \div 3}{30 \div 3} = \frac{9}{10}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the GCD of 27 and 30 is found.<|endoftext|>
