[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve the problem, we need to follow the sequence of transformations applied to the point \((1, 1, 1)\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Rotation \(180^\circ\) about the \(y\)-axis:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Rotating a point \((x, y, z)\) \(180^\circ\) about the \(y\)-axis changes the coordinates to \((-x, y, z)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Applying this rotation to \((1, 1, 1)\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    (1, 1, 1) \rightarrow (-1, 1, 1)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Reflection through the \(yz\)-plane:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Reflecting a point \((x, y, z)\) through the \(yz\)-plane changes the coordinates to \((x, -y, z)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Applying this reflection to \((1, 1, 1)\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    (1, 1, 1) \rightarrow (1, -1, 1)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Reflection through the \(xz\)-plane:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Reflecting a point \((x, y, z)\) through the \(xz\)-plane changes the coordinates to \((y, x, -z)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Applying this reflection to \((1, -1, 1)\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    (1, -1, 1) \rightarrow (-1, 1, 1)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Rotation \(180^\circ\) about the \(y\)-axis:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Reflecting a point \((x, y, z)\) through the \(y\)-axis \(180^\circ\) about the \(y\)-axis changes the coordinates to \((-x, y, -z)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Applying this rotation to \((-1, 1, 1)\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    (-1, 1, 1) \rightarrow (1, -1, -1)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the final coordinates of the point after all these transformations are:
