[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Find the remainder when $1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \dots + 100^3$ is divided by 6.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \dots + 100^3 =$ the sum of cubes of the first 100 natural numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m If we subtract $100^3$ from both sides, we obtain $1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \dots + 100^3 - 100^3 =$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m & \left(\underbrace{1+2+3+\dots+100}_{\textstyle 100+1+2+3+\dots+100} \right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m & - \left(\underbrace{100^3-100^3}_{0} \right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m & = 1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \dots + 100^3 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Then,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m s = \frac{s}{6},
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m where $s$ represents the sum of cubes of the first 100 natural numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 100+1+2+3+\dots+100 = \frac{s}{6},
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m which means that when $s$ is divided by 6, the remainder is $\boxed{33}$.
