[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve the equation \(\sqrt{x+7} = 9\), we need to eliminate the square root by squaring both sides of the equation. Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Start with the given equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \sqrt{x+7} = 9
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Square both sides of the equation to get rid of the square root:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    (\sqrt{x+7})^2 = 9^2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. The left side simplifies to \(x + 7\), and the right side simplifies to \(81\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    x + 7 = 81
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. Next, isolate \(x\) by subtracting 7 from both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    x + 7 - 7 = 81 - 7
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. Simplify both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    x = 74
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the value of \(x\) is \(\boxed{74}\).<|endoftext|>
