[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplify \begin{align}\cos 10^\circ \cos 30^\circ \cos 50^\circ \cos 70^\circ \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We know \large\;\cos x\cos y\cos z=(1/4)(\cos x\cos(90^\circ-y))\cos(30^\circ-z)\cos 70^\circ \tag{1}\end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, \begin{align}\cos 10^\circ \cos 30^\circ \cos 50^\circ \cos 70^\circ &= \left[\begin{align}\cos 10^\circ&=\cos 70^\circ \cdot (\cos 50^\circ+\cos 30^\circ-1) \\\\&=\cos 70^\circ \cdot\frac{4-\cos 10^\circ}{4}\end{align}\right]\\\cos 10^\circ \cos 30^\circ \cos 50^\circ \cos 70^\circ &=\left[\begin{align}\cos 30^\circ&=\frac{1}{2} \\\\&=\cos 50^\circ\end{align}\right]\\\cos 10^\circ \cos 30^\circ \cos 50^\circ \cos 70^\circ &=\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{2}{4} \\\\&=\boxed{\frac{1}{4}}\end{align}<|endoftext|>
