[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m How many ways can 1995 be factored as a product of two two-digit numbers? (Two factorizations of the form $a\cdot b$ and $b\cdot a$ are considered the same).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine the number of ways to factor 1995 as a product of two two-digit numbers, we need to find pairs \((a, b)\) such that \(a \cdot b = 1995\), and both \(a\) and \(b\) are two-digit integers. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's find the one-digit factor of 1995 by testing each possible two-digit number:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1995 \div 1 = 1995 \quad (\text{not a tolerance factor})
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1995 \div 2 = 997.5 \quad (\text{not a whole number})
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1995 \div 3 = 665 \quad (\text{a two-digit number})
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1995 \div 4 = 498.75 \quad (\text{not a whole number})
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1995 \div 5 = 399 \quad (\text{a two-digit number})
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1995 \div 6 = 332.5 \quad (\text{not a whole number})
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1995 \div 7 = 285.294 \quad (\text{not a whole number})
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1995 \div 8 = 249.375 \quad (\text{not a whole number})
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1995 \div 9 = 221.6667 \quad (\text{not a whole number})
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1995 \div 10 = 199.5 \quad (\text{not a whole number})
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1995 \div 11 = 180.4545 \quad (\text{not a whole number})
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From the above, we see that the two-digit factor of 1995 is 1995. To verify, we multiply 1995 by 1997:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1995 \cdot 1997 = 1995 \cdot (2000 - 1) = 1995 \cdot 2000 - 1995 = 1995 \cdot 2000 - (1995 \cdot 100 - 1995) = 1995 \cdot 2000 + 600 \cdot 1995 - 1995 = 1995 \cdot 2000 - 1995 \cdot 1995
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This confirms that \((1995, 1997)\) is a factorization.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \((1995, 1997)\) is a pair of two-digit numbers, they are considered the same. Therefore, there is only one way to factor 1995 as a product of two two-digit numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{1}
