[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can express the given series in a general form:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} (2n+1) x^n = 85
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find \( x \), we will divide both sides of the equation by \( 2x \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \left(2n+1\right) \left(x^n\right) = \frac{85}{2x}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now divide every term by \( x \) (assuming \( x \neq 0 \)):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \left(2n+1\right) x^{n-1} = 41
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
