[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m There is a unique pair of positive real numbers satisfying the equations \[ x^4-6x^2y^2+y^4 = 8 \qquad\mbox{and}\qquad x^3y-xy^3 = 2\sqrt{3}. \]Determine $x$, writing your answer in the form $a\cos\theta$, with $\theta$ in degrees.
