[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the last two digits in the sum of the factorials of the first 100 positive integers, we can break down the problem into smaller steps and use modular arithmetic to simplify calculations.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. First, calculate the first 100 positive integers:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &1, 2, 3, 4, \ldots, 99, 100 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Next, calculate the factorial of each number and sum them:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &1, (2 \times 1), (3 \times 2), (4 \times 3), \ldots, (99 \times 49), 100 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Now, we will compute each factorial separately and then find the last two digits sum of those factorials:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &f(1) = 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &f(2) = 2 \times 1 = 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &f(3) = 3 \times 2 = 6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &f(4) = 4 \times 3 = 12 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &f(5) = 5 \times 4 = 20 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &\vdots \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &f(100) = 100 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &\text{last two digits of} \quad f(1) = 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &\text{last two digits of} \quad f(2) = 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &\text{last two digits of} \quad f(3) = 6 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &\text{last two digits of} \quad f(4) = 12 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &\vdots \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &\text{last two digits of} \quad f(100) = 100 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. Sum the last two digits of these factors:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &1 + 2 + 6 + 12 + 20 + 42 + 70 + 104 + 156 + 188 + 232 + 268 + 318 + 368 + 432 + 486 + 542 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. Calculate the sum step-by-step using Python:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \sum \left[ f(n) \mod 100 \right] \text{ for } n \, \text{from} \, 1 \, \text{to} \, 100
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's calculate this using Python:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Define the first 100 positive integers
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m first_n_integers = range(100)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Calculate the factorial of each number
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m factorials = [1]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m for n in first_n_integers:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     factorials.append(factorials[-1] * n)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Calculate and sum the last two digits of the factorials
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m sum_last_two_digits = sum(factorial % 100 for factorial in factorials)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Output the result
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m print(sum_last_two_digits)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```
