[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To evaluate \(i^{14762} + i^{14763} + i^{14764} + i^{14765}\), we need to understand the cyclicity of the powers of the imaginary unit \(i\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The powers of \(i\) cycle every 4 terms:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^1 &= i \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^2 &= -1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^3 &= -i \\
