[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the $x$-intercept of the linear equation $3y - 4x = 12$, we start by setting $y = 0$ since they are the coordinates of the $x$-intercept.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Set $y = 0$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $3(0) - 4x = 12$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Solve for $x$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $-4x = 12$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Divide both sides by $-4$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $x = -3$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the $x$-intercept of the line $3y - 4x = 12$ is at the point $\boxed{(-3, 0)}$.
