[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m If the digits 2, 3, 5 and 7 are arranged in a four-digit odd number, there are exactly $(7-2)! = 7! = 5040$ permutations.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m If the digits are not in an order, there are $(7-1)! = 6!$ permutations.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the probability is $\frac{5040 - 6!}{5040} = \frac{120 - 720}{5040} = \frac{118 \cdot 5}{7 \cdot 7 \cdot 12} = \frac{390}{7 \cdot 12} = \frac{30}{7}$.
