[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Compute \[\dfrac{2^3-1}{2^3+1}\cdot\dfrac{3^3-1}{3^3+1}\cdot\dfrac{4^3-1}{4^3+1}\cdot\dfrac{5^3-1}{5^3+1}\cdot\dfrac{6^3-1}{6^3+1}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 1: Calculate \(2^3 - 1\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We know that \(2^3 = 8\), so \[2^3 - 1 = 8 - 1 = 7\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 2: Calculate \(\dfrac{7}{2^3+1}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we have the denominator squared (\(2^3 + 1\)), so we can substitute it in:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\dfrac{7}{2^3+1} = \dfrac{7}{7+1} = \dfrac{7}{8}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 3: Calculate \(\dfrac{3^3 - 1}{3^3 + 1}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we need to find the value of \(3^3\) and \(3^3 + 1\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{array}{r l}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3^3 = 27 & \quad \text{and} & \quad 27 + 1 = 28 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3^3 - 1 = 27 - 1 = 26 & \quad \text{and} & \quad 28 + 1 = 29 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m For the second fraction, we will calculate the numerator.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \dfrac{26}{29}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 4: Calculate \(\dfrac{4^3 - 1}{4^3 + 1}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m For the next part, we need to find the value of \(4^3\) and \(4^3 + 1\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{array}{r l}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4^3 = 64 & \quad \text{and} & \quad 64 + 1 = 65 \\
