[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Compute $\cos 36^\circ.$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute \(\cos 36^\circ\), we can use the known values and relationships between trigonometric functions.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The angle \(36^\circ\) is on a coordinate circle with the unit circle, where angles are measured in radians. We know from trigonometry that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 36^\circ = \cot \left(\frac{\pi}{6}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now we need to find \(\cot \left(\frac{\pi}{6}\right)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From trigonometric values of common angles, we know:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cot x = \frac{1}{\tan x}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m And from the unit circle values: 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(\tan 36^\circ = \frac{\sin 36^\circ}{\cos 36^\circ} = \sin 60^\circ\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(\tan \frac{\pi}{6} = \cot \left(\frac{\pi}{6}\right) = \sin \frac{\pi}{3}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using known trigonometric values, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \sin 60^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \sin \frac{\pi}{3} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, \(\cot \left(\frac{\pi}{6}\right) = \frac{1}{\sin 60^\circ} = \frac{1}{\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}} = \frac{2}{\sqrt{3}} = \frac{2}{\sqrt{3}} \cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{\sqrt{3}} = \frac{2\sqrt{3}}{3}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 36^\circ = \cot \left(\frac{\pi}{6}\right) = \frac{2\sqrt{3}}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\frac{2\sqrt{3}}{3}}<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
