[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To evaluate \(i^{22} + i^{222}\), we need to understand the concept of powers of the imaginary unit \(i\). The imaginary unit \(i\) is defined such that \(i^2 = -1\), and every integer can be written as a power of \(i\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's start by defining \(i\) as follows based on its powers:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^1 = i \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^2 = -1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^3 = i \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^4 = -1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^5 = i \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^6 = -1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^7 = i \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \quad \vdots
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Repeating this pattern, we can see that \(i\) acts on pairs of powers of 2. Specifically, \(i^k = (-1)^{k/2} (i)^k\). Since \(k\) is even, \(i^k = (-1)^{k/2} i^k\) simplifies to \((-1)^{k/2 + k} i^{2k} = (-1)^k i^{2k} = (-1)^k (-1)^{2k} (-1)^{2k} = (-1)^{4k} = (-1)^k\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, for any integer \(n\), \(i^n = (-1)^n\). This property allows us to simplify the exponents:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. For \(i^{22}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^{22} = (-1)^{22} = -1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. For \(t^{222}\), since \(222 = 22 \times 10 + 2\), and \(22\) is even, \(t^{222}\) is \((t^k)^{22} = t^{22k} = t^22 t^22 t^22 t^22 t^22 t^22 t^22 t^22 t^22 = t^2 t^2 t^2 t^2 t^2 t^2 t^2 t^2 t^2 = t^{10} t^{10} t^{10} t^{10} t^{10} t^{10} t^{10} t^{10} t^{10} t^{10} = t^{20}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^{222} = t^{20}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^{22} + i^{222} = -1 + t^{20}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{-1 + t^{20}}<|endoftext|>
