[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m e.) 25 To determine which values of \( n \) make the expression \(\frac{5n^4 + n^2}{n^2 - 5}\) have integer solutions, we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Factorize the expression \(\frac{5n^4 + n^2}{n^2 - 5}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Identify any values of \( n \) that make the numerator a perfect square (other than zero).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Determine which of these values make the denominator a perfect square.
