[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the volume of a cylinder, we use the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ V = \pi r^2 h \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m where:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \( r \) is the radius of the cylinder's base
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \( h \) is the height of the cylinder
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \( \text{radius} (r) = 3 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \( \text{height} (h) = 10 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 1: Substitute the given values into the formula.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ V = \pi (3)^2 (10) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 2: Calculate the square of the radius.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 3^2 = 9 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 3: Multiply the squared radius by the height.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 9 \times 10 = 90 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 4: Write the final volume using this calculation.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ V = 90\pi \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the volume of the cylinder is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{90\pi}<|endoftext|>
