[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the units digit of $3^{2004}$, we need to understand the pattern of changes in the units digit as we repeatedly multiply a number by 3.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Starting Unit Digits:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \\[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    3^1 \quad 3^{0}=1 \quad 3^2=9\quad 3^3=27\quad 3^4=81 \quad 3^5=243\quad \text{...}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    We observe that the unit digits repeat in a cycle: 3, 9, 1, 7, 8, 9, ...
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Calculating Units Digits:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \\[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    3^1 3^2 \quad 3^3 \quad 3^4 \quad \ldots \quad 3^{2004}
