[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Sam the Sham is an unfair shoe salesman. He has a pair of shoes that was priced at $\$60$ last week. To entice customers, he wants to put a "$25\%$ off'' tag on the shoes but he still wants the customer to pay $\$60$ for the shoes. He raises the price of the shoes so that after the $25\%$ discount the shoes will cost $\$60$. In dollars, what must the new price of the shoes be before the discount?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Yes, given the information,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The original price of the shoes was 60 dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Sam raises the price by 25%, subsequently claiming that the customer should pay 60 dollars considering the $25\%$ off discount.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's solve the problem step by step using Python code for accurate and fast calculations.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Calculate the original price before applying the $25\%$ discount.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Apply the $25\%$ discount to the original price to get the new price after the discount.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's do this calculation.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Original price = $60
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Applying $25\%$ discount on the original price:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Discount} = 0.25 \times 60 = 15
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    So, the new price after the discount is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{New price} = 60 - 15 = 45
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the new price of the shoes before the discount was $45. We can confirm this using Python code.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Original price of the shoes
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m original_price = 60
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Applying 25% discount
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m discount = 0.25 * original_price
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m new_price = original_price - discount
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m print(new_price)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```output
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 45.0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The new price of the shoes before the discount was \(\boxed{45}\) dollars.<|endoftext|>
