[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute $\tan 45^\circ$, we use the definition of the tangent function. The tangent of an angle is the ratio of the opposite side to the adjacent side in a right triangle. For a $45^\circ$ angle, the opposite side is equal to the adjacent side, and the hypotenuse is $\infty$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The definition of the tangent of a $45^\circ$ angle is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \tan 45^\circ = \frac{\text{opposite}}{\text{adjacent}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
