[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Yes, this is a problem of permutations. A permutation is a rearrangement of elements in a set. The number of permutations of n distinct elements is n!.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In this case, we have 7 distinct colored hats, so the number of permutations of them is 7!.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's calculate that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1st way: H1H2H3H4H5H6H7
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2nd way: H2H3H4H5H6H7H1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3rd way: H3H4H5H6H7H1H2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4th way: H4H5H6H7H1H2H3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5th way: H5H6H7H1H2H3H4
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6th way: H6H7H1H2H3H4H5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 7th way: H7H1H2H3H4H5H6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here, there are 7! different permutations since there is a unique way to arrange the hats.
