[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine my brother's age, let's denote my age as \(x\) years.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. According to the problem, six years from now, my brother will be twice as old as I will be. So, six years later, my brother's age will be \(2x + 6\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. We are also told that my brother is 4 times as old as I am six years from now. So, six years ago, my brother's age was \(2x\). Therefore, my brother's age six years from now will be \(2 \times 2x\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2x + 6 = 2 \times 2x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Simplify the equation from step 2:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2x + 6 = 4x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. Rearrange the equation to isolate \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6 = 4x - 2x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6 = 2x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. Solve for \(x\) to find my current age:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = \frac{6}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = 3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, my brother is currently \(\boxed{3}\) years old.<|endoftext|>
