[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    The prime numbers are 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, etc. The smallest prime number is 2. Therefore, the second smallest prime number is 3.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Square the second smallest prime number:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    3^2 = 3 \times 3 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Find the cube of the result from step 2:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    9^3 = 9 \times 9 \times 9 = 81 \times 9 = 729
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the cube of the square of the second smallest prime number is \boxed{729}.
