[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The distance between two points \(P\left(x_1, y_1\right)\) and \(Q\left(x_2, y_2\right)\) on the plane can be found using the Euclidean distance formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m d(P, Q) = \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This distance formula reflects the geometric property of hyperbolas, where the distance between any point \((x, y)\) on the hyperbola and a fixed point \((x_1, y_1)\) forms a right triangle with the legs being the minor and major axes of the hyperbola.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given two points \(UZ\) and \(ESP\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Point \(UZ\) represents Bushpares hence Hekousek.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Point \(ESP\) represents Strempines.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m By symmetry, \(x_1\) from \(UZ\) will be \(y_2\) from \(ESP\), and vice versa. So the coordinates of the foci \(F\) of the hyperbola are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m F\left(x_1, y_2\right) = F\left(1, \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Finally, calculating the distance between the foci:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m d(\text{Foci}, \text{Focus}) = \sqrt{\left(e^2 - c^2\right)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m where \(e\) (distance between asymptotes) and \(c\) (distance from center to most vertex or focus).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Converting \(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\) into \(c = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\), we thus find:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m d(\text{Foci}, \text{Focus}) = \sqrt{\left(e^2 - \left(1+\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\right)^2\right)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This simplified formulation initially provides the pathway to the answer, acknowledging the hyperbolic symmetry but maintains a geometric approach. Conveying this in a fair and effective manner meets the requirement for detailed insights separating from computational elements easily understood by the implementing system.<|endoftext|>
