[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Regarding solving equations with $t$, we note that the equation $t^2+10t-6y=56$ describes ${y}$ as a function, where $y$ is the initial height and $t$ is the time seconds. To find the time when the ball hits the ground, we have:
