[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m **Step-by-Step Solution and Formula Applied:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given \( \angle ABO = 60^\circ \) means measuring \(\angle ABO\) and the side \(BO = 5\) helps us solve into two trapezoids.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given that \( \frac{AB}{2} = BO \), we will use the formula for the length of a chion:
