[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m When the base-10 integers 200 and 1200 are expressed in base 2, how many more digits does 1200 have than 200 (after being converted)?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve this problem, we need to convert the given base-10 integers into binary and compare the lengths of the binary representations.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Convert 200 into binary.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 200 can be converted into binary as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 200 = 10010002
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The binary representation of 200 is `1001000`, which has 6 digits.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Convert 1200 into binary.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1200 can be converted into binary as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1200 = 1001000000100002
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The binary representation of 1200 is `1001000000100002`, which has 19 digits.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Calculate the difference in the number of digits:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Difference = Number of digits in `10010002` - Number of digits in `1001000000100002`
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m            = 6 - 19
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m            = -13
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since the number of digits cannot be negative, we'll take the absolute value of the difference:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 32 - 13 = 19
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, 1200 has 19 more digits than 200 after being converted.
