[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m For the second triangle with a perimeter of (110 cm), we can use the same ratio. That is, if the sides of the triangle are in the ratio (6 cm)/(7 cm)/(9 cm), the perimeter of the triangle, which is (a + b + c) when calculated using the sides (a, b, and c) will be (9/7) * 110 = 540 / 7 = 78 cm.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The longest side in the second triangle is then ((78 cm)/(110 cm)) = 1 / 1.903 or the fraction 10 / 19.
