[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve the inequality \(\frac{1}{x^2+1} > \frac{3}{x} + \frac{17}{10}\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Clear the denominators by finding a common denominator**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \frac{1}{x^2+1} > \frac{3}{x} + \frac{17}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    To clear the fractions, multiply every term by \(10x(x^2+1)\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    10x > 10\left(\frac{3x}{x}\right) + 10\left(\frac{17(x^2+1)}{10x}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Simplify the terms on the right-hand side**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    10x = \frac{3 \cdot 10x}{x} + \frac{17 \cdot 10(x^2+1) - 17x}{10x}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    10x = \frac{30x}{x} + \frac{17(x^2+1)}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    10x = 30 + \frac{17(x^2+1)}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Combine the fractions on the right-hand side**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    10x = 30 + \frac{17x^2 + 17}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    10x = 30 + 1.7x^2 + 1.7
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    10x = 31.7x^2 + 31.7
