[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Sure, I can help you solve this problem.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's identify the common difference (d) of the given arithmetic sequence. The first term (a) is -8, and the common difference is 10 - (-8) = 18.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we can use the formula for the $n^{th}$ term of an arithmetic sequence to find the $2005^{\text{th}}$ term ($a_{2005}$):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$a_{2005} = a + (n - 1)d$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substituting the values, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$a_{2005} = -8 + (2005 - 1) \times 18$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$a_{2005} = -8 + 2004 \times 18$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$a_{2005} = -8 + 36176$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$a_{2005} = 36168$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we need to find the difference between the $2005^{\text{th}}$ term ($a_{2005}$) and the $2004^{\text{th}}$ term ($a_{2004}$).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$a_{2005} - a_{2004} = 36168 - 36169$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
