[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The matrix
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} 3 & -1 \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}\]is its own inverse.  Enter the ordered pair $(c,d).$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine the values of \( c \) and \( d \) such that the matrix
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -1 \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m is its own inverse, we need to ensure that the product of the matrix and its inverse is the identity matrix. The identity matrix \( I \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m I = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's denote the matrix by \( A \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -1 \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The inverse of \( A \), denoted \( A^{-1} \), can be found using the formula for the inverse of a 2x2 matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A^{-1} = \frac{1}{\det(A)} \begin{pmatrix} d & 1 \\ -c & 3 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m where \(\det(A)\) is the determinant of \( A \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we calculate the determinant of \( A \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \det(A) = \det \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -1 \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} = (3 \cdot d) - (-1 \cdot c) = 3d + c
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \( A \) is its own inverse, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A \cdot A^{-1} = I
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Multiplying both sides by \( A^{-1} \), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A^{-1} \cdot A = I \quad \text{or} \quad I = A^{-1} \cdot A
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A \cdot A^{-1} = 1 \cdot A^2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This gives us:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -1 \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -1 \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 1: Compute \( A \cdot A^{-1} \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we calculate \( A^2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A^2 = A \cdot A = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -1 \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -1 \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \cdot 3 + (-1) \cdot c & 3 \cdot (-1) + (-1) \cdot d \\ c \cdot 3 + d \cdot c & c \cdot (-1) + d \cdot d \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 9 - c & -3 - d \\ 3c + cd & -c + d^2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 2: Set up the determinant equation
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 9 - c & -3 - d \\ 3c + cd & -c + d^2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (9 - c) - (-3 - d) = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 9 - c + 3 + d = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 12 + c - d = 1 \quad \text{(1)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (3c + cd) - (-c + d^2) = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3c + cd + c - d^2 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4c + cd - d^2 = 1 \quad \text{(2)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 3: Solve the system of equations
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We now have two equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 12 + c - d = 1 \quad \text{(1)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4c + cd - d^2 = 1 \quad \text{(2)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From equation (1):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m c - d = 1 - 12
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m c - d = -11 \quad \text{(3)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
