[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (2x + y) - (x + y) = 13 - 10
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplifying, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2x + y - x - y = 3 \implies x = 3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, substitute \(x = 3\) back into the first equation to find \(y\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x + y = 10 \implies 3 + y = 10 \implies y = 7
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now that we have \(x = 3\) and \(y = 7\), we can calculate \(x^2 - y^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x^2 - y^2 = x^2 - (y^2 - 2xy + x^2) = 2x^2 - y^2 + 2xy - x^2 = x^2 + 2xy - y^2 = (x + y)^2 - 3xy
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substitute \(x + y = 10\) and \(xy = 3 \cdot 7 = 21\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (x + y)^2 - 3xy = 10^2 - 3 \cdot 21 = 100 - 63 = 37
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the value of \(x^2 - y^2\) is \(\boxed{37}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -40
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
