[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Understand the recursive nature of the function. The function now depends on the output of the function $f(x)$ for all integers greater than 1000.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Use the first case of the function definition: $f(n) = n - 3$ for $n \geq 1000$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Iterate the recursive calls until we reach the point where $n$ is less than 1000. In each iteration, we will find the value $f(n)$. Then, we will use this value as the input for the next recursive call in the alternating function.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. Ensure to handle all possible cases and apply the recursive definitions until we reach $n = 0$ or $n = 1000$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's implement this step-by-step process:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m def f(n):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     if n >= 1000:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m         return n - 3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     else:
