[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m What is the first digit (from left to right) of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the first digit (from left to right) of the base 8 representation of $473_{10}$, we need to convert it to base 8.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Determine the highest power of 8 less than or equal to 473:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The highest power of 8 less than or equal to 473 is \(8^3 = 512\). To check if 512 is even, we observe that 512 is even.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Therefore, \(8^3\) is indeed a power of 8.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Calculate the number of base 8 digits:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Since \(8^3 = 512\) is the highest power of 8 less than or equal to 473, and it is already a power of 8, we only need one digit to represent it.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Convert 512 to base 8:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - To convert 512 to base 8, we repeatedly divide 512 by 8 and keep track of the remainders.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \begin{array}{r|l}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      512 \div 8 &= 64 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      64 \div 8 &= 8 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      8 \div 8 &= 1 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      1 \div 8 &= 0 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Reading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \(512_{10} = 1000_8\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Extract the first digit:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The base 8 representation of 473 is \(473_10\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The first digit is the leftmost digit in this base 8 representation, which is \(0\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the first digit of the base 8 representation of \(473_{10}\) is \(\boxed{0}\).<|endoftext|>
