[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Compute $\arcsin \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}.$  Express your answer in radians.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute \(\arcsin \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\), we need to find the angle \(\theta\) in the principal range of the arc sine function, which is from \(-\frac{\pi}{2}\) to \(\frac{\pi}{2}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The formula for \(\arcsin x\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \arcsin x = \begin{cases} 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     -\frac{\pi}{2} & \text{if } -1 \leq x \leq 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     \frac{\pi}{2} & \text{if } x > 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     \frac{3\pi}{2} & \text{if } x < -1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given \(x = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\), we need to determine which case applies.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Check which cases match:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(-1 \leq x \leq 1\) implies \(-\sqrt{2} \leq x \leq \sqrt{2}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(x > 1\) implies \(x > \sqrt{2}\), which is not in the given range.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(x < -1\) implies \(-\sqrt{2} \leq x < -\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\), which is not in the given range.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(\sqrt{2} \approx 1.414\) and \(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \approx 0.707\), we can see that \(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} > 1\) and this corresponds to the second case of the arcsine formula. Therefore, we use:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \arcsin \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} = \frac{\pi}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\frac{\pi}{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
