[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Two triangles are similar. The ratio of their areas is 1:4. If the height of the smaller triangle is 3 cm, how long is the corresponding height of the larger triangle, in centimeters?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve this problem, we can use the properties of similar triangles. The ratio of the areas of two similar triangles is equal to the square of the ratio of their corresponding side lengths.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given that the ratio of the areas of the two triangles is 1:4, we can set up the following equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area}_1 : \text{Area}_2 = 1 : 4
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here, \(\text{Area}_1\) and \(\text{Area}_2\) are the areas of the first and second triangles, respectively. Since the ratio of their areas is 1:4, it follows that the ratio of their corresponding side lengths is also 1:4.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The ratio of the corresponding height (or altitude) of the triangles is equal to 1:4. This means that if the height of the smaller triangle is 3 cm, the height of the larger triangle will also be 4 times the height of the smaller triangle.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the height of the larger triangle, we multiply the height of the smaller triangle by 4:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Height of the larger triangle} = 4 \times \text{Height of the smaller triangle} = 4 \times 3 \, \text{cm} = 12 \, \text{cm}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the corresponding height of the larger triangle is \(\boxed{12}\) cm.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
