[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the perfect-square integer that is closest to 273, we can start by estimating the square root of 273:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \sqrt{273} \approx 16.5179
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since the square of 16.5179 is less than 273, we consider 16 as our starting point. Now, we check the square of 15 to see if it's greater than 273:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 15^2 = 225
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since 225 is less than 273, the closest perfect-square integer to 273 is 16.
