[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $a_1+a_2= \vec {t} t_\mathrm{0}$ . Show that these two conditions guarantee two different common vectors in  $\,\vec s = t_1\,\vec{4}t_2$ $\,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \vec t=vec \,r(t)$ What does t look like here ?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m What argument would you use to solve this problem. This is similar to trying to solve 
