[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m draw(Circle((30,45), 22));
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m draw(Circle((58, 45), 22));
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m label("1000", (44, 45));
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [/asy]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m I assume that $A$ and $B$ are disjoint Venn diagrams.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, $|A| + |B| = 3011$ and $|A \cap B| = 1000$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We must also have $|A| \ge |B|$ because $A$ has a higher "density" than $B$, and $B$ has twice as many elements as $A$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Setting up the equation, we get $|B| = 1000$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since $|A \cap B| = 1000$, $|A| \ge 1000$ as well.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, $|A| = 1000 + |A| \le 3010$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since $A \ne B$, $A$ has a higher number of elements than $B$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m If we divide the proportion of elements in $A$ by the proportion of elements in $B$, we get $\frac{|A|}{|B|} = \frac{1000}{1000} = 1$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, $|A| = \frac{1000}{1} = \boxed{1000}$.
