[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve for the values of \( x \) in the determinant equation
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{vmatrix} a + x & a - x & a - x \\ a - x & a + x & a - x \\ a - x & a - x & a + x \end{vmatrix} = 0,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m we will use cofactor expansion.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's write down the determinant:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{det} = \begin{vmatrix} a + x & a - x & a - x \\ a - x & a + x & a - x \\ a - x & a - x & a + x \end{vmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We will expand this determinant along the first row. The determinant can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{det} = (a + x) \begin{vmatrix} a + x & a - x \\ a - x & a + x \end{vmatrix} - (a - x) \begin{vmatrix} a - x & a - x \\ a - x & a + x \end{vmatrix} + (a - x) \begin{vmatrix} a - x & a + x \\ a - x & a + x \end{vmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we need to compute each of the 2x2 determinants. Notice that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{vmatrix} a + x & a - x \\ a - x & a + x \end{vmatrix} = (a + x)(a + x) - (a - x)(a - x) = (a + x)^2 - (a - x)^2,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{vmatrix} a - x & a - x \\ a - x & a + x \end{vmatrix} = (a - x)(a + x) - (a - x)(a - x) = (a - x)^2 - (a - x)^2 = 0,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{vmatrix} a - x & a + x \\ a - x & a + x \end{vmatrix} = (a - x)(a - x) - (a - x)(a + x) = (a - x)^2 - (a - x)^2 = -2a^2.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substituting these back into the expression for the determinant, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{det} = (a + x)((a + x)^2 - (a - x)^2) - (a - x)(0) + (a - x)(-2a^2).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplify each term:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (a + x)((a + x)^2 - (a - x)^2) = (a + x)(a^2 + 2ax + x^2 - (a^2 - 2ax + x^2)) = (a + x)(2ax + 2x) = (a + x)(2x(a + 1)).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -(a - x)(-2a^2) = -2a^3 + 2a^2(x) = -2a^3 + 2ax^2.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So the determinant becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (a + x)(2x(a + 1)) - 2a^3 + 2ax^2 = 2a^2x + a + 2x^2a - 2a^3 + 2ax^2 = 3x^2a + a + 3ax^2 - 2a^3.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Set the determinant equal to zero:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3x^2a + a + 3ax^2 - 2a^3 = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Factor out the common term \(a\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m a(3x^2 + 1 + 3x^2 - 2a^2) = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This gives us two factors:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3x^2 + 1 + 3x^2 - 2a^2 = 0 \quad \text{or} \quad 3x^2 + 1 = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Solve the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3x^2 + 1 = 0 \implies 3x^2 = -1 \implies x^2 = -\frac{1}{3} \implies x = \pm \frac{i}{\sqrt{3}}.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Solve the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3x^2 + 1 = 0 \implies 3x^2 = -1 \implies x^2 = -\frac{1}{3} \implies x = \pm \frac{i}{\sqrt{3}}.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the solutions are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = \frac{i}{\sqrt{3}}, \quad x = -\frac{i}{\sqrt{3}}.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The possible values of \(x\) are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
