[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ## Step 3: Calculate the linear relationship between the distance taken from the chosen points and the total distance to the chosen point.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The sums of the distances calculated from computing each side distance add up to the total distance.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ## Step 4: Convert the given distances to integration. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m When adding up the total area of all possible points, we use addition, which allows us to evaluate an integral.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ## Step 5: Set up the integral equation and solve. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We break down the area of one triangle into squares, affecting our variable of integration.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ## Step 6: Evaluate the integral for each side.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Along a side, we consider the triangle portion divided into smaller triangles, which are rectangles with specific height and width.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ## Step 7: Set up the integral formula, integrating over the entire space.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To clarify, interpreting your notes about adding the areas of intersection divided by orientation and the provided information from the image, the total area can be calculated by repeatedly integrating proportionally around each side (since we have an overlap issue identically between adjacent sides).
