[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Certainly. We can factor a variable with a exponent base step-by-step like this:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 1: Factor $55z^{17}$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The prime factor of $55$ is $5 \cdot 11$. We can expand the factor:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$55z^{17} = 5 \cdot 11 \cdot z^{17}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 2: Factor $121z^{34}$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $121$ is $11 \cdot 11$, so we can use a similar step-by-step approach for this part:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$121z^{34} = 11 \cdot 101 \cdot z^{34}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 3: Combine the two factors
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now we can multiply both sides of the equation by $z^{17}$ to cancel out the exponents:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$55z^{17} \cdot z^{17} + 121z^{34} \cdot z^{17} = 5 \cdot 101 \cdot z^{17} + 11 \cdot 11 \cdot z^{34}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 4: Slowly undo the exponents again
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can undo these steps to get: $z^{17}(55 \cdot z^{17} + 121z^{17}) = z^{17}(5 + 11)(z^{17} \cdot z) = z^{17} \cdot 16 \cdot z^{18} = z^{17+18} \cdot 16 = z^{35} \cdot 16$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m That's it! The first step was to write $z^{17}$ by $55z^{17}$, and the second step was to write $z^{34}$ by $121z^{34}$, but to manually do this requires a good understanding of high-school algebra. I'm sure you're good with this already, so you should be able to handle the rest. Here's a walkthrough: $$55z^{17} + 121z^{34} $$ $$= 55 + 1333z^{17} + 121z^{34}$$ $$= 121z^{17} + 55 + 1333z^{17}$$ $$= (z^{17} + 13z^{17})(121 + 55)$$ $$= 13 \cdot 13z^{17} + 121 + 55$$ $$13^2z^{17} + 13 \cdot z^{17} + 121 + 55$$ $$= 13z^{17}(13 + 1) + z^{17}(121 + 55)$$ $$= 13z^{17}(13 + 1)(13 + 55)$$ $$= 13z^{17}(13 + 1)(13 + 55)$$ $$= 13 \cdot 13z^{17} + 13 \cdot 13(13 + 55) + (13 + 1)(13 + 55)$$ $$= 169z^{17} + 13 \cdot 13 \cdot 13 + 170 \cdot 13 + 160$$ $$= 169z^{17}<|endoftext|>
