[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Solving these equations gives:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[a = 2 \quad \text{or} \quad a = -2\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m However, we must also consider the factorization of the quadratic equation $a^2 - 4$. The equation $a^2 - 4 = 0$ can be written as $(a - 2)(a + 2) = 0$, which implies that $a = 2$ and $a = -2$ are the roots of the quadratic equation. These roots, when removed from the original quadratic equation, still make the expression undefined (for those values of $a$ that make both forms of the denominator zero simultaneously).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's consider these roots programmatically to ensure we didn't miss any. We will evaluate the expression at $a = 2$ and $a = -2$ programmatically to check if they cause any singularity.
