[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine how many positive integers less than or equal to 10,000 are divisible by 2, 5, or 10, we need to use the principle of inclusion and exclusion. The principle of inclusion and exclusion for three sets \( S_1, S_2, \) and \( S_3 \) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m |S_1 \cup S_2 \cup S_3| = |S_1| + |S_2| + |S_3| - |S_1 \cap S_2| - |S_1 \cap S_3| - |S_2 \cap S_3| + |S_1 \cap S_2 \cap S_3|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here, the sets are \( S = \{1, 2, 3, \ldots, 10000\} \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \( S_1 = \{2, 4, 6, \ldots, 10000\} \) (numbers divisible by 2)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \( S_2 = \{5, 10, 15, \ldots, 10000\} \) (numbers divisible by 5)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \( S_3 = \{10, 20, 30, \ldots, 10000\} \) (numbers divisible by 10)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we calculate the sizes of the individual sets:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m |S| = 25000
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we find the sizes of the pairwise intersections \( S_1 \cap S_2 \) and \( S_1 \cap S_3 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m |S_1 \cap S_2| = 25000
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m |S_1 \cap S_3| = 25000
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m |S_2 \cap S_3| = 25000
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we need to find the size of the intersection of \( S_1 \cap S_2 \) and \( S_1 \cap S_3 \). Since \( S_2 \) and \( S_3 \) are exactly the sets we have, their intersections are simply \( S_1 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m |S_1 \cap S_2 \cap S_3| = 25000
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We will now sum the sizes of the individual sets and the intersections:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m |S_1 \cup S_2 \cup S_3| = 25000 + 25000 - 25000 - 25000 - 25000 + 25000
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m |S_1 \cup S_2 \cup S_3| = 25000
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the total number of positive integers less than or equal to 10,000 that are divisible by 2, 5, or 10 is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{25000}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
