[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Centers of symmetric $\triangle ABC$ and $\triangle ACD$ are $H$ and $K,$ respectively, and are equidistant from two diagonal $Eq$ and $He$ of $\triangle ABC.$ Let point $L$ lie on $\overline{A C}$ such that $EQ = HQ$ and $HE = HL.$ If triangle $CLH$ is similar to triangle $ALD$ with a common perimeter, then what is the length of segment $\overline{M N}$, where point $M$ is the midpoint of side $\overline{L D} ?$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
