[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The projection of $\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 3 \\ z \end{pmatrix}$ onto $\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}$ is
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\frac{12}{35} \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}.\]Find $z.$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the value of \( z \), we need to calculate the projection of the vector \(\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 3 \\ z \end{pmatrix}\) onto the vector \(\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}\). The formula for the projection of a vector \(\mathbf{a}\) onto a vector \(\mathbf{b}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{a} = \frac{\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b}}{\mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b}} \mathbf{b}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here, \(\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 3 \\ z \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}\). The cross product \(\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}\) will give us the normalized version of \(\mathbf{a}\). After that, we can compute the projection using the equation above.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step-by-Step Calculation
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Compute the cross product \(\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} = \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    0 & 3 & z \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -3 & 5 & -1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} = \mathbf{i} \left(3 \cdot (-1) - z \cdot 5\right) - \mathbf{j} \left(0 \cdot (-1) - z \cdot (-3)\right) + \mathbf{k} \left(0 \cdot 5 - 3 \cdot (-3)\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} = \mathbf{i} (-3 - 5z) - \mathbf{j} (3z) + \mathbf{k} (0 + 9)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -3 - 5z \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -3z \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    9
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Compute the dot product \(\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b}\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = 0 \cdot (-3) + 3 \cdot 5 + z \cdot (-1)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = 0 + 15 - z
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Compute the dot product \(\mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b}\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b} = (-3) \cdot (-3) + 5 \cdot 5 + (-1) \cdot (-1)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b} = 9 + 25 + 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b} = 35
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Compute the projection:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{a} = \frac{\begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -3 - 5z \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -3z \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    9
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \end{pmatrix}}{35} \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -3 \\ 5 \\ -1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    = \frac{1}{35} \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -3 - 5z \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -3z \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    9
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    = \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \frac{-3 - 5z}{35} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \frac{-3z}{35} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \frac{9}{35}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    We are given that this projection is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{a} = \frac{12}{35} \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -3 \\ 5 \\ -1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Equating the scalar components:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \frac{-3 - 5z}{35} = \frac{12}{35}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Cross multiply to solve for \(z\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -3 - 5z = 12
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -5z = 12 + 3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -5z = 15
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    z = -3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Final Answer
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the value of \( z \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{-3}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
