[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the projection of the vector \(\mathbf{a}\) onto \(\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}\), we can use the formula for the projection of vector \(\mathbf{a}\) onto \(\mathbf{b}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{a} = \frac{\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b}}{\mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b}} \mathbf{b}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m where \(\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} a_1 \\ a_2 \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we need to calculate \(\mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b} = 1 \cdot 1 + (-3) \cdot (-3) = 1 + 9 = 10
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we can find the projection:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{a} = \frac{2}{10} \mathbf{b} = \frac{1}{5} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{5} \\ -\frac{3}{5} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the projection of \(\mathbf{a}\) onto \(\mathbf{b}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{5} \\ -\frac{3}{5} \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 1/5 \\ -3/5 \end{pmatrix}
