[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve this problem, we will use the system of equations provided. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given the Venn diagram and the intersections:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ |A| = 2 |B| \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ |A \cup B| = |A| + |B| - |A \cap B| \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ |A \cap B| = 1000 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's express these equations in terms of \(|A|\) and \(|B|\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. \( |A| = 2 |B| \) can be converted to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ |A| = 2(|B|) = 2 \times 1000 = 2000 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The equations now become:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 2000 = 2|B| \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 1000 = |A| + |B| - 1000 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Solving these equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 1000 = |A| + |B| - 1000 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 2000 = 2|B| \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ |B| = 1000/2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ |B| = 500 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substituting \(|B| = 500\) in the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 2000 = 2 \times 500 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 2000 = 1000 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This confirms our calculations are correct. So, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{2000}
