[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the units digit of \(29 \cdot 79 + 31 \cdot 81\), we will calculate the product \(29 \cdot 79\) and then add \(31 \cdot 81\) to it. We will handle each step sequentially to identify the units digit.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we compute \(29 \cdot 79\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 29 \cdot 79 = 29 \cdot (80 - 1) = 29 \cdot 80 - 29 \cdot 1 = 2320 - 29 = 2291
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we compute \(31 \cdot 81\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 31 \cdot 81 = 31 \cdot (80 + 1) = 31 \cdot 80 + 31 \cdot 1 = 2480 + 31 = 2511
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we add the two products:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2291 + 2511 = 4802
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The units digit of 4802 is 2. Therefore, the units digit of \(29 \cdot 79 + 31 \cdot 81\) is \(\boxed{2}\).<|endoftext|>
