[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To convert the base-16 number \( 021_{16} \) to a base-10 integer, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Identify the positional values:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Each digit in base-16 can be independently multiplied by the appropriate power of 16.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Assign positions to the base-16 digit:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The digit 2 is in the 16th position.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The digit 1 is in the 15th position.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Multiply these values to find the base-10 number:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    021_{16} &= 0 \times 16^2 + 2 \times 16^1 + 1 \times 16^0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    &= 0 \times 256 + 2 \times 16 + 1 \times 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    &= 0 + 32 + 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    &= 33
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the base-10 equivalent of \( 021_{16} \) is \boxed{33}.<|endoftext|>
