[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To simplify the given complex expression $(2+3i)(1-2i)$, we will use the distributive property of multiplication. This means we will multiply each term in the first complex number by each term in the second complex number.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Distribute each term in the first complex number $(2+3i)$ to each term in the second complex number $(1-2i)$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$(2+3i)(1-2i) = 2 \cdot 1 + 2 \cdot (-2i) + 3i \cdot 1 + 3i \cdot (-2i).$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Calculate each term:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$= 2 - 4i + 3i - 6i^2.$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Combine like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The terms involving $\text{i}$ ($i$) cancel each other out:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$= 2 - 6i - 6i^2.$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. Substitute $i$ with $\frac{1}{i} = -1$, which resembles an imaginary number:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$= 2 - 6\left(-1\right) - 6\left(-\frac{1}{i}\right),$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m which simplifies as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$= 2 + 6 + 6\left(\frac{1}{i}\right),$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$= 8 + 6i. $$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. Finally, write the answer as a floating-point number:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$= 8.6632\\
