[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. First, identify the range of three-digit integers: Between 100 and 999 (inclusive). This means \(100 \leq a \leq 999\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. According to the property of multiples, a number \(a\) is divisible by 13 if \(a\) can be written as \(13 \times b\) where \(b\) is an integer.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. We need to determine how many three-digit numbers \(a\) can be written as \(13 \times b\). That is, we need to find the largest integer \(b\) such that \(13b\) is still a three-digit number (with \(b\) being an integer).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. Calculate the maximum value for \(b\).
