[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From this, we realize that \(b\) cannot exceed 6 because any larger value for \(b\) would make \(a\) less than 100.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6. Therefore, the maximum value for \(a\) is 78.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 7. To verify that there isn't any other value of \(b\) to be considered, we check the next possible value for \(b\), which is not an integer.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 8. Hence, we have checked all integers up to 6 as the digits \(b\) that could potentially make \(a\) a three-digit number.
