[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given the matrix \(\mathbf{M}\) and the equation \(\mathbf{M} \mathbf{v} = -4 \mathbf{v}\) for all three-dimensional vectors \(\mathbf{v}\), we can start by letting \(\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\ v_2 \\ v_3 \end{pmatrix}\). This implies:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\ v_2 \\ v_3 \end{pmatrix} = -4 \begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\ v_2 \\ v_3 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This gives us two separate equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. \(\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\ v_2 \\ v_3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -4v_1 \\ -4v_2 \\ -4v_3 \end{pmatrix}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. \(\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\ v_2 \\ v_3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -4v_1 \\ -4v_2 \\ -4v_3 \end{pmatrix}\) (which is the same equation after rearranging terms)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This equation suggests that \(\mathbf{M}\) must be a scalar multiple of the identity matrix \(\mathbf{I}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{M} = \mathbf{I}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(\mathbf{M}\) is a \(3 \times 3\) matrix and \(\mathbf{I}\) is \(3 \times 3\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{M} = \mathbf{I}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the matrix \(\mathbf{M}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This is the identity matrix, which appears when the determinant of \(\mathbf{I}\) is zero, indicating the only solution where \(\mathbf{M}\) is a matrix that satisfies the given equation.<|endoftext|>
