[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    M_2 + 4 M_3 = 0 \quad \text{(2)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    M_3 = 0 \quad \text{(3)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Solve the system of equations:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    From equation (3), we know that \(M_3 = 0\). So, we can substitute \(M_3\) with \(0\) in equation (2):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    M_2^* = -M_2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Then substitute \(M_2^* = -M_2\) into equation (1):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    M_1 - 4 M_2^* = 0 \implies M_1 + 4 M_2 = 0 \quad \text{(4)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Interpret the constraint \(M_1 - 4 M_2 = 0\) and \(M_2^* = -M_2\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Since \(M_2^* = -M_2\), we can express \(M_2\) in terms of \(M_1\) and \(M_3\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    M_2 = -\frac{M_1}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Substitute \(M_2 = -\frac{M_1}{4}\) into equation (4):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    M_1 + 4 \left(-\frac{M_1}{4}\right) = 0 \implies M_1 + M_1 = 0 \implies 2M_1 = 0 \implies M_1 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. **Determine \(M_2\) and \(M_3\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    M_2 = -\frac{M_1}{4} = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    M_3 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6. **Verify the consistency:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Substitute \(M_1 = 0\), \(M_2 = 0\), and \(M_3 = 0\) into the original equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{M} \mathbf{v} = -4 \mathbf{v}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Since \(\mathbf{M} = \begin{bmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    0 & 0 & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    0 & 0 & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    0 & 0 & 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \end{bmatrix}\), this equation holds for all \(\mathbf{v}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the \(3 \times 3\) matrix \(\mathbf{M}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\begin{bmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 0 & 0 & 0 \\
