[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Divide 12 by 2:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      12 \div 2 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Finally, 6 is not divisible by 2, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 3.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      6 \div 3 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Divide 2 by 2 again:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      2 \div 2 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    So, the prime factorization of 192 is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    192 = 2^6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Simplify \(\sqrt{192}\)**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Substitute the prime factorization of 192 into the square root:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \sqrt{192} = \sqrt{2^6}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Use the property of square roots that \(\sqrt{a^2} = a\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \sqrt{2^6} = 2^3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Calculate \(2^3\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      2^3 = 2 \times 2 \times 2 = 8
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the simplified form of \(\sqrt{192}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{8}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
