[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute \(\tan 20^\circ + \tan 40^\circ + \sqrt{3} \tan 20^\circ \tan 40^\circ\), we can use properties of roots of unity and trigonometric identities. Here is a detailed step-by-step approach:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Utilize the identity for sum of roots of unity:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    The identity \(\tan (60^\circ - x) = \frac{\tan 60^\circ - \tan x}{1 + \tan 60^\circ \tan x}\) can be used here. In this case, let \(x = 40^\circ\). Then, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \tan (60^\circ - 40^\circ) = \frac{\tan 60^\circ - \tan 40^\circ}{1 + \tan 60^\circ \tan 40^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Since \(\tan 60^\circ = \sqrt{3}\) and \(\tan 40^\circ\), we can substitute and simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \tan(20^\circ - 40^\circ) = \frac{\sqrt{3} - \tan 40^\circ}{1 + \sqrt{3} \tan 40^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Express the tangent expressions:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    We know that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \tan (60^\circ - x) = \frac{\tan 60^\circ - \tan x}{1 + \tan 60^\circ \tan x}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Substituting \(x = 40^\circ\), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \tan (60^\circ - 40^\circ) = \frac{\sqrt{3} - \tan 40^\circ}{1 + \sqrt{3} \tan 40^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \tan 20^\circ + \tan 40^\circ + \sqrt{3} \tan 20^\circ \tan 40^\circ = \tan(60^\circ - 40^\circ) + \sqrt{3} \tan 20^\circ \tan 40^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Let \(y = \tan 20^\circ\). Then:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \tan 40^\circ + \sqrt{3} \cdot y = y + \sqrt{3} \cdot \tan 20^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    We need to find \(\tan 20^\circ + \tan 40^\circ\). Note that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \tan 20^\circ + \tan 40^\circ = \frac{\tan 60^\circ - \tan 40^\circ}{1 + \tan 60^\circ \tan 40^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Using the identity \(\tan (60^\circ - x) = \frac{\tan 60^\circ - \tan x}{1 + \tan 60^\circ \tan x}\) again, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \tan (60^\circ - 40^\circ) = \frac{\tan 60^\circ - \tan 40^\circ}{1 + \tan 60^\circ \tan 40^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Recall that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \tan (60^\circ - 40^\circ) = \frac{\sqrt{3} - \tan 40^\circ}{1 + \sqrt{3} \tan 40^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    y = \tan 60^\circ - \tan 40^\circ = \sqrt{3} - \tan 40^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Thus:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \tan 20^\circ + \tan 40^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{3} - \tan 40^\circ}{1 + \sqrt{3} \tan 40^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Combine the results:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    We have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \tan 20^\circ + \tan 40^\circ + \sqrt{3} \tan 20^\circ \tan 40^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{3} - \tan 40^\circ}{1 + \sqrt{3} \tan 40^\circ} + \sqrt{3} \cdot \frac{\sqrt{3} - \tan 40^\circ}{1 + \sqrt{3} \tan 40^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Simplifying the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    = \frac{\sqrt{3} - \tan 40^\circ + 3(\tan 30^\circ - \tan 40^\circ)}{1 + \sqrt{3} \tan 40^\circ} = \frac{\sqrt{3} - \tan 40^\circ + 3(\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} - \tan 40^\circ)}{1 + \sqrt{3} \tan 40^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    = \frac{\sqrt{3} - \tan 40^\circ + 3 \left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} - \tan 40^\circ\right)}{1 + \sqrt{3} \tan 40^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    = \frac{\sqrt{3} - \tan 40^\circ + 3 \left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} - \tan 40^\circ\right)}{1 + \sqrt{3} \tan 40^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Using the exact values for \(\tan 20^\circ\) and \(\tan 40^\circ\), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \boxed{1}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]<|endoftext|>
