[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A new green technology can be installed in your home for a one-time installation cost of $\$10,\!000$ and annual maintenance costs of $\$650$ per year. If the green technology is supposed to save you $\$1200$ each year in energy bills, how many whole years will it take to recuperate your costs?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Sure, let's solve the problem step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Calculate the cost per year since the technology will pay it off over the number of years:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Annual maintenance cost: $650
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Annual savings: $1200
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Use the formula:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Cost per year} = \frac{\text{Annual saving}}{\text{Annual maintenance cost}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Substitute the values into the formula:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Cost per year} = \frac{1200}{650}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Perform the division:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \frac{1200}{650} \approx 1.8526 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. **Determine the number of years it will take to pay back the cost:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Number of years} = \frac{\text{Cost per year}}{\text{Annual cost}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Number of years} = \frac{1.8526}{10000}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6. **Perform the division:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \frac{1.8526}{10000} \approx 0.00018526
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 7. **Since the number of years must be a whole number, round it up:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Number of years} = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, it will take \boxed{1} whole year for the green technology to recover its costs.<|endoftext|>
