[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve the problem, we need to determine the fraction of unit cubes that have at least two painted faces on a 6-by-6-by-6 cube.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 1: Total number of unit cubes
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The 6-by-6-by-6 cube has:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 6^3 = 216 \text{ unit cubes} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 2: Total number of unit cubes without any painted faces
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since each face of the cube is a 6-by-6 grid, a 6-by-6-by-6 cube has:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 6 \times 6 \times 6 = 216 \text{ unit cubes on each face} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 216 \times 6 = 1296 \text{ unit cubes in total} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 3: Subtracting the unit cubes without any painted faces
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The unit cubes on the outside of the outer surface of the cube have only one painted face and no painted interior faces. So, these are the only unit cubes without any painted faces on the entire cube.
