[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Compute $\dbinom{30}{27}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute \(\binom{30}{27}\), we will use Pascal's triangle multiplication method. Pascal's triangle allows us to convert binomial coefficients into product terms.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{30}{27} = \frac{30!}{27!(30-27)!}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Calculate factorials:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(30!\) (30 factorial) is the product of all integers from 1 to 30.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(30-27 = 3\) (since we subtract 27 because we are choosing 27 elements).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(27!\) (27 factorial) is the product of all integers from 1 to 27.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Knowledge of factorials:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(30! = 30 \times 29 \times 28 \times \ldots \times 2 = 625,024,015,275,456\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(27! = 27 \times 26 \times 25 \times \ldots \times 1 = 16,972,674,001,200\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Compute the actual value:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    30! = 625,024,015,275,456
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    27! = 16,972,674,001,200
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. Compute \(\binom{30}{27}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \binom{30}{27} = \frac{30!}{27!(30-27)!} = \frac{30!}{27! \cdot 3!}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Since \(3! = 3 \times 2 \times 1 = 6\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \binom{30}{27} = \frac{30!}{27! \cdot 6}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. Simplify the fraction:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \binom{30}{27} = \frac{30!}{27! \cdot 6} = \frac{30 \times 29 \times 28 \times \ldots \times 2}{27 \times 26 \times 25 \times \ldots \times 1 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Notice that \(30!\) includes \(27!\) but missing \(2!\). Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    30! = 27! + 25 \cdot 24 \cdot 23 \cdot \ldots \cdot 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6. Cancel out \(27!\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \binom{30}{27} = \frac{27 + 25 \cdot 24 \cdot 23 \cdot \ldots \cdot 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1}{(30-27)!} = \frac{27 + 28 \cdot 27 \cdot 26 \cdot \ldots \cdot 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1}{3!}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Simplify further:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \binom{30}{27} = \frac{27 + 28 \cdot 27 \cdot 26 \cdot \ldots \cdot 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1}{6}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 7. Calculate the remaining product:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Multiply and simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    27 \cdot 28 \cdot 27 \cdot 26 \cdot \ldots \cdot 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1 = 28 \cdot 27 \cdot 26 \cdot \ldots \cdot 3 \cdot 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - This is a product of a sequence from 28 down to 3.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The result of this product is \(28 \times 27 = 756\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Multiply by any selection from 1 to 27 gives:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      25 \times 24 \times 23 \times \ldots \times 3 \times 2 \times 1 = 756
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 8. So:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \binom{30}{27} = \frac{756 + 756}{6} = \frac{1512}{6} = 252
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Final Answer:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{252}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
