[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the value of $3 \times (7 - 5) - 5$, we need to follow the order of operations, which in this case is simple here, as we are multiplying before subtracting, and finishing with addition.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we simplify inside the parentheses:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3 \times ((7 - 5)) - 5 = 3 \times 2 - 5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we perform the multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3 \times 2 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Then, we perform the subtraction:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6 - 5 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the final answer is $\boxed{1}$.<|endoftext|>
