[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Find $\frac{7}{17} - \frac{4}{51}$. Reduce your answer to simplest form.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To subtract the two fractions, we need a common denominator. In this case, the least common multiple (LCM) of 17 and 51 is 51 × 17 = 867. So, we'll convert both fractions:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $\frac{7}{17} = \frac{7 ⋅ 51}{17 ⋅ 51} = \frac{357}{867}$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m And
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $\frac{4}{51} = \frac{4 ⋅ 17}{51 ⋅ 17} = \frac{68}{867}$
