[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \log_2 \frac{2}{1} + \log_2 \frac{3}{2} + \cdots + \log_2 \frac{2009}{2008} + \log_2 \frac{2010}{2009}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can combine the logs using the property \(\log_b (xy) = \log_b x + \log_b y\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \log_2 \left( \frac{2}{1} \cdot \frac{3}{2} \cdot \frac{4}{3} \cdot \cdots \cdot \frac{2010}{2009} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Notice that in the product, all the terms \(\frac{k}{k+1}\) are sequentially decreasing, so they can be grouped:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \log_2 (2010)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we need to express \(2010\) in terms of its prime factors (since logarithms can be taken of a product rather than a sum):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2010 = 2 \times 3 \times 5 \times 67
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \log_2 (2010) = \log_2 (2 \times 3 \times 5 \times 67)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using the logarithm property \(\log_b (xy) = \log_b x + \log_b y\), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \log_2 (2010) = \log_2 2 + \log_2 3 + \log_2 5 + \log_2 67
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(\log_b (a) = \frac{\log_c (a)}{\log_c (b)}\), the change of base formula gives:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \log_2 2 = 1, \quad \log_2 3 = \log_2 (3^1) = 1, \quad \log_2 5 = \log_2 (5^1) = 1, \quad \log_2 67 = \log_2 (67^1) = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \log_2 (2010) = 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 4
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the largest integer less than \(\log_2 \frac{2}{1} + \log_2 \frac{3}{2} + \cdots + \log_2 \frac{2009}{2008} + \log_2 \frac{2010}{2009}\) is 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
