[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Allison's cube has a 5 on all six faces. So her roll must be between 1 and 5.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Brian's cube, however, has faces numbered 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5. Three of the faces have a 2, and three have a 6. C'est comme ça, se taise, on va lire, apprenons...
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Brian's roll ranges between 1 and 6.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Noah's cube, being the sum of Allison's and Brian's cube, must be between 1 and 6 as well. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Brian's roll being greater than Brian's index & less than 6 is also 1,2,3,4,5 (depending on where his die was placed).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Noah's roll being greatest than Brian, Allison and zero etc are all valid cases for Allison.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Hence, the probability that Ana Roll is greater than Brian and Noah's is 5/6 per roll.
