[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The integers between 0 and 8 inclusive involve: \{0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8\}.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We want to find out how many of these integers have a unique inverse modulo 9. The inverse of a number \(a\) modulo \(n\) is a number \(b\) such that \(a \times b \equiv 1 \pmod{n}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
