[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Ok, let's convert $\rm{A03_{16}}$ to a base 10 integer.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The 'digits' A through F represent the values 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, and 15 in order.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To do this conversion, we will represent each digit as a power of 16 and add them up.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here's the process:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Identify the binary representation of each digit in order: 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Multiply each binary digit by 16 raised to the indicated power
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Add the results together to get the base 10 representation
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. Convert the result to hexadecimal.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The binary representation of $\rm{A03_{16}}$ is 101010101
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, let's multiply each digit by 2 raised to the indicated power:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 101010101 \times 2^5 &= 3200
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 101010101 \times 2^4 &= 12800
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 101010101 \times 2^3 &= 6400
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 101010101 \times 2^2 &= 3200
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 101010101 \times 16 &= 16000
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, let's add all the items together:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3200 + 12800 + 6400 + 3200 + 16000 &= 24000
