[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let $\bold{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\bold{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$.  Find the area of the parallelogram with vertices $\bold{0}$, $\bold{v}$, $\bold{w}$, and $\bold{v} + \bold{w}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the area of the parallelogram with vertices \(\bold{0}\), \(\bold{v}\), \(\bold{w}\), and \(\bold{v} + \bold{w}\), we can use the cross product of vectors. The area of the parallelogram is given by the magnitude of the cross product of two vectors \(\bold{v}\) and \(\bold{w}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we need to define the vectors:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \bold{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \bold{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The cross product \(\bold{v} \times \bold{w}\) is computed as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \bold{v} \times \bold{w} = \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5 & -3 & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 11 & -2 & 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Expanding this determinant, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \bold{v} \times \bold{w} = \mathbf{i} \left( (-3)(0) - (0)(-2) \right) - \mathbf{j} \left( (5)(0) - (0)(11) \right) + \mathbf{k} \left( (5)(-2) - (-3)(11) \right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = \mathbf{i} (0) - \mathbf{j} (0) + \mathbf{k} (-10 + 33)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 0\mathbf{i} - 0\mathbf{j} + 23\mathbf{k}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 23 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The magnitude of the cross product vector \(\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 23 \end{pmatrix}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \|\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 23 \end{pmatrix}\| = \sqrt{0^2 + 0^2 + 23^2} = \sqrt{256} = 16
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The area of the parallelogram is the absolute value of this magnitude (since it is a geometric statement of the parallelogram area):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{16}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
