[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    We can see that \(a_8 = a_3\) and \(a_{15} = a_7\). The sequence seems to repeat every 19 terms. Therefore, we need to find \(a_{2018} \cdot a_{2020} \cdot a_{2022} \mod 11\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Since 2018, 2020, and 2022 are also in the repeating cycle of 19 terms, we can compute the terms \(a_{2018} \mod 11\), \(a_{2020} \mod 11\), and \(a_{2022} \mod 11\) and then find their product.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    The repeating cycle of the sequence is \(4, 3, 7, 9, 3, 8, 5, 1, 9, 3, 1, 3, 5, 9, 8, 7\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
