[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m John recently bought a used car for $\$5000$ for his pizza delivery job. He gets $\$10$ for each pizza he delivers, but he has to spend $\$3$ on gas for each pizza he delivers. What is the minimum whole number of pizzas John must deliver in order to earn back the money he spent on the car he bought?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine the minimum number of pizzas John must deliver to earn back the money he spent on the car, we need to set up an equation. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let \( x \) be the number of pizzas John delivers. The cost he spent is \( 5000 \) dollars, but he will make \( 10x \) dollars from delivering \( x \) pizzas. Additionally, he will spend \( 3x \) dollars on gas.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The total earnings should equal the cost he spent, so we can write the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 10x + 3x = 5000 + 10x + 3x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplify the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 10x - 3x + 10x = 5000 + 10x + 3x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2x = 5000 + 10x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Rearrange the terms:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5000 = 2x + 10x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5000 = 12x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Solve for \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = \frac{5000}{12}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Calculate the value:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = 416.6667
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since John can only deliver a whole number of pizzas, he must deliver at least 417 pizzas to earn back his \( \$5000 \) cost.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To verify, calculate the earnings:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - If John delivers 0 pizzas, he earns \( 10 \times 0 = 0 \) dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Deliver 1 pizza, he earns \( 10 \times 1 = 10 \) dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Deliver 2 pizzas, he earns \( 10 \times 2 = 20 \) dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Deliver 3 pizzas, he earns \( 10 \times 3 = 30 \) dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Deliver 4 pizzas, he earns \( 10 \times 4 = 40 \) dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Deliver 5 pizzas, he earns \( 10 \times 5 = 50 \) dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Deliver 6 pizzas, he earns \( 10 \times 6 = 60 \) dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Deliver 7 pizzas, he earns \( 10 \times 7 = 70 \) dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Deliver 8 pizzas, he earns \( 10 \times 8 = 80 \) dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Deliver 9 pizzas, he earns \( 10 \times 9 = 90 \) dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Deliver 10 pizzas, he earns \( 10 \times 10 = 100 \) dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Total earnings from delivering 417 pizzas:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 10 \times 417 = 4170 \text{ dollars}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m John spent \( 5000 \) dollars, so he must have earned back \( 5000 - 4170 = 830 \) dollars. Thus, the minimum whole number of pizzas John must deliver is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{417}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
