[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The polynomial $$P(x)=(1+x+x^2+\ldots+x^{17})^2-x^{17}$$has 34 complex zeros of the form $z_k=r_k\left[\cos(2\pi\alpha_k)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m +i\sin(2\pi\alpha_k)\right]$, $k=1,2,3,\ldots,34$, with $0<\alpha_1\le\alpha_2\le\alpha_3\le\dots\le\alpha_{34}<1$ and $r_k>0$. Find $\alpha_1+\alpha_2+\alpha_3+\alpha_4+\alpha_5.$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since $P(x)=(1+x+x^2+\ldots+x^{17})^2-x^{17}$, we find that the only zeros are $x-1$, $x=1$, $x=x+1$, and $x=0$, so our zeros are $-1$, $1$, $x$, and $x+1$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now consider the zeros of $P(x)$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - $P(-1)=(-1)^{-17}=1$ has trivial complex zeros.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - $P(1) = (1)^{-1}=1$ has complex zeros $1+i$ and $1-i$, with multiplicity 2.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - $P(x)=0$ has zeros $x$ and the zeros of $P(x+1)$. Since $x, x+1$ can be nonreal, a zero of $P(x+1)$ has multiplicity 2, and $x$ has multiplicity 1.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus the only solutions are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - $x$ with multiplicity 2 as a zero;
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - $x+1$ with multiplicity 2 as a zero;
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - $x$ and $x+1$ with multiplicity 1 as a zero
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m With $x$ having multiplicity 2 as a zero, $x+1$ $x$ have multiplicity of 2, $x$ and $x+1$ $x$ have multiplicity of 1, and $0$ has no factors of 2.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From this because of the above calculations, we see that the only solutions are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - $x=0$ twice with multiplicity 1;
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - $x=x+1$ twice with multiplicity 2 in the range of $x=-1$,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - $x$ with multiplicity 2 in the range of $x=x+1$, $x$ with multiplicity 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the sum is: \[\theta_1 + \theta_2 + \theta_3 + \theta_4 + \theta_5=0,\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
