[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Sure, let's start with the fact that \( 8! \) (8 factorial) is the product of all positive integers from 1 to 8, and \( 7! \) (7 factorial) is the product of all positive integers from 1 to 7. Therefore, \( 8! - 7! \) will be the product of the integers from 9 to 8 minus the integers from 1 to 7, which simplifies the calculation to just 1. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, we can compute:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 8! - 7! = 9 \times 8 \times 7
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, calculate \( 9 \times 8 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 9 \times 8 = 72
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, calculate \( 72 \times 7 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 72 \times 7 = 504
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{504}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
