[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Define the operation $\spadesuit$ as $a\,\spadesuit\,b = |a- b|$ . What is the value of $2\, \spadesuit\,(4\,\spadesuit\,7)$?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the value of \(2 \spadesuit (4 \spadesuit 7)\), we need to use the operation defined by \(a \spadesuit b = |a - b|\). Let's break this down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we need to evaluate the inner operation \(4 \spadesuit 7\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[4 \spadesuit 7 = |4 - 7| = |-3| = 3.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now that we have the result of the inner operation, we can use this result to evaluate \(2 \spadesuit 3\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[2 \spadesuit 3 = |2 - 3| = |-1| = 1.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the value of \(2 \spadesuit (4 \spadesuit 7)\) is \(\boxed{1}\).<|endoftext|>
