[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Victor ate \(\frac{2}{5}\) of his sandwich. Since Victor eats \(\frac{15}{8}\) of his sandwich, we need to measure out the fraction of Victor's sandwich that Kelsey eats.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Kelsey's eating fraction} = \frac{15}{8} \div \frac{2}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Dividing by a fraction is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal. So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \frac{15}{8} \times \frac{5}{2} = \frac{15 \times 5}{8 \times 2} = \frac{75}{16}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
