[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine the measure of the triangle's largest angle, we can use the properties of isosceles triangles and some basic geometric principles.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Identify the given information:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - One of the angles opposite an equal side is \(40^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The triangle is isosceles, which means the two equal sides are perpendicular and of equal length.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Determine the angles in the triangle's parts:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Since the triangle is isosceles, the two equal angles on each side are equal.
