[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's evaluate $\log_4 {64}$, which means finding the power to which 4 must be raised to obtain 64:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \index{$\log_4 a$}\log_4 a = b \iff a = 4^b$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \index{$\log_4 a$}\log_4 a = \log_4 {64} = b
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we need to find the power of 4 that gives 64. We start by expressing 64 as a power of 4:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \index{$64 = 4^{\log_4 64}$}\begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 64 &= 4^{\log_4 64} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &= 4^{\log_4 \left(2^3\right)} \quad \text{(since $\log_4 4 = 1$)...}\\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &= 4^{3} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &= 64
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, we find that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \index{$64!=4^{\log_4 64}$}\log_4 64 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the answer is $\boxed{2}$..didReceiveMemoryWarning()
