[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve this problem, we need to determine how many girls are in Angie's class. Let's begin by understanding the ratio given:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ============
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2 : 3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 2 / x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = (2 / 3) girls / students
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We know there are 20 students in the class. To find the value of \( x \), we set up the proportion:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \( \frac{2}{3} = \frac{20}{x} \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve for \( x \), we cross-multiply:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
