[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine the number of six-inch by six-inch square tiles needed to cover an area of x square inches, we can use the following formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Area of tile = (side length) x (side length)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In this case, the side length of the tile is 6 inches (since each tile is 6 inches by 6 inches). We know that the area of the rectangular section is 3 x 2 = 6 square inches.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the number of tiles needed is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Tiles_needed = Area of tile / (side length) x (side length)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Tiles_needed = 6 / 6 x 6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Tiles_needed = 1 x 6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Tiles_needed = 6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
