[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine the area of the triangle with vertices \( A(1, 1) \), \( B(6, 1) \), and \( C(3, 7) \), we can use the formula for the area of a triangle given its vertices \((x_1, y_1)\), \((x_2, y_2)\), and \((x_3, y_3)\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's assign the coordinates to the vertices:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \( A(1, 1) \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \( B(6, 1) \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \( C(3, 7) \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substitute these coordinates into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| 1(1 - 7) + 6(7 - 1) + 3(1 - 1) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplify inside the absolute value:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
