[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Compute $\sin 60^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute \(\sin 60^\circ\), we need to recall that \(\sin\) is the sine function. For any angle \(\theta\), \(\sin \theta = \frac{\text{opposite}}{\text{hypotenuse}}\), and \(\sin 60^\circ\) can be derived from the 30-60-90 triangle where the length of the opposite side is 1 and the hypotenuse is \(\sqrt{3}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here's the step-by-step explanation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Identify the sides of the triangle:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The hypotenuse is \(\sqrt{3}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - One of the non-perpendicular sides (hypotenuse opposite \(60^\circ\)) is 1.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The opposite side to \(60^\circ\) is 1 (and it is the same length as the hypotenuse right next to it in this 30-60-90 triangle).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Use the Pythagorean theorem to find the length of the other leg (opposite angle \(60^\circ\)):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    (\text{hypotenuse})^2 = (\text{opposite side})^2 + (\text{adjacent side})^2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    (\sqrt{3})^2 = 1^2 + (\text{adjacent side})^2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    3 = 1 + (\text{adjacent side})^2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    (\text{adjacent side})^2 = 3 - 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{adjacent side}^2 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{adjacent side} = \sqrt{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Now, we can find \(\sin 60^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \sin 60^\circ = \frac{\text{opposite side}}{\text{hypotenuse}} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the value of \(\sin 60^\circ\) is \(\boxed{\frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
