[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Determine the value of the infinite product $(2^{1/3})(4^{1/9})(8^{1/27})(16^{1/81}) \dotsm.$  Enter your answer in the form "\sqrt[a]{b}", which stands for $\sqrt[a]{b}.$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the value of the infinite product \(\prod_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{2^n}{4^n} \cdot \frac{3^n}{8^n} \cdot \frac{4^n}{16^n} \cdots\), we start by simplifying each term in the product.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, observe that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{2^n}{4^n} = \frac{2^n}{2^2^n} = \frac{1}{2^{2n-2}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Similarly, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{3^n}{8^n} = \frac{1}{2^{3n-2}}, \quad \frac{4^n}{16^n} = \frac{1}{2^{4n-2}}, \quad \text{and so on.}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the infinite product can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \prod_{n=1}^{\infty} \left( \frac{1}{2^{2n-2}} \cdot \frac{1}{2^{3n-2}} \cdot \frac{1}{2^{4n-2}} \cdot \ldots \right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can factor out the common denominator \(2^{2n-2}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \left( \frac{1}{2^{2n-2}} \cdot \frac{1}{2^{3n-2}} \cdot \frac{1}{2^{4n-2}} \cdot \ldots \right) = \left( \frac{1}{2^{2n-2}} \right)^2 \left( \frac{1}{2^{2n-2}} \cdot \frac{1}{2^{3n-2}} \cdot \frac{1}{2^{4n-2}} \cdot \ldots \right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{1}{2^{2n}} \cdot \frac{2^{8n}}{2^{2n}} = \frac{1}{2^{2n}} \cdot \frac{2^{8n}}{2^{2n}} = \frac{1}{2^{2n}} \cdot \frac{1}{2^{2n}} = \frac{1}{2^{4n}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the infinite product is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \prod_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{2^n}{4^n} = \frac{1}{2^{4n} \cdot (2^{4n})} = \frac{1}{2^{4n} \cdot 2^{4n}} = \frac{1}{2^{8n}} = \frac{1}{256}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Expressing this in the form \(\sqrt[a]{b}\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \sqrt[8]{256}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the value of the infinite product is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\sqrt[8]{256}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
