[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $\angle CAB + \angle ACD$ is the sum of the measures of arcs $AB$, $AC$, and $BD$.  Since the hexagon $ABCD$ is a regular hexagon, each central angle measures $360^\circ/6 = +60^\circ$, and each exterior angle measures $360^\circ/7$ or $54.44^\circ$.  
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, $ \dfrac{\angle CAB}{360^\circ} = \dfrac{180^\circ}{30} = +60^\circ$ and $\dfrac{\angle ACB_0}{360^\circ} = \dfrac{180^\circ}{30} = +60^\circ$.   
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So we have the following sequence of equalities: 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$\Adjacent + Adjacent = 54.44^\circ + 54.44^\circ = +12^o\cos \angle ACB_0$$ $$ \arc{AB} + \arc{AC} + \arc{BD} = \arc{AB} + \arc{AC} + \arc{BC} = 3 \cdot 36^\circ = +108^\circ \textrm{ } 9^\circ$$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Setting the two equalities together we have  
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $$9^\circ + pEC + 30^\circ + pEC = 12^\circ + pEC + 9^\circ + pEC
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   $$$$2 pEC = 9$$ $$pEC= 4.5^\circ$$ By hypothesis, $\angle ABC = 40^\circ \implies \angle BAC = 180^\circ - 40^\circ - 2 pEC = 100^\circ - 2 \cdot 4.5^\circ = 100^\circ - 9^\circ = 91^\circ$ 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, it might be helpful to first compute the angle scoring.  For example:  
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Angle $\angle CAB = +9^\circ$, Angle $\angle ACB_{0} = +60^\circ$, Angle $\angle BD_{0} = +72^\circ$, hence  
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 	91^\circ + \angle CAB + \angle ACD &= 91^\circ + +9^\circ + 30^\circ + +9^\circ \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 	&= 130^\circ + 6 \cdot 40^\circ \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 	&= 130^\circ + 240^\circ \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 	&= 370^\circ \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 	&= 16 \cdot 225^\circ + 0^\circ + 0^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So the answer is $$\boxed{370^\circ}$$<|endoftext|>
