[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Leah walks 2.5 meters from the base of the pole toward the point where the cable is attached to the ground. Her head just touches the cable, which means the height of the pole is equal to the height of Leah plus the length of the cable.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's denote the length of the cable as \( L \). When Leah walks to the point where the cable is attached, her head touches the cable, which means the height of the pole \( H \) plus the length \( L \) of the cable is equal to Leah's height plus the distance \( x - 2.5 \) from the base to the point where the cable is attached:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
