[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, \( L \) is 4 meters. We need to find the height of the pole \( H \). The height of the pole is the sum of Leah's height and the length of the cable:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ H = 1.5 + L \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ H = 1.5 + 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ H = 5.5 \text{ meters} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the height of the pole is \(\boxed{5.5}\) meters.<|endoftext|>
