[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given that the set of vectors \(\left\{ \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}, \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ k \end{pmatrix} \right\}\) is linearly dependent, we know that the vectors \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ k \end{pmatrix}\) are linearly dependent if and only if one is a scalar multiple of the other. This means there exists some scalar \(a\) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ k \end{pmatrix} = a \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This leads to the equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3 = a \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m k = 2a
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From the first equation, we immediately get \(a = 3\). Substituting this value into the second equation, we find:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m k = 2 \cdot 3 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the only possible value for \(k\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{6}
