[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The numerator is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (-11 + 13i)^3 \cdot (24 - 7i)^4
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 2: Distribute \((-11 + 13i)\) and \((24 - 7i)\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Use the binomial theorem to expand these products:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m a^3 = \left(-11 + 13i\right)^3 = \sum_{k=0}^{3} \binom{3}{k} (-11)^{3-k} (13i)^k
