[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We need to compute $81_9 - 72_9$ using base 9 arithmetic.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Convert both numbers from base 9 to base 10:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - $81_9$ can be converted to base 10 as $8 \cdot 9^1 + 1 \cdot 9^0 = 72 + 1 = 73$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - $72_9$ can be converted to base 10 as $7 \cdot 9^1 + 2 \cdot 9^0 = 63 + 2 = 65$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Perform the subtraction in base 10:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - $73 - 65 = 8$. So, the result is $8$ in base 10.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Convert the result back to base 9:
