[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Find $\sin \frac{11 \pi}{3}.$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find $\sin \frac{11 \pi}{3},$ we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. First, reduce the angle $\pi / 3$ to an equivalent angle within the unit circle by subtracting multiples of $2\pi$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \sin \frac{11 \pi}{3} = \sin \left( \pi / 3 - 2\pi \right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Simplify the angle:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \pi / 3 - 2\pi = \frac{\pi}{3} - \frac{6\pi}{3} = \frac{\pi - 6\pi}{3} = \frac{-5\pi}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Reduce the angle $-5\pi/3$ further by adding multiples of $2\pi$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -5\pi/3 = -2\pi - \pi/3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. Finally, simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -2\pi - \pi/3 = -\frac{6\pi}{3} - \frac{\pi}{3} = -\frac{6\pi + \pi}{3} = -\frac{7\pi}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \sin \frac{11 \pi}{3} = \sin \left( -\frac{7\pi}{3} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. Using the property of sine that $\sin(-\theta) = -\sin(\theta)$, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \sin \left( -\frac{7\pi}{3} \right) = -\sin \left( \frac{7\pi}{3} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6. Now, reduce $\frac{7\pi}{3}$ to an equivalent angle within the first period of sine (from 0 to $2\pi$):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \frac{7\pi}{3} = 2\pi - \frac{\pi}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 7. Since $2\pi$ is a full cycle of the sine function, we know that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \sin(2\pi - \theta) = -\sin(\theta)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 8. Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -\sin \left( \frac{7\pi}{3} \right) = -\left( -\sin \left( \frac{\pi}{3} \right) \right) = \sin \left( \frac{\pi}{3} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 9. From the joint diagram we know:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \sin \left( \frac{\pi}{3} \right) = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 10. Thus, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     \sin \frac{11 \pi}{3} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\boxed{\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}}\]<|endoftext|>
