[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{1}{x^6-x^5+2x^3-3x+1} = -q(x) 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{cases}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, if we multiply the first equation by \(x^6 - 4x^5 + 3x^3 + x^2 - 1\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
