[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We are looking for the largest sequence of polynomials that are decreasing in magnitude and positive at the origin. Let's write the function as a polynomial plus one part:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m q(x) = f(x) + 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Where \(f(x)\) is a polynomial with no repeated terms and whose degree cannot be too high because we're looking for the multiplicity of the root of the denominator.
