[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, we need the highest degree term \(q(x)\) can have. The highest degree term in \(f(x) + 1\) is \(+1\). Note that the multiplicity of \(f(x)\) can be greater than 1 except for \(f(x) = 0\). Given this, we need to have a degree 6 for our \(q(x)\) and cannot have repeats in the denominator that can make it higher than 6 since we're looking at the numerator's leading term. So the largest possible degree for \(q(x)\) is 6.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
