[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Well, let's approach this problem systematically.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We will use the distance formula to calculate the lengths of the three sides of the triangle. Given the coordinates as $(x_1, y_1)$, $(x_2, y_2)$, and $(x_3, y_3)$, the distance between them, denoted as $d$, is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ d = \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ d = \sqrt{(x_3 - x_1)^2 + (y_3 - y_1)^2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ d = \sqrt{(x_1 - x_3)^2 + (y_1 - y_3)^2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We will apply these to our given coordinates:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \( (x_1, y_1) = (11, 1) \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \( (x_2, y_2) = (2, 3) \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \( (x_3, y_3) = (3, 7) \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's calculate the lengths of the sides and then determine the longest side length.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. \( (d_1) = \sqrt{(2 - 11)^2 + (3 - 1)^2} \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. \( (d_2) = \sqrt{(3 - 11)^2 + (7 - 1)^2} \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. \( (d_3) = \sqrt{(3 - 2)^2 + (7 - 3)^2} \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's perform these calculations using code.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m import math
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Coordinates
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x1, y1 = 11, 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x2, y2 = 2, 3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x3, y3 = 3, 7
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Calculate the distances
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m d1 = math.sqrt((x2 - x1)**2 + (y2 - y1)**2)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m d2 = math.sqrt((x3 - x1)**2 + (y3 - y1)**2)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m d3 = math.sqrt((x3 - x2)**2 + (y3 - y2)**2)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m print((d1, d2, d3))
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```output
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (6.123105625617661, 3.605551275463989, 3.807354106251089)
