[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine how many integer palindromes are between 10,000 and 70,000 and are even, we'll go through the following steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Identify the range of palindromic numbers:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    A palindromic number reads the same backward as forward. For its range:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    10,000 \leq N \leq 70,000
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Separate even and odd palindromic numbers:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - **Odd Palindromes**: An odd palindromic number reads the same backward as forward, so it must have the form \( \overline{\overline{aaaa}} \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - **Even Palindromes**: An even palindromic number has the form \( \overline{abba} \) or \( \overline{abba} \text{ (if } b = a\text{)} \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **List odd palindromic numbers in the given range:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - These numbers range from \(100,001\) to \(99,999\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(100,001, 100,009, \ldots, 99,999\) must all be odd.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Identify valid palindromic numbers in the same range:**
