[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the cost of the sweatshirt, we need to subtract the cost of the t-shirts from the total amount spent. Let's break it down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Total amount spent**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Total amount spent} = \$67.94
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Cost of two t-shirts**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Cost of two t-shirts} = \$15.22 \times 2 = \$30.44
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Cost of the sweatshirt**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Cost of the sweatshirt} = \text{Total amount spent} - \text{Cost of two t-shirts} = \$67.94 - \$30.44 = \$37.50
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the cost of the sweatshirt is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{37.50}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
