[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Alice has a square garden that she wants to plant with flowers. The garden is 6 feet long and 6 feet wide. She plants flowers in the center of the garden, covers a quarter of the garden with soil, and leaves the rest as a flower garden. If each flower needs 1 square foot of space, how many flowers can Alice plant in her garden?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine how many flowers Alice can plant in her garden, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Calculate the area of the garden:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    The garden is a square with each side measuring 6 feet.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Area of the garden} = 6 \, \text{feet} \times 6 \, \text{feet} = 36 \, \text{square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Calculate the area of the flowers:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Alice plants flowers in the center of the garden and covers a quarter of the garden with soil.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Area of the flowers} = \frac{1}{4} \times 36 \, \text{square feet} = 9 \, \text{square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Determine the number of flowers available:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Each flower needs 1 square foot of space.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Number of flowers} = 9 \, \text{flowers}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, Alice can plant \(\boxed{5}\) flowers in her garden.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{5}{7}
