[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ is 8.  Find the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors $2 \mathbf{a} + 3 \mathbf{b}$ and $\mathbf{a} - 5 \mathbf{b}.$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \(2a + 3b\) and \(a - 5b\), we need to use the property that the area of a parallelogram formed by two vectors \(a\) and \(b\) is given by the magnitude of the cross product \(a \times b\). Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Identify the vectors:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{v_1} = 2 \mathbf{a} + 3 \mathbf{b}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{v_2} = \mathbf{a} - 5 \mathbf{b}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Find the cross product \(v_1 \times v_2\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    v_1 \times v_2 = 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    2 & 3 & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    1 & -5 & 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Compute the determinant:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    v_1 \times v_2 = 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{i} \left(3 \cdot 0 - 0 \cdot (-5)\right) - 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{j} \left(2 \cdot 0 - 0 \cdot 1\right) + 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{k} \left(2 \cdot (-5) - 3 \cdot 1\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    v_1 \times v_2 = 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{i} (0) - 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{j} (0) + 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{k} (-10 - 3)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    v_1 \times v_2 = 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{i} (0) - 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{j} (0) + 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \mathbf{k} (-13)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    v_1 \times v_2 = 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -13 \mathbf{k}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Calculate the magnitude of \(v_1 \times v_2\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    The magnitude of a vector \(\mathbf{k}\) is 1 (since it is a scalar multiple of the \(z\)-axis):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \Vert v_1 \times v_2 \Vert = \sqrt{(-13)^2} = \sqrt{169} = 13
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \(2 \mathbf{a} + 3 \mathbf{b}\) and \(\mathbf{a} - 5 \mathbf{b}\) is \(\boxed{13}\).<|endoftext|>
