[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Compute $\tan 75^\circ.$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's find the values of $\sin 75^\circ$ and $\cos 75^\circ$ with the help of the identity $\sin 60^\circ = \dfrac{\sqrt 3}{2}$, $\cos 60^\circ = \dfrac{1}{2}$. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Then, we have $\sin 75^\circ = \sin (60^\circ + 15^\circ) = \sin 60^\circ \cos 15^\circ + \cos 60^\circ \sin 15^\circ = \dfrac{\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2}}{4}$,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Taking the opposite, we have $\cos 75^\circ = \cos (60^\circ + 15^\circ) = \cos 60^\circ \cos 15^\circ - \sin 60^\circ \sin 15^\circ = \dfrac{\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}}{4}$. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we need to compute $\tan 75^\circ = \frac{\sin 75^\circ}{\cos 75^\circ}$. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \tan 75^\circ &= \frac{\frac{\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2}}{4}}{\frac{\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}}{4}} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &= \frac{\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &= \frac{(\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2})(\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2})}{(\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2})(\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2})} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &= \frac{6 + 2\sqrt{12} + 2 + 2}{6 - 2} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &= \frac{8 + 4\sqrt{3}}{4} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &= 2 + \sqrt{3} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, $\boxed{2 + \sqrt 3}$.<|endoftext|>
