[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can use the combination formula: \( C(n, k) \), which represents the number of ways to choose \( k \) elements from a set of \( n \) elements without regard to the spot in the set.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here, \( n = 9 \) and \( k = 2 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ C(9, 2) = \frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \frac{9!}{2! \times 7!} = \frac{9 \times 8 \times 7!}{2 \times 1 \times 7!} = \frac{9 \times 8}{2 \times 1} = 72 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
