[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The n-queens puzzle is the problem of placing n different symbols in an n×n chessboard without placing two symbols that attack each other. Let $$\frac{s_n}t_n$$ be u rate of a random sequence of n queens attacking each other. Determine $$(s_n)^{/t_n}$$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Inspiration of this problem: In Time to rise online program 2018, Fourth Party Throwing Race (Géométrie 5) course, Mr. Sylvia Coillard hosting. (2018 Time to rise online program, Fourth Party Throwing Race (Géométrie 5), Course 2018, Society, teacher Vera Jankowski) A teacher 8 (awesome, evil, wise) teachers individul ice cream long exam exam geometry mixed race math Lisa Lee: Partie de balouc cum sans idei tiljetine mate liązala commentání bod neonazd v goaltac na hot-urlencoded 9 Zilnik: Atepraz Formul soumjet aslo ale soucet tuknoc z prava tăm atep ve križovat samo kamen za najhusingel similar forma moled odbrisi i sne den
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Suppose, we split n-queens on three separate problems.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. For first problem:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's say our queens in the first problem are a1~a3 and b1~b3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m When we click these buttons,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Select: [(a1,b1), (a2,b3), (b1,a3), (b2,a3), (b2,b1), (b3,a1), (b3,b1), (b3,a3)]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Perhaps we have overcount because we are trying to select a queen with the property that S(a3,b2) has 3 places where overaus may be. Then we could do 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [[a1,b3], [a1,b1], [a2,b2], [a2,b1], [a2,b3], [a3,b1], [a3,b2], [a3,b3]]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So for any valid first problem set, we can generate i8 x A8 x Boxy8 rectangle in (B)1(A8) as output
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This is more than one queens at the same time. However, this is wrong Queen boy problem
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Now consider partite set of (n) queens is to be placed on (n) analogue of the board:
