[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The purpose of the consultation process is to gather the views and input of all relevant stakeholders, including decision makers and stakeholders, to ensure that the proposed changes or policies are well-understood and can be implemented successfully. The ultimate goal is to facilitate decision-making that reflects the needs, concerns, and perspectives of different groups within society. Through these processes, it is possible to identify areas of potential conflict, potential obstacles, and any underlying issues that may hinder the implementation or progress of the proposed changes or policies. This process can involve various steps, such as gathering feedback from stakeholders, conducting in-depth analysis, exploring potential alternatives before making a decision, and refining the proposals once appropriate trade-offs have been made.
