[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the measure of the minor arc $AK$, we start by using the relationship between the angle formed by a chord on a circle and the arc it intercepts. Specifically, if the central angle of the minor arc is $42^\circ$, then the central angle of the intercepted major arc is $2 \times 42^\circ = 84^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can use this information to find the measure of the arc $AK$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Arc } AK = 2 \times \text{Central Angle} = 2 \times 42^\circ = 84^\circ.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's confirm this calculation using Python.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Given angle of the major arc (angle between two radii)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m major_arc_angle = 2 * 42  # 84 degrees
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # The measure of the minor arc is half of the central angle of the major arc
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m minor_arc_angle = major_arc_angle / 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m print(minor_arc_angle)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```output
