[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute \((1 + i)^4\), we can use the binomial theorem or simply by plugging in the value. The binomial theorem states that \((a + b)^n = \sum_{k=0}^{n} \binom{n}{k} a^{n-k} b^k\), where $\binom{n}{k}$ is a binomial coefficient given by $\binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In this case, \(a = 1\), \(b = i\), and \(n = 4\). So we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (1 + i)^4 = \sum_{k=0}^{4} \binom{4}{k} (1)^{4-k} (i)^k
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's calculate each term individually:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{For } k = 0:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{4}{0} (1)^{4-0} (i)^0 = 1 \cdot 1 \cdot 1 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{For } k = 1:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{4}{1} (1)^{4-1} (i)^1 = 4 \cdot 1 \cdot i = 4i
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{For } k = 2:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{4}{2} (1)^{4-2} (i)^2 = 6 \cdot 1 \cdot (-1) = -6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{For } k = 3:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{4}{3} (1)^{4-3} (i)^3 = 4 \cdot 1 \cdot (-i) = -4i
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{For } k = 4:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{4}{4} (1)^{4-4} (i)^4 = 1 \cdot 1 \cdot 1 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Adding these up, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (1 + i)^4 = 1 + 4i - 6 - 4i + 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 1 + 1 + (-6 - 4i + 4i) - 4i
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 5 - 4i
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, \((1 + i)^4 = 5 - 4i\).
