[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve the problem \(\begin{pmatrix} 3 & 0 \\ 1 & 2 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} -5 & -7 \\ 4 & -9 \end{pmatrix}\), we need to perform vector addition. The following steps involve vector addition.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Add the corresponding elements column-wise:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \(\begin{pmatrix} 3 & 0 \\ 1 & 2 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} -5 & -7 \\ 4 & -9 \end{pmatrix}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. The first row element:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    3 + (-5) = 3 - 5 = -2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. The second row element:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    0 + 2 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the resulting vector is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
