[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - A parabola has the general form \(y = \frac{B^2 - 4AC}{4A}\). For the equation \(y = \frac{B^2 - 4AC}{4A}\), we have \(A = -50\), \(B = -50\), and \(C = 1\).
