[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m There are eight furlongs in a mile. There are two weeks in a fortnight. The British cavalry traveled 2800 furlongs in a fortnight. How many miles per day did the cavalry average?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the average speed of the British cavalry during their fortnight, we need to calculate the average distance traveled per day.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's figure out the total distance traveled in furlongs:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2800 \, \text{furlongs} \times 2 \text{ (days per week)} = 5600 \, \text{furlongs}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 1: Calculate the total distance traveled per fortnight:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1 \text{ fortnight} = 3 \text{ days}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5600 \, \text{furlongs} \times 3 \text{ days} = 16800 \, \text{furlongs}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 2: Compute the total distance per day:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 16800 \, \text{furlongs} \div 3 \text{ days} = 5600 \, \text{furlongs per day}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the average speed of the British cavalry during their 3-day fortnight was:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{5600}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
