[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the value of \( k \), we need to use the property of intersection of a line and a curve. Specifically, for the lines \( -2x + y = k \) and \( 0.5x + y = 14 \), if they intersect at \( x = -8.4 \), then substituting \( x = -8.4 \) into one line equation will solve for \( y \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here's the step-by-step solution:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
