[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 0.5(-8.4) + y = 14 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Simplify and solve for \( y \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ -4.2 + y = 14 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ y = 14 + 4.2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ y = 18.2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Now, substitute \( x = -8.4 \) into the equation \( -2x + y = k \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ -2(-8.4) + 18.2 = k \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. Calculate the value of \( -2(-8.4) \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ -2(-8.4) = 16.8 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ -16.8 + 18.2 = k \]
