[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. \(\mathbf{a} = k (\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c})\) for some scalar \(k\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, substitute the given magnitudes and magnitudes of \(\mathbf{a}, \mathbf{b}, \mathbf{c}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{a} = 1, \quad \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b} = 3, \quad \mathbf{c} \cdot \mathbf{c} = 6.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using the given equation \(\|\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{c}\| = 1\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
