[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 0 = 1 + \frac{1}{3\sqrt{2}} + 0.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This is only possible if \(k = 0\), but \(k\) is not zero because it must be positive. Therefore, the correct approach is to recognize the magnitudes as inverses of the lengths:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
