[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A taxi ride costs $\$1.50$ plus $\$0.25$ per mile traveled.  How much, in dollars, does a 5-mile taxi ride cost?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To calculate the cost of a 5-mile taxi ride, we need to consider both the fixed cost per mile and the cost per mile.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Fixed cost per mile: \$1.50
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Cost per mile: \$0.25
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the total cost, we add the fixed cost to the variable cost per mile multiplied by the number of miles traveled.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Total cost} = \text{Fixed cost} + (\text{Cost per mile} \times \text{Distance of the ride})
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Total cost} = \$1.50 + (\$0.25 \times 5)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Total cost} = \$1.50 + \$1.25
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Total cost} = \$2.75
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the total cost for the 5-mile taxi ride is \boxed{2.75}.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
