[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \(\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}\), we can use the dot product and the base area formula for a parallelogram.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's calculate the dot product of the two vectors. The dot product is given by the sum of the products of the corresponding entries of the vectors:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{v} = 3 \cdot 1 + 1 \cdot (-3) + (-2) \cdot 4
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 3 - 3 - 8
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = -8
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The magnitude of one of the vectors (either \(\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}\) or \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}\)) can be taken, but it will not change the area of the parallelogram because the parallelogram's area is an invariant property. Therefore, we only need to find the magnitude of the resultant (opposite) vector to the diagonals to get the area.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m However, we don't have the magnitudes of the original vectors. Instead, we can use the fact that the area is half the magnitude of the resultant vector. We can find the magnitude of the resultant vector without needing the vectors' magnitudes directly.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's denote the resultant vector as \(\mathbf{R}\). Using the formula for the magnitude of the resultant of two vectors \(\mathbf{u}\) and \(\mathbf{v}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m R = \sqrt{\mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{v}^2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m where \(\mathbf{u} = \begin{pmatrix} u_1 \\ u_2 \\ u_3 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\ v_2 \\ v_3 \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m For our vectors, \(\mathbf{u} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Calculate the dot product \(\mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{v}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{v} = 3 \cdot 1 + 1 \cdot (-3) + (-2) \cdot 4 = 3 - 3 - 8 = -8
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, substitute into the magnitude formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m R = \sqrt{(-8)^2} = \sqrt{64} = 8
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This means the magnitude of the resultant vector is 8. The area of the parallelogram is twice this magnitude:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area} = 2 \times 8 = 16
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \(\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{16}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
