[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given the information provided, we can calculate the side length of the square base (since the square base gives us its area) and then use it to find the height of the pyramid.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The formula for the area of a square is \( \text{side}^2 \). In this case, the area is given as 288 square cm, so we can set up an equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{side}^2 = 288 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Taking the square root of both sides, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{side} = \sqrt{288} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To confirm the magnitude of the side, we can use Python to perform the calculation and verify the square root.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
