[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m import math
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Given area of the square base
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m area = 288
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Calculate side length of the square base
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m side_length = math.sqrt(area)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Calculate the volume of the pyramid
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Since the peak is 15 cm from each of the other vertices,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # the side of the square base (let's call it s) can be found by dividing the area of the square base by the height of the pyramid
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # area of the square base as a fraction of s
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m fraction = area / (side_length**2 * 2)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m side_half = math.sqrt((fraction / (side_length**2 * 2)))
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # The height of the pyramid (h) can be found using the Pythagorean theorem
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # consider a right triangle formed by the height of the pyramid, the side of the base, and the slant height from the peak to the center of the base
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # calculate the slant height (l) using the Pythagorean theorem:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # l = sqrt((side_half)^2 + 15^2)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # l = sqrt((side_half)^2 + 225)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m l = math.sqrt(side_half**2 + 15**2)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # The volume of the pyramid is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m volume = (side_half * 15)**3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```output
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Done
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The area of the square base is 288 square cm. The height of the pyramid is calculated as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The side length of the square base is \(\sqrt{288} = \sqrt{64 \cdot 4.5} = 8\sqrt{4.5} = 12\sqrt{6} \approx 20.04\) cm.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using the Pythagorean theorem, the height of the pyramid is \(\sqrt{(15)^2 + (12\sqrt{6})^2} = \sqrt{225 + 864} = \sqrt{1089} = 33\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Lastly, the volume of the pyramid is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (\text{side of the base})^3 \cdot \text{height of the pyramid} = 12\sqrt{6}^3 \cdot 33
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 12 \cdot 6\sqrt{6} \cdot 33 = 2652\sqrt{6} \approx 12604.07 \text{ cubic cm}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the volume of the pyramid is approximately \( \boxed{12604.07} \) cubic centimeters.<|endoftext|>
