[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We already know:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 60^\circ = \frac{1}{2} \quad \text{and} \quad \sin 60^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Calculate \(\cos \theta\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x' = (4 + 7\sqrt{3}) \cdot \frac{1}{2} - (7 - 4\sqrt{3}) \cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Calculate \(\sin \theta\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x' = (4 + 7\sqrt{3}) \cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} + (7 - 4\sqrt{3}) \cdot \frac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's simplify these expressions step by step using code.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m import math
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
