[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve for the ordered pair \((a, b)\) such that \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ a \\ -7 \end{pmatrix} \times \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 4 \\ b \end{pmatrix} = \mathbf{0}\), we need to use the cross product formula for 3D vectors. The cross product of vectors \(\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \\ z \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} w \\ p \\ q \end{pmatrix}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} yb - zq \\ zb - \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} \\ xq - y \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given vectors are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
