[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we sum these scores:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 83 + 96 + 81 + 82 + 83 + 95 = 507
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we calculate the total marking period score, which is 90% of the sum of these scores:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 0.90 \times 507 = 456.3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This total score represents 100% of the total grading program, so the sum of the grades for the remaining two tests must be 456.3. Therefore, the sum of the percent scores of the two missing grades is:
