[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A 6-sided die is weighted so that the probability of any number being rolled is proportional to the value of the roll.  (So, for example, the probability of a 2 being rolled is twice that of a 1 being rolled.)  What is the expected value of a roll of this weighted die?  Express your answer as a common fraction.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the expected value of a roll of a weighted die, we first need to determine the probabilities of each possible outcome.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since the die is weighted, the probability of rolling a one (P(1)) would be \( \frac{1}{6} \). Similarly, the probability of rolling a two (P(2)) is also \( \frac{1}{6} \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The expected value (EV) of a single roll is calculated by multiplying each possible outcome by its corresponding probability and summing these products:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ EV = P(\text{1}) \times n(1) + P(\text{2}) \times n(2) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ P(\text{1}) = \frac{1}{6}, \quad P(\text{2}) = \frac{1}{6} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can compute the expected value using these probabilities:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ EV = \left(\frac{1}{6}\right) \times 1 + \left(\frac{1}{6}\right) \times 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's calculate this value using Python to ensure accuracy.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Given probabilities
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m P_1 = 1/6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m P_2 = 1/6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Expected value
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m expected_value = (P_1 * 1) + (P_2 * 2)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m print(expected_value)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```
