[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m AB \times BC \times \sin C = 58
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We need to find $AB^2 + AC^2 + BC^2$. To do this, we can use the fact that the sum of squares of the side lengths of a triangle plus three times the sum of the squares of its medians is twice the sum of the medians' squares plus three times the sum of the squares of the medians:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m AB^2 + AC^2 + BC^2 = 2 \times \frac{1^2 + 1^2 + 1^2}{2}\times m_1^2 + 3 \times \frac{1}{2} \times 1^2 \times m_1^2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
