[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the value of \(f(5)\) for the function \(f(x) = \dfrac{x+1}{3x-4}\), we need to substitute \(x = 5\) into the function. The function can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(x) = \dfrac{x+1}{3x-4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, substitute \(x = 5\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(5) = \dfrac{5+1}{3(5)-4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, simplify the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 5 + 1 = 6 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(5) = \dfrac{6}{3 \cdot 5 - 4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, simplify the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 3 \cdot 5 = 15 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 15 - 4 = 11 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So the expression now is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(5) = \dfrac{6}{11} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the value of \(f(5)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \boxed{\dfrac{6}{11}} \]<|endoftext|>
