[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m For the third condition: \( b(a - 1) + b(2 - b) = 5 \) becomes \( b(a - 1) + b(2 - b) = 5 \). Simplifying, we get \( b(2a - 1 - b) = 5 \). Substituting \( b = 5 \), we get \( 5(2a - 1 - 5) = 5 \) which simplifies to \( 5(2a - 6) = 5 \) which further simplifies to \( 2a - 6 = 1 \) or \( 2a = 7 \) or \( a = \frac{7}{2} \). However, \( a = 0 \) satisfies the first condition and the solved forms, \( b = 5 \) is a valid solution.
