[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute \((\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}) \cdot [(\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a})]\), we need to perform vector calculus operations step-by-step. Let's start with \(\mathbf{a}\), \(\mathbf{b}\), and \(\mathbf{c}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 10 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ \pi \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -2 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, calculate \(\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 10 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ \pi \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 - 5 \\ 10 - \pi \\ 1 - 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -8 \\ 10 - \pi \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, compute \(\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ \pi \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -2 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 + 2 \\ \pi + 2 \\ 0 - 7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ \pi + 2 \\ -7 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Then, compute \((\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a})\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -2 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 10 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 + 3 \\ -2 - 10 \\ 7 - 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -12 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, compute the cross product \((\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a})\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a}) = \begin{vmatrix} \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\ 7 & \pi + 2 & -7 \\ 1 & -12 & 6 \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This determinant can be expanded as:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{i} (\pi + 2 \cdot 6 - (-7) \cdot (-12)) - \mathbf{j} (7 \cdot 6 - (-7) \cdot 1) + \mathbf{k} (7 \cdot (-12) - 1 \cdot \pi + 1 \cdot \pi + 2)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = \mathbf{i} (\pi + 12 - 84) - \mathbf{j} (42 + 7) + \mathbf{k} (-84 + 2)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = \mathbf{i} (-72) - \mathbf{j} (49) + \mathbf{k} (-82)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = \begin{pmatrix} -72 \\ -49 \\ -82 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Finally, compute the dot product \((\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}) \cdot [(\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a})]\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}) \cdot [(\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a})] = \begin{pmatrix} -8 \\ 10 - \pi \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} -72 \\ -49 \\ -82 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = (-8)(-72) + (10 - \pi)(-49) + 1(-82)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
