[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m An ambulance travels at 40 mph and can follow a 20-mile route making no stops to get to the hospital. A helicopter travels at one mile per minute, and the air route is 15 miles to get to the same hospital. However, the helicopter takes three minutes for takeoff and three minutes for landing. How many fewer minutes does it take for the helicopter to complete its trip (takeoff, flight and landing) than for the ambulance to complete its trip?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine the difference in minutes between the ambulance and the helicopter completing their trips, we need to calculate the travel time for each individual.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Ambulance Trip
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Speed of the ambulance: \( 40 \) mph
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Distance of the ambulance's route: \( 20 \) miles
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using the formula \( \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Speed}} \), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Time}_{\text{ambulance}} = \frac{20 \text{ miles}}{40 \text{ mph}} = \frac{20}{40} = \frac{1}{2} \text{ hour}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Converting this to minutes:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Time}_{\text{ambulance}} = \frac{1}{2} \times 60 = 30 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Helicopter Trip
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Speed of the helicopter: \( 1 \) mile per minute
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Distance of the helicopter's route: \( 15 \) miles
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using the same formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Time}_{\text{helicopter}} = \frac{15 \text{ miles}}{1 \text{ mile/min}} = 15 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Difference in Travel Times
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find out how many fewer minutes it takes for the helicopter to complete its trip compared to the ambulance, we subtract the time of the helicopter trip from the time of the ambulance trip:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Difference} = \text{Time}_{\text{helicopter}} - \text{Time}_{\text{ambulance}} = 15 \text{ minutes} - 30 \text{ minutes} = -15 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The result shows that the helicopter takes 15 minutes fewer than the ambulance.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{-15}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
