[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Find the inverse of the matrix
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\ -1 & 7 \end{pmatrix}.\]If the inverse does not exist, then enter the zero matrix.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the inverse of the given 2x2 matrix, we can use the following steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    The formula to find the inverse matrix \( A^{-1} \) for a matrix \( A \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    A^{-1} = \frac{1}{\text{det}(A)} \text{adj}(A)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    where \(\text{det}(A)\) is the determinant of matrix \( A \) and \(\text{adj}(A)\) is the adjugate of the matrix \( A \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Calculate the Determinant:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    The determinant of a 2x2 matrix \( \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{det}(A) = ad - bc
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    For our matrix \( A = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\ -1 & 7 \end{pmatrix} \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{det}(A) = (2)(7) - (3)(-1) = 14 + 3 = 17
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Compute the Adjugate:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    The adjugate of a 2x2 matrix \( \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \) is found by swapping the elements and changing their signs:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{adj}(A) = \begin{pmatrix} d & -b \\ -c & a \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    For our matrix \( A \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{adj}(A) = \begin{pmatrix} 7 & 3 \\ 1 & 2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Form the Inverse Matrix:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Using the formula \( A^{-1} = \frac{1}{\text{det}(A)} \text{adj}(A) \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    A^{-1} = \frac{1}{17} \begin{pmatrix} 7 & 3 \\ 1 & 2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Simplifying this:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    A^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{7}{17} & \frac{3}{17} \\ \frac{1}{17} & \frac{2}{17} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. **Final Answer:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    The inverse of the matrix \( \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\ -1 & 7 \end{pmatrix} \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} \frac{7}{17} & \frac{3}{17} \\ \frac{1}{17} & \frac{2}{17} \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 7/17 & -3/17 \\ 1/17 & 2/17 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Extracted Answer]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix}\frac{7}{17}&\frac{3}{17}\\\frac{1}{17}&\frac{2}{17}\end{pmatrix}
