[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3x - 11 = \begin{pmatrix} r \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ k \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This gives us two separate equations to determine \(r\) and \(k\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. From the \(x\)-term:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3 = r + 4t.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. From the \(y\)-term:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -11 = 1 + kt.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can solve these equations step-by-step.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, solve for \(r\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3 = r + 4t.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m r = 3 - 4t.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, solve for \(k\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -11 = 1 + kt.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m kt = -11 - 1.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m kt = -12.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m k = \frac{-12}{t}.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(t\) can be any real number, we need the simplest form where \(t\) is a non-zero value. Given that there is no restriction on \(t\) other than it being non-zero, the simplest solution would be \(t = 1\). Substituting \(t = 1\) into the equation for \(k\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m k = \frac{-12}{1} = -12.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the ordered pair \((r, k)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (r, k) = \left(3 - 4t, -12\right).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substituting \(t = 1\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m r = 3 - 4 \cdot 1 = 1,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m k = -12.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the ordered pair \((r, k)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{(1, -12)}.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
