[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find \(\tan 22.5^\circ\), we can use the half-angle tangent formula for an angle \(k \pi\). The half-angle formula for tangent is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \tan \frac{k\pi}{2} = \frac{\sin \frac{k\pi}{2}}{\cos \frac{k\pi}{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m For \(k = 22.5\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \tan 22.5^\circ = \tan \left(2 \pi - 15^\circ\right) = \cot 15^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We will use the definition of cosine and sine for \(k = 15^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos 15^\circ = \sin 75^\circ, \quad \sin 15^\circ = \cos 75^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using the tangent half-angle formula, we replace \(\frac{k\pi}{2}\) with \(15^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \tan 22.5^\circ = \frac{\sin 15^\circ}{\cos 15^\circ} = \frac{\cos 75^\circ}{\sin 75^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We already know that \(\cos 75^\circ = \sin 15^\circ\) and \(\sin 75^\circ = \cos 15^\circ\). Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \tan 22.5^\circ = \frac{\sin 15^\circ}{\cos 15^\circ} = \frac{\sin 15^\circ}{\sin 75^\circ} = \frac{\sin 15^\circ}{\cos 15^\circ} = \frac{\sin 75^\circ}{\cos 75^\circ} = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(\cos 15^\circ = \sin 75^\circ\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \tan 22.5^\circ = \frac{\sin 22.5^\circ}{1} = 2\sin 11.25^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the value of \(\tan 22.5^\circ\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
