[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplify \(12 \div 5 + 3 \times 4 - 7\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve the expression \(12 \div 5 + 3 \times 4 - 7\), we need to follow the order of operations, often remembered by the acronym PEMDASH (Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), Addition and Subtraction (from left to right)).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 1: Identify and perform the division first. We need to divide 12 by 5.
