[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     - Radius of each small circle: \( r = \frac{0.2}{2} = 0.1 \) feet.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Calculate the area of the larger circle**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     - Area of the larger circle: \( A_{\text{large}} = \pi \times R^2 = \pi \times 3^2 = 9\pi \) square feet.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Calculate the area of each smaller circle**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     - Area of one smaller circle: \( A_{\text{small}} = \pi \times r^2 = \pi \times 0.1^2 = \pi \times 0.01 = 0.01\pi \) square feet.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Calculate the total area of the three smaller circles**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     - Total area of the three smaller circles: \( 3 \times A_{\text{small}} = 3 \times 0.01\pi = 0.03\pi \) square feet.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. **Calculate the fraction of the area of the larger circle occupied by the smaller circles**:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     - Fraction occupied: \( \frac{\text{Total area of the smaller circles}}{\text{Area of the larger circle}} = \frac{0.03\pi}{9\pi} = \frac{0.03}{9} = \frac{3}{900} = \frac{1}{300} \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
