[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Six construction workers that work at the same rate can build a house in 1.5 days.  How long does it take 15 construction workers, working at the same rate, to finish building a house?  Express your answer as a fraction in lowest terms.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine how long it takes 15 construction workers to build a house, we need to first find out the rate at which the workers build houses and then use that rate to figure out the time required for 15 workers to build the same house.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Determine the rate of one construction worker:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Six workers can build one house in 1.5 days.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Therefore, one worker can build one house in \(\frac{1 \text{ day}}{6}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Calculate the rate for 15 workers:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - With six workers, the group can build \(6 \times 1 \text{ day} = 6 \text{ days}\) to build one house.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - With 15 workers, the group can build \(15 \times 6 \text{ days} = 90 \text{ days}\) to build one house.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Express the time required for 15 workers to build a house as a fraction:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - We know that 6 days is the time for 6 workers.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Therefore, half of that time is the time for 15 workers, because \(6\) is half of \(90\) (since \(6 \times 90 = 540\)).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Hence, one half of 90 days is \(\frac{90}{2} = 45 \text{ days}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Consider the problem constraints:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The problem states "if possible in \(\mathrm{fraction}\)".
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Since \(45 \text{ days}\) fits within the given \(fraction\) form, we can use 45 as our final answer.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the time it takes for 15 construction workers to build a house is \(\boxed{45 \text{ days}}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Ground Truth]
