[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the intersection point of the two lines, we need to set their coordinates equal to each other because they both pass through a common origin:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{cases} 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = 2 - t \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m y = 3 + 5t 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{cases} 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = 0 - u \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m y = 7 + 4u 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can set the equations equal to each other:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2 - t = 0 - u
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2 - t = -u \quad \text{(Equation 1)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we equate the coordinates of both lines:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3 + 5t = 7 + 4u
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5t - 4u = 4 \quad \text{(Equation 2)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We now have a pair of linear equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{cases} 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2 - t = -u \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5t - 4u = 4 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To eliminate \(u\), we can solve Equation 1 for \(u\) in terms of \(t\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
