[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine the area of the stairway structure, we need to calculate the area of the four risers and three treads. The stairway's design is a combination of a stepped section, two triangular sections, and two regular trapezoid-shaped sections.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 1: Calculate the area of the risers
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m There are three risers, each 8 inches high. We need to calculate the area of one riser and then multiply by three.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area of one riser} = \text{height of one riser} \times \text{length of one riser} = 8 \times 8 = 64 \text{ square inches}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area of three risers} = 3 \times 64 = 192 \text{ square inches}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 2: Calculate the area of the tread
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The tread is 10 inches deep and twice as wide as the riser.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Width of one tread} = 10 / 2 = 5 \text{ inches}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area of one tread} = \text{width of one tread} \times \text{deeper == two times broadness of one riser} = 5 \times 10 = 50 \text{ square inches}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 3: Calculate the total area of the risers and the tread
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Total area} = \text{Area of three risers} + \text{Area of one tread} = 192 + 50 = 242 \text{ square inches}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 4: Calculate the area of the treads
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m There are three treads, each 10 inches deep and 30 inches long. We need to calculate the area of one tread and then multiply by three.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Width of one tread} = 10 / 2 = 5 \text{ inches}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area of one tread} = \text{length of tread} \times \text{width of one tread} = 30 \times 5 = 150 \text{ square inches}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area of three treads} = 3 \times 150 = 450 \text{ square inches}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 5: Calculate the area of the remaining section
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The staircase has a stub that is 3 inches tall and 8 inches wide. We need to calculate the area of this stub.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
