[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m If $f(x)=g(g(x))-g(x)$ and $g(x)=2x-1$, find $f(3)$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find \( f(3) \), we need to start with the given functions:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(x) = g(g(x)) - g(x) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ g(x) = 2x - 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we need to find \( g(g(3)) \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Calculate \( g(3) \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ g(3) = 2(3) - 1 = 6 - 1 = 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Now, evaluate \( g(g(3)) = g(5) \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ g(5) = 2(5) - 1 = 10 - 1 = 9 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Finally, we need to find \( f(3) \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(3) = g(g(3)) - g(3) = 9 - 5 = 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \boxed{4} \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
