[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we need to identify which numbers are prime and which are not.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A prime number is a natural number greater than 1 that has no positive divisors other than 1 and itself.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's check each prime number individually:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. \( p_1 = 21 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Divisors: 1, 3, 7, 21.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Only divisors: 1, 3, 7.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Hence, 21 is not a prime number.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. \( p_2 = 23 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Divisors: 1, 23.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Only divisor: 23.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Hence, 23 is a prime number.
