[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the ratio \(\frac{x}{y}\) given the equation \(\frac{10x-3y}{13x-2y} = \frac{3}{5}\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Cross-multiply to eliminate the fractions:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    5 \left(10x - 3y\right) = 3 \left(13x - 2y\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Expand both sides:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    5 \cdot 10x - 5 \cdot 3y = 3 \cdot 13x - 3 \cdot 2y
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    50x - 15y = 39x - 6y
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Isolate the terms involving \(x\) and \(y\) on one side of the equation:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    50x - 39x = -15y + 6y
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    11x = -9y
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Solve for \(\frac{x}{y}\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \frac{x}{y} = \frac{-9y}{11y}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. **Simplify the fraction:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \frac{x}{y} = \frac{-9}{11}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the ratio \(\frac{x}{y}\) is \(\boxed{-\frac{9}{11}}\).<|endoftext|>
