[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the 205th term in a geometric sequence, we can use the formula for the nth term of a geometric sequence:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ a_n = a \cdot r^{n-1} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m where:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \( a_n \) is the nth term,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \( a \) is the first term,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \( r \) is the common ratio,
