[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To simplify the trigonometric expression \(\cos 54^\circ \cos 4^\circ - \cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ\), we will use a trigonometric identity known as the product-to-sum formula. The identity we will use is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos(A + B) = \cos A \cos B - \sin A \sin B
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step-by-Step Simplification:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Identify the pairs for the sum of angles:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \cos 54^\circ \cos 4^\circ + \cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Here, \(A = 54^\circ\) and \(B = 4^\circ\), and \(C = 36^\circ\) and \(D = 86^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Apply the product-to-sum formula \(\cos(A + B) = \cos A \cos B - \sin A \sin B\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \cos 54^\circ \cos 4^\circ - \cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ = \left(\cos 54^\circ \cos 4^\circ - \cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Substitute the assumed angles for \(A\), \(B\), and \(C\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \left(\cos 54^\circ \cos 4^\circ - \cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Simplify the expression:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Notice that the expression inside the parentheses can be paired as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \left(\cos 54^\circ \cos 4^\circ\right) - \left(\cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Using the double-angle identity for cosine \(\cos 2A = 2\cos^2 A - 1\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
