[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let $\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 10 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix},$ $\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ \pi \\ 0 \end{pmatrix},$ and $\mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -2 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}.$  Compute
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[(\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}) \cdot [(\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a})].\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This is a vector calculus problem that translates into polar coordinates. We start by finding the vectors expressions, then we will operate the cross product, dot product, and then cross product.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Compute $\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 10 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ \pi \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 - 5 \\ 10 - \pi \\ 1 - 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -8 \\ 10 - \pi \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Compute $\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ \pi \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -2 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 - (-2) \\ \pi - (-2) \\ 0 - 7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ \pi + 2 \\ -7 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Compute $\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a}$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -2 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 10 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 - (-3) \\ -2 - 10 \\ 7 - 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -12 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. Use the vector triple product identity:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a}) = (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{b}) = (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{b}) = (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{b})
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. Express \(\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a}\) and \(\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{b}\) in terms of \(\mathbf{a}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -12 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{c} - \mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ \pi + 2 \\ -7 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6. Cross products of the vectors in Check One:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{b}) = \begin{vmatrix} \mathbf{k} & \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} \\ 1 & -12 & 6 \\ 7 & \pi + 2 & -7 \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since this is a determinant of a 3x3 matrix, it can be further evaluated as:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{b}) = \begin{vmatrix} 1 & -12 & 6 \\ 7 & \pi + 2 & -7 \\ 1 & -12 & 6 \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 7. Expand the determinant:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{vmatrix} 1 & -12 & 6 \\ 7 & \pi + 2 & -7 \\ 1 & -12 & 6 \end{vmatrix} = 1 \begin{vmatrix} \pi + 2 & -7 \\ -12 & 6 \end{vmatrix} - (-12) \begin{vmatrix} 7 & -7 \\ 1 & 6 \end{vmatrix} + 6 \begin{vmatrix} 7 & \pi + 2 \\ 1 & -12 \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 1((\pi + 2) \cdot 6 - (-7) \cdot (-12)) + 12(7 \cdot 6 - 7 \cdot 1) + 6(7 \cdot (-12) - 1 \cdot (\pi + 2))
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 1(6\pi + 12 - 84) + 12(42 - 7) + 6(-84 + \pi + 2)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 1(6\pi - 72) + 12(35) + 6(-82 + \pi)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 6\pi - 72 + 420 - 404 + 6\pi
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 12\pi + 2\pi - 42
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 14\pi - 42
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 8. Cross product with \((\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b})\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}) = \begin{pmatrix} -8 \\ 10 - \pi \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}) \times (\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}) = \begin{vmatrix} \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\ -8 & 10 - \pi & 1 \\ 113 & 1 - \pi & -1 \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Expanding this determinant, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = \mathbf{i}((10 - \pi) \cdot (-1) - 1 \cdot 1) - \mathbf{j}((-8) \cdot (-1) - 1 \cdot 113) + \mathbf{k}((-8) \cdot (1 - \pi) - 1 \cdot (113))
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 1(-10 + \pi) - (-8 - 113)(1) + \mathbf{k}(-8 + \pi - 113)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = -10 + \pi + 111 - 113 + 8\pi
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 10\pi + 11
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 9. Compute the final result with the main vectors:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}) \cdot [(\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{c}) \times (\mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a})]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = (14\pi - 42)(10\pi + 11)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 10. We can now expand this product:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 14\pi(10\pi + 11) - 42(10\pi + 11)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 140\pi^2 + 154\pi - 420\pi - 462
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 140\pi^2 - 266\pi - 462
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 11. The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{140\pi^2 - 266\pi - 462}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
