[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Convert the point $(\sqrt{2},-\sqrt{2})$ in rectangular coordinates to polar coordinates.  Enter your answer in the form $(r,\theta),$ where $r > 0$ and $0 \le \theta < 2 \pi.$
