[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the projection of the vector \(\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}\) onto the vector \(\mathbf{u} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}\), we use the formula for the projection of \(\mathbf{v}\) onto \(\mathbf{u}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{u}} \mathbf{v} = \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{u}}{\mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{u}} \mathbf{u}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we calculate the dot product \(\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{u}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{u} = 3 \cdot 2 + 0 \cdot (-3) = 6 + 0 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we calculate the dot product \(\mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{u}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{u} = 2 \cdot 2 + (-3) \cdot (-3) = 4 + 9 = 13
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we substitute these dot products into the projection formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{u}} \mathbf{v} = \frac{6}{13} \mathbf{u} = \frac{6}{13} \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We then multiply each component of \(\mathbf{u}\) by \(\frac{6}{13}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{proj}_{\mathbf{u}} \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{6}{13} \cdot 2 \\ \frac{6}{13} \cdot (-3) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{12}{13} \\ -\frac{18}{13} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the projection of the vector \(\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}\) onto the vector \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} \frac{12}{13} \\ -\frac{18}{13} \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
