[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Find the units digit of the following within the indicated number base: $52_7 + 62_7$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Sure, let's find the units digit of the given addition in base 7. We will start by adding the digits from right to left, carrying over where necessary.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here's how it looks in base 7:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 52_7 &= 5 \cdot 7 + 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 62_7 &= 6 \cdot 7 + 2 \quad (\text{carry over from above}) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &= 42_7
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now we add these base 7 numbers directly:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5 \cdot 7 + 6 &+ 4 \cdot 7 + 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &= 5 \cdot 7 + 2 \cdot 7 + 6 + 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &= 5 \cdot 7 + 4 \cdot 7 + 6 + 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &= 6 \cdot 7 + 2 + 6 + 2  
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So after adding $5 \cdot 7 + 2$ and $6 \cdot 7 + 2$, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6 \cdot 7 + 2 + 6 &\equiv 6 \cdot 7 + 2 + 6 \equiv 2 + 6 + 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &\equiv 8 + 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m &\equiv 0 \quad (\text{since } 8 < 6) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the number $52_7 + 62_7$ in base 7 is $82$, and the units digit is \(\boxed{2}\).<|endoftext|>
