[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{C} = \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ -1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -4 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m which means:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{B} = \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ -1 \\ g \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -4 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -4 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Determine the ratio \( t \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{B} = 8 + t \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -4 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, solve for \( t \) in terms of the ratio \( \frac{1}{u} \), which we found to be \( 2 \sqrt{2} - 2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -4 \\ g \end{pmatrix} = 8 + (2\sqrt{2} - 2) \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -4 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 4 + (2 - 2\sqrt{2}) \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -4 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = y \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substitute \( y \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 4 + (2 - 2\sqrt{2}) \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -4 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 4 + (2 - 2\sqrt{2}) \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = g \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ g = 4 + (4 - 4\sqrt{2}) \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ g = 2 (2 - 4\sqrt{2}) \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m **3. Find the point on the vector \( \bold{v} \)**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ c(t) = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ t \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's find the position of \( c(t) \) on the vector \( \bold{w} \) at this point:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ p(t) = c(t) - w \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ t \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ -1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \]
