[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (a) $r$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m As we know, the angle $\phi$ in polar coordinates can be calculated using the cotangent function.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 	- The $X$ coordinate is $-2$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 	- The $Y$ coordinate is $-2$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 	- The value of $|X|$ is $2$ (i.e., points are right next to the axes).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 	- The value of $|Y|$ is $1$ (i.e., points lie on the $x$-axis).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 	- Hence, $\phi = arctan(Y/X) = arctan(2/-2) = arctan(-1) = -\frac{\pi}{4}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the polar coordinate of the point $(-2,-2)$ belonging to the $xy$-plane $\mathbb{R}^2$ is $\left(-\frac{\pi}{4}, -\frac{\pi}{4}\right)$. Thus, $(" -2, -2)"$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (b) $\theta$ (counterclockwise from the positive $x$-axis)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $\theta$ is the angle in the polar coordinate system measured counterclockwise from the positive $x$-axis.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Considering the negative coordinates, it is assigned with the value of $(-\frac{\pi}{4})$. Thus, $\theta$ (counterclockwise from the positive $x$-axis) is $-\frac{\pi}{4}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (c) $r$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $r$ is the distance from the origin ($0,0$) to the point $(x,y)$ in the $xy$-plane.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using the Pythagorean theorem, we find the distance:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ r = \sqrt{x^2 + y^2} = \sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-2)^2} = \sqrt{4 + 4} = \sqrt{8} = 2\sqrt{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, $r$ is $2\sqrt{2}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
