[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the units digit of the sum \(3^1 + 3^3 + 3^5 + 3^7 + \ldots + 3^{2009}\), we need to recognize the pattern in the series. Each term in the series is a power of 3. Specifically, the powers of 3 cycle every four terms:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3^1 = 3 \quad \text{(units digit is 3)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3^2 = 9 \quad \text{(units digit is 9)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3^3 = 27 \quad \text{(units digit is 7)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3^4 = 81 \quad \text{(units digit is 1)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3^5 = 243 \quad \text{(units digit is 3)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3^6 = 729 \quad \text{(units digit is 9)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3^7 = 2187 \quad \text{(units digit is 7)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m and so on.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The sequence repeats every four terms: \(3, 9, 7, 1\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we need to determine the units digit of the sum of four terms:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (3 + 9 + 7 + 1) \mod 10^k
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m For \(k = 4\), we first find the units digits of each term in the sequence:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3, 9, 7, 1 \rightarrow \text{units digits 3, 9, 7, 1}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we sum these units digits:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3 + 9 + 7 + 1 = 20 \rightarrow \text{units digit of 20 is 0}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since the sum of four terms (each being 20), the result is 0. Therefore, the units digit of the sum \(3^1 + 3^3 + 3^5 + 3^7 + \ldots + 3^{2009}\) is \(\boxed{0}\).<|endoftext|>
