[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find out how long it takes for 15 construction workers to build the house, we first need to determine the time it takes for just one worker to build the house. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Determine the work rate of one worker:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Six workers can build a house in 1.5 days.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Therefore, the total amount of work done by six workers in one day is 1/1.5 = 2/3 houses.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Determine the work rate of one worker:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The total work rate of six workers is \(\frac{2}{3}\) houses per day.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - If we want to find the work rate per day for one worker, we divide the total work rate by the number of workers:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \text{Work rate of one worker} = \frac{\frac{2}{3}}{6} = \frac{2}{3} \times \frac{1}{6} = \frac{2}{18} = \frac{1}{9} \text{ houses per day}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Determine the number of days it takes for 15 workers to build the house:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - If one worker can build \(\frac{1}{9}\) of the house per day, then 15 workers can build:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \text{Daily work of 15 workers} = 15 \times \frac{1}{9} = \frac{15}{9} = \frac{5}{3} \text{ houses per day}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Determine the time it takes to build one house:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(\frac{5}{3}\) houses take \(\frac{3}{5}\) days to complete.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Therefore, the time to build one house is \(\frac{3}{5}\) days.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. **Convert the fraction to its simplest form:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The fraction \(\frac{3}{5}\) is already in its simplest form.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m **Conclusion:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m It takes \(\boxed{\frac{3}{5}}\) days for 15 construction workers to build one house.<|endoftext|>
