[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, solve the first equation for \(u\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[u = 2 + t\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, substitute \(u = 2 + t\) into the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[7 + 4(2 + t) = 3 + 5t\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[7 + 8 + 4t = 3 + 5t\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[15 + 4t = 3 + 5t\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[15 - 3 = 5t - 4t\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[12 = t\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now substitute \(t = 12\) back into \(u = 2 + t\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[u = 2 + 12 = 14\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the point of intersection is \((x, y) = (u, w) = (14, 3 + 10) = (14, 13)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the point where the lines intersect is \(\boxed{(14, 13)}\).<|endoftext|>
