[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve the problem, we need to determine the area of \(\triangle CDE\) given that \(\triangle ABC\) has an area of 6 square centimeters and \(\overline{AB} \parallel \overline{DE}\). We also know that \(BD = 4BC\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's denote the length of \(BC\) as \(x\). Therefore, \(BD = 4x\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(AB \parallel DE\), \(\triangle ABC\) and \(\triangle CDE\) are similar by the AA (Angle-Angle) similarity criterion. This means that the ratios of the corresponding sides are equal.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The ratio of the sides of \(\triangle ABC\) to \(\triangle CDE\) is the same as the ratio of \(AB\) to \(DE\). Let's denote the length of \(DE\) as \(y\). Then, the ratio of the sides is:
