[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Find the $3 \times 3$ matrix $\mathbf{M}$ such that for a $3 \times 3$ matrix $\mathbf{N},$ $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{N}$ is the result of swapping the first row and second row of $\mathbf{N},$ and doubling the third row of $\mathbf{N}.$  In other words,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\ d & e & f \\ g & h & i \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} d & e & f \\ a & b & c \\ 2g & 2h & 2i \end{pmatrix}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the \(3 \times 3\) matrix \(\mathbf{M}\) such that \(\mathbf{M} \mathbf{N} = \begin{pmatrix} d & e & f \\ a & b & c \\ 2g & 2h & 2i \end{pmatrix}\) for any \(3 \times 3\) matrix \(\mathbf{N}\), let's denote \(\mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} m_{11} & m_{12} & m_{13} \\ m_{21} & m_{22} & m_{23} \\ m_{31} & m_{32} & m_{33} \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{M} \mathbf{N} = \begin{pmatrix} d & e & f \\ a & b & c \\ 2g & 2h & 2i \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m we start by expressing this in matrix form:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} m_{11} & m_{12} & m_{13} \\ m_{21} & m_{22} & m_{23} \\ m_{31} & m_{32} & m_{33} \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\ d & e & f \\ g & h & i \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a m_{11} + d m_{21} + g m_{31} & a m_{12} + d m_{22} + g m_{32} & a m_{13} + d m_{23} + g m_{33} \\ m_{11} + e m_{21} + h m_{31} & m_{12} + e m_{22} + h m_{32} & m_{13} + e m_{23} + h m_{33} \\ a m_{11} + 2g m_{21} + i g m_{31} & a m_{12} + 2g m_{22} + i g m_{32} & a m_{13} + 2g m_{23} + i g m_{33} \\ m_{11} + 2h m_{21} + 2i m_{31} & m_{12} + 2h m_{22} + 2i m_{32} & m_{13} + 2h m_{23} + 2i m_{33} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} d & e & f \\ a & b & c \\ 2g & 2h & 2i \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This gives us a system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{11} + d m_{21} + g m_{31} = a m_{11} + d m_{21} + g m_{31} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{12} + e m_{22} + h m_{32} = a m_{12} + e m_{22} + h m_{32} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m a m_{13} + d m_{23} + g m_{33} = a m_{13} + d m_{23} + g m_{33} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{11} + e m_{21} + h m_{31} = a m_{11} + e m_{21} + h m_{31} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{12} + e m_{22} + h m_{32} = a m_{12} + e m_{22} + h m_{32} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m a m_{13} + d m_{23} + g m_{33} = a m_{13} + d m_{23} + g m_{33} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{11} + 2g m_{21} + i g m_{31} = a m_{11} + 2g m_{21} + i g m_{31} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{12} + 2g m_{22} + i g m_{32} = a m_{12} + 2g m_{22} + i g m_{32} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{13} + 2g m_{23} + i g m_{33} = a m_{13} + 2g m_{23} + i g m_{33} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{11} + 2h m_{21} + 2i m_{31} = a m_{11} + 2h m_{21} + 2i m_{31} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{12} + 2h m_{22} + 2i m_{32} = a m_{12} + 2h m_{22} + 2i m_{32} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{13} + 2h m_{23} + 2i m_{33} = a m_{13} + 2h m_{23} + 2i m_{33}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplifying the above system:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. The first row's right-hand side terms are equal:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    m_{11} + d m_{21} + g m_{31} = a m_{11} + d m_{21} + g m_{31}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    This is always true.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. The second row's right-hand side terms are equal:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    m_{12} + e m_{22} + h m_{32} = a m_{12} + e m_{22} + h m_{32}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    This is also always true.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. The third row's right-hand side terms are equal:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    a m_{13} + d m_{23} + g m_{33} = a m_{13} + d m_{23} + g m_{33}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    This is always true.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. The fourth row's right-hand side terms are equal:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    m_{11} + e m_{21} + h m_{31} = a m_{11} + e m_{21} + h m_{31}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    d m_{21} + g m_{31} = a m_{21} + g m_{31}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    d m_{21} = a m_{21}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    This implies:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    d = a \quad \text{(since \(m_{21}\) is unspecified)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. The fifth row's right-hand side terms are equal:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    m_{12} + e m_{22} + h m_{32} = a m_{12} + e m_{22} + h m_{32}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    e m_{22} + g m_{32} = a e m_{22} + h m_{32}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    e m_{22} = a + h g m_{32}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    If \(g \neq 0\), we can divide both sides by \(g\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \frac{e}{g} m_{22} = a + h m_{32} \quad \text{(1)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6. The sixth row's right-hand side terms are equal:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    a m_{13} + d m_{23} + g m_{33} = a m_{13} + d m_{23} + g m_{33}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    This is always true.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 7. The seventh row's right-hand side terms are equal:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    m_{11} + 2g m_{21} + i g m_{31} = a m_{11} + 2g m_{21} + i g m_{31}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    i g m_{31} = a g m_{31}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    0 = 0 \quad \text{(since \(m_{31}\) is unspecified)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 8. The eighth row's right-hand side terms are equal:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    m_{12} + 2g m_{22} + i g m_{32} = a m_{12} + 2g m_{22} + i g m_{32}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    This is always true.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 9. The ninth row's right-hand side terms are equal:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    m_{13} + 2g m_{23} + i g m_{33} = a m_{13} + 2g m_{23} + i g m_{33}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    i g m_{33} = a g m_{33}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    0 = 0 \quad \text{(since \(m_{33}\) is unspecified)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the \(3 \times 3\) matrix \(\mathbf{M}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 1 & x & y \\ z & 1 & x \\ 2z & 2x & x \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
