[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve for \(\angle PRQ\), we need to use the properties of parallel lines and triangles. Given that \(TS \parallel RQ\), we know that corresponding angles are equal. In the triangle \(PQR\), the angle \(\angle RPQ = 65^\circ\). Since \(TS \parallel RQ\), the corresponding angle \(\angle RTQ = \angle RPQ = 65^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, consider the triangle \(TSQ\). The sum of the angles in any triangle is \(180^\circ\). Therefore, we can write the equation for the angles in triangle \(TSQ\) as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \angle SNP + \angle TSQ + \angle RTS = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(\angle TSQ = 145^\circ\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \angle SNP + 145^\circ + \angle RTS = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We also know that \(\angle RST = 180^\circ - 65^\circ = 115^\circ\). Therefore, \(\angle RTS = \angle RST - \angle NSR = 115^\circ - \angle SNP\). Since \(\angle NRQ = 180^\circ - 115^\circ = 65^\circ\), \(\angle NSR = 65^\circ\) because \(TS \parallel RQ\), making \(\triangle NSR \cong \triangle NRP\) (by the congruence of corresponding angles and the parallel lines).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, \(\angle NSR = \angle SNP = 65^\circ\). Therefore, \(\angle RTS = 180^\circ - 145^\circ = 35^\circ\), and \(\angle SNP = 180^\circ - \angle RTS = 180^\circ - 35^\circ = 145^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \angle SNP + \angle PRQ + \angle PRQ = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(\angle NRQ = 65^\circ\), we can find \(\angle PRQ\) by using the fact that the sum of angles in a triangle is \(180^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \angle PRQ = 180^\circ - \angle NSR = 180^\circ - 65^\circ = 115^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m However, we can directly solve for \(\angle PRQ\) using the fact that \(\angle NSR = \angle SNP\) and the properties of parallel lines and triangles. Since \(\angle NRQ = 65^\circ\) and \(\angle NSR = 180^\circ - 145^\circ = 35^\circ\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \angle SAN + \angle NQS + \angle NRP = 180^\circ \implies \angle SAN + \angle NQS + \angle PRQ = 180^\circ \implies \angle PRQ = 180^\circ - \angle SAN - \angle NQS = 115^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the measure of \(\angle PRQ\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{115}
