[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    So, the repeating part can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    0.72\frac{6}{9} = 0.72\overline{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Express \(0.72\overline{2}\) as a fraction:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    To convert the repeating decimal \(0.72\overline{2}\) to a fraction, let \(x\) be the repeating decimal:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    x = 0.72\overline{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Multiply both sides by 100 to shift the decimal point two places to the right:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
