[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Now, subtract the original \(x\) from this equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    100x - x = 72.2\overline{2} - 0.72\overline{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Simplify the left and right sides:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    99x = 72
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Solve for \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    x = \frac{72}{99}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Simplify the fraction \(\frac{72}{99}\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 72 and 99. The GCD of 72 and 99 is 9. Divide both the numerator and the denominator by their GCD:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
