[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1, \tan \frac{2\pi}{5}, \tan \frac{4\pi}{5}, \tan \frac{8\pi}{5}, \tan \frac{16\pi}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Dividing each of these roots by $\tan \frac{\pi}{5}$, we get the first five roots of the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{\tan \frac{\pi}{5} + i}{\tan \frac{\pi}{5}} = 1 + i, \quad \frac{\tan \frac{\pi}{5} - i}{\tan \frac{\pi}{5}} = \frac{-i}{\sqrt{2}}, \quad \frac{\tan \frac{\pi}{5} - i}{\tan \frac{2\pi}{5}} = \tan \frac{\pi}{10} - i, \quad \frac{\tan \frac{\pi}{5} + i}{\tan \frac{4\pi}{5}} = \tan \frac{4\pi}{5} - i, \quad \frac{\tan \frac{\pi}{5} + i}{\tan \frac{8\pi}{5}} = \tan \frac{4\pi}{5} + i
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since the denominators are the fifth roots of unity, the values of the imaginary part must be simply multiplied by the same factor to get the real part.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{\tan \frac{\pi}{5} + i}{\tan \frac{\pi}{5} - i} = \cos \frac{2n \pi}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This means:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1 + i = e^{\frac{2\pi i}{10}} \quad \text{or} \quad 1 + i = e^{i \pi (2n \mod 10)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplifying, we can find the corresponding values of $n$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1 + i = e^{\frac{i \pi}{10}} = \cos \frac{\pi}{10} + i \sin \frac{\pi}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1 = \cos \frac{\pi}{10} + i \sin \frac{\pi}{10} \quad \text{or} \quad 1 = \cos \frac{i \pi}{10} + i \sin \frac{i \pi}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m And the values of $n$ that satisfy this are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos \frac{n \pi}{10} = \frac{\pi}{10} \quad \text{or} \quad \cos \frac{i n \pi}{10} = \frac{\pi}{10} \quad \text{or} \quad \cos \frac{2n \pi}{10} = \frac{\pi}{10} \quad \text{or} \quad \cos i \frac{2n \pi}{10} = \frac{\pi}{10} \quad \text{or} \quad \cos 2n \pi/10 = \frac{\pi}{10} \quad \text{or} \quad \cos (2n + 1) \frac{2\pi}{10} = \frac{\pi}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The only values of $n$ that satisfy this are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m n = 5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So the answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{5}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
