[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Sure, I can help you with that! To compute $\binom{11}{9}$, we can use the formula for combinations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{n}{r} = \frac{n!}{r!(n-r)!}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In this case, $n = 11$ and $r = 9$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Plugging in the values, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{11}{9} = \frac{11!}{9!(11-9)!} = \frac{11!}{9!(11-9)!}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplifying this expression, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{11}{9} = \frac{11!}{9!2!} = \frac{11 \times 10}{2 \times 1} = \frac{110}{2} = 55
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the value of $\binom{11}{9}$ is 55.<|endoftext|>
