[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute the determinant of the 2x2 matrix \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{vmatrix} -5 & 3 \\ 4 & -4 \end{vmatrix},
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \] we use the formula for the determinant of a 2x2 matrix. The determinant of a matrix \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{vmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{vmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m is given by \(ad - bc\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here, \(a = -5\), \(b = 3\), \(c = 4\), and \(d = -4\). Substituting these values into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{vmatrix} -5 & 3 \\ 4 & -4 \end{vmatrix} = (-5)(-4) - (3)(4).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Calculating each term separately:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (-5)(-4) = 20,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (3)(4) = 12.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the determinant is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 20 - 12 = 8.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the determinant of the matrix is \boxed{8}.<|endoftext|>
