[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A cube has eight vertices (corners) and twelve edges. A segment, such as $x$, which joins two vertices not joined by an edge is called a diagonal. Segment $y$ is also a diagonal. How many diagonals does a cube have? [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m /* AMC8 1998 #17 Problem */
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m pair A=(0,48), B=(0,0), C=(48,0), D=(48,48);
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m pair E=(24,72), F=(24,24), G=(72,24), H=(72,72);
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m pen d = linetype("8 8");
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m draw(A--D--C--B--cycle);
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m draw(D--H--G--C);
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m draw(A--E--H);
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m draw(B--F--E);
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m draw(F--G);
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m draw(H--A--G, d);
