[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the sum of the two matrices $\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\ 1 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 8 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix}$, we need to add the corresponding elements of the matrices together.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Add the first element of the first matrix to the first element of the second matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -5 + 0 = -5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Add the second element of the first matrix to the second element of the second matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    1 + 8 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Add the third element of the first matrix to the third element of the second matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    -4 + (-4) = -4 - 4 = -8
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Putting these results together, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} -5 \\ 9 \\ -8 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\ 9 \\ -8 \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
