[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine how many dollars Mike will be offered in 12 more years, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Identify the initial offer and the double-for-profit trend:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Three years ago, Mike paid \(\$1.25\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Currently, the offer price (new price) is double the original amount: \(2 \times \$1.25 = \$2.50\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Understand the doubling trend:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The sticker price \(P\) doubles every 3 years.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Therefore, after 3 years, the new sticker price becomes \(\text{New Price} = P \times 2\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - In 12 years, \(12\) divided by \(3\) gives \(4\). So, the offer price will be \(P \times 2^4\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Compute the new offer price after 12 years:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(P \times 2^4 = P \times 16\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - So, the current offer price is \(\$16.00\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, in 12 more years, Mike will be offered \(\boxed{16}\) dollars.<|endoftext|>
