[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      Since 10 is less than 60, we need to find the next multiple of 60, which is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      60 \times 1 = 60
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      The next integer, 1, is greater than 60, so we need to check the multiples of 60.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Check the multiples of 60 within the range 10 to 100:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Multiples of 60 are 60 itself and numbers of the form \(60k\) where \(k\) is an integer.
