[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve for \(\binom{19}{9}\), we can use Pascal's Identity. Pascal's Identity states that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{n}{k} = \binom{n}{n-k}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m and
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{n}{k} = \binom{n-1}{k-1} + \binom{n-1}{k}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we use the identity with \(n = 19\) and \(k = 9\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{19}{9} = \binom{19}{19-9}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{19}{9} = \binom{19}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We also use the identity with \(n = 18\) and \(k = 9\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{18}{9} = \binom{18}{18-9}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{18}{9} = \binom{18}{9}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This identity is always true. To find \(\binom{18}{9}\), we can use Pascal's Identity:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{18}{9} = \binom{17}{10} + \binom{17}{9}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We know from the problem statement that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{17}{9} = 24310
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We need to find \(\binom{17}{10}\). Using Pascal's Identity again with \(n = 17\) and \(k = 10\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{17}{10} = \binom{17}{17-10}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{17}{10} = \binom{17}{7}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We know from the problem statement that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{17}{7} = 19448
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we can substitute these values back into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{18}{9} = 19448 + 24310
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \binom{18}{9} = 43758
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, we have:
