[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}^{2016}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute \(\begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}^{2016}\), we will use concepts from both matrix multiplication and exponential properties. Let's proceed step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's define \( A = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix} \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We need to find \( A^{2016} \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 1: Determine the Eigenvalues of \( A \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The eigenvalues of \( A \) can be found by solving the characteristic equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \det(A - \lambda I) = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m where \( I \) is the identity matrix. First, compute \( A - \lambda I \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A - \lambda I = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix} - \lambda \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 - \lambda & -4 \\ 1 & -1 - \lambda \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, compute the determinant:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \det(A - \lambda I) = \begin{vmatrix} 3 - \lambda & -4 \\ 1 & -1 - \lambda \end{vmatrix} = (3 - \lambda)(-1 - \lambda) - (-4)(1)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = (3 - \lambda)(-1 - \lambda) + 4
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = -3 - 3\lambda + \lambda + \lambda^2 + 4
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = \lambda^2 - 2\lambda + 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = (\lambda - 1)^2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The eigenvalues are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \lambda_1 = 1 \quad \text{and} \quad \lambda_2 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 2: Determine the Eigenvectors of \( A \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m For \(\lambda_1 = 1\), solve \((A - I)\mathbf{v} = \mathbf{0}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (A - I)\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -4 \\ 1 & -2 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This gives us the system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2x - 4y = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x - 2y = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = 2y
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substitute \( x = 2y \) into the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2(2y) - 4y = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4y - 4y = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This is consistent. So, an eigenvector corresponding to \(\lambda_1 = 1\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{v}_1 = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since the eigenvalue is the same, \( A \) is diagonalizable and thus, the Jordan form is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m J = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 3: Compute \( A^{2016} \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \( A^{2016} = (AJ)^{2016} = J^{2016} \), we can compute the 2016th power of the Jordan form:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (JAJ)^{2016} = J^{2016}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The Jordan form \( J \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m J = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The 2016th power of the identity matrix \( I \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m I^{2016} = (I^3)^{672} = (I^2)^{1036} = (I^2)^{672}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \( I^2 \) is the identity matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m I^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (I^2)^{1036} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}^{1036} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m J^{2016} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Putting it all together, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}^{2016} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Ground Truth]
