[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the center of circle \( C_2 \) is \( (-15, 0) \) and the radius is \( \sqrt{240} = 4\sqrt{15} \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 2: Determine the tangency condition
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A line segment \( PQ \) is tangent to both circles if it is perpendicular to the radii drawn from the center of each circle to the point of tangency. The radius to the point of tangency of circle \( C_1 \) from point \( P \) and the radius to the point of tangency of circle \( C_2 \) from point \( Q \) are perpendicular to the line \( PQ \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The distance from the center of circle \( C_1 \), \( (10, 0) \), to the line \( PQ \) (considering the projection of \( PQ \) on the tangent line) can be found using the formula for the distance from a point to a line. However, a simpler approach is to recognize that the shortest line segment will be the one that is directly below the radius of each circle at the point of tangency.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The distance from the point of tangency to the point \( P \) on the horizontal ring \( C_1 \) is the same as the radius of \( C_1 \), which is 6. The distance from the point of tangency to the point \( Q \) on the horizontal ring \( C_2 \) is the distance from the point \( Q \) to the point \( P \) itself on \( C_1 \). The vertical distance between these points is the same as the vertical distance from \( Q \) to the vertical line passing through \( (0, 0) \) dividing the horizontal ring into two equal components, which is \( \frac{81-36}{2} = 6 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 3: Find the length of the line segment \( PQ \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The length of the line segment \( PQ \) is the sum of the radius of \( C_1 \) and the vertical distance from \( Q \) to the vertical line passing through the point of tangency. Therefore, the length is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6 + 6 = 12
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the length of the shortest line segment \( PQ \) that is tangent to both circles \( C_1 \) and \( C_2 \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{8}
