[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the value of \(x\) given the equations \(2x + 3y = 4\) and \(y = 34\), we can substitute the value of \(y\) into the first equation and solve for \(x\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Start with the equation \(2x + 3y = 4\) and substitute \(y = 34\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    2x + 3(34) = 4
