[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To simplify \((5-3i)(-4+3i)\), we use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials). Distributing each term in the first binomial to each term in the second binomial, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (5-3i)(-4+3i) = 5(-4) + 5(3i) + (-3i)(-4) + (-3i)(3i)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, let's compute each term:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. \(\boxed{5(-4)} = \boxed{-20}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Similarly for the imaginary parts:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(\boxed{5(3i)} = \boxed{15i}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. \(\boxed{(-3i)(-4)} = \boxed{12i}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. \(\boxed{(-3i)(3i)} = \boxed{-9i^2}\) (since \(i^2 = -1\))
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Putting it all together, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5(-4) + 5(3i) + (-3i)(-4) + (-3i)(3i) = -20 + (15i) + (12i) - 9i^2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(i^2 = -1\), we can simplify further:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -20 + (15i) + (12i) - 9(-1) = -20 + 15i + 12i + 9
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Combining the real parts and the imaginary parts:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -20 + 9 + 15i + 12i = -11 + 27i
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the simplified form of \((5-3i)(-4+3i)\) is:
