[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Sure, let's break this down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Find the side length of the square:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - An area of a square is given by the formula \( \text{Area} = \text{side length}^2 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - We know the area is 25 square units.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Let \(\text{side length} = 5\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Determine the width of the rectangle:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The width of the rectangle is double the width of the square.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Let \(\text{width} = 2 \times 5 = 10\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Find the length of the rectangle:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The length of the rectangle is double its width.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Let \(\text{length} = 2 \times 10 = 20\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. **Calculate the area of the rectangle:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The area of a rectangle is given by the formula \( \text{Area} = \text{length} \times \text{width} \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Substitute the values we found:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \text{Area} = 20 \times 10 = 200
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the area of the rectangle is \(\boxed{200}\).<|endoftext|>
