[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \right.\]Find $f(-7)+f(0)+f(7)$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find \( f(-7) + f(0) + f(7) \) for the piecewise function
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(x) = \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x^2+1 & \text{ if } x > 5, \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2x-3 & \text{ if } -5 \le x \le 5, \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3 & \text{ if } x < -5,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{cases} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m we need to evaluate each expression separately.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's evaluate \( f(7) \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \( 7 > 5 \), we use the first part of the piecewise function:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(7) = 7^2 + 1 = 49 + 1 = 50. \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, let's evaluate \( f(-7) \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \( -7 \le -5 \), we use the second part of the piecewise function:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(-7) = 2(-7) - 3 = -14 - 3 = -17. \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Finally, let's evaluate \( f(0) \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \( 0 \le 5 \), we use the second part of the piecewise function:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(0) = 2(0) - 3 = 0 - 3 = -3. \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we add these values together:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(-7) + f(0) + f(7) = -17 + (-3) + 50. \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Performing the addition and addition operations step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ -17 + (-3) = -17 - 3 = -20, \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ -20 + 50 = 30. \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
