[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute the product \(98 \times 102\) accurately, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition. There are several ways to solve this problem, but I will provide you with a more straightforward approach using the greedy algorithm or by performing vertical multiplication with counting.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step-by-Step Solution
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m #### Using the Distributive Property
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can perform the multiplication directly by recognizing that 102 is similar to 100 + 2. So we can rewrite the multiplication as:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[98 \times 102 = 98 \times (100 + 2)\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Then, we use the distributive property to break it down:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[98 \times (100 + 2) = (98 \times 100) + (98 \times 2)\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, calculate each part separately:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[98 \times 100 = 9800\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[98 \times 2 = 196\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Add the results together:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[9800 + 196 = 9996\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\boxed{9996}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
