[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Carolyn went to the tooth dentist three times a week for an average of two hours per visit. She spent an average of 40 minutes washing her hair and bought brushes and floss for $15 each. If she wants to visit the dentist monthly and could reduce her visits by 10% in the future to focus only on her teeth, how much time will she save per month, and how much she will spend on brushes and floss in the future? Let's break down Carolyn's dental visits and the implications of reducing her visits step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Dental Visits:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Carolyn visits the dentist 3 times per week.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Each visit lasts 2 hours, 40 minutes.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Total time for one visit: \(2 \text{ hours} + 40 \text{ minutes} = 2 + \frac{40}{60} = 2 + \frac{2}{3} = 2.67 \text{ hours}\). Converting to minutes: \(2.67 \times 60 = 160 \text{ minutes}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Total visits per month: \(3 \times 4 = 12\) visits.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Total time per month: \(12 \times 160 = 1920 \text{ minutes}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Brushing and Flossing:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - She spends an average of 15 dollars per brush and floss.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Total brush and floss cost per visit: \(15 \text{ dollars} + 15 \text{ dollars} = 30 \text{ dollars}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Total cost for brushes and floss per month: \(30 \text{ dollars} \times 12 = 360 \text{ dollars}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Since she reduces her visits by 10% in the future, let's assume she visits only 10% of the time in the future.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Number of future visits: \(4 \times 0.1 = 0.4\), so she effectively visits 48% of the time. Thus, the marketing expenses remain the same.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Total future cost: \(360 \text{ dollars} \times 0.6 = 216 \text{ dollars}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Saving on Brushing and Floss:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The savings per month is the difference between the total cost of visits and the total cost of marketing.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Savings per month: \(1920 - 216 = 1704 \text{ dollars}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the amount of time Carolyn will save per month is \(\boxed{1072}\) minutes (since 160 minutes per visit times 12 visits over 12 months gives 1920 minutes, and 1920 - 1072 = 848 minutes), and the total amount she will spend on brushes and floss in the future is \(\boxed{216}\) dollars.
