[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine the value of \( k \) for which the line represented by the equation \(-\frac{1}{2}-2kx = 5y\) contains the point \(\left(\frac{1}{4}, -6\right)\), we need to substitute \( x = \frac{1}{4} \) and \( y = -6 \) into the equation and solve for \( k \).
