[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine the ordered pair \((c, d)\) for the plane given by the parametric equation \(\mathbf{v}(t) = \begin{pmatrix} 1 + t \\ 3t \\ 1 - t \end{pmatrix}\), we need to eliminate the parameter \(t\). 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The parametric equations of the line are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{v}(t) = \begin{pmatrix} 1 + t \\ 3t \\ 1 - t \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We introduce a new parameter \(s\) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m s = t
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substituting \(t = s\) into the parametric equations, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{v}(s) = \begin{pmatrix} 1 + s \\ 3s \\ 1 - s \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we eliminate the parameter \(s\) by solving for \(t\) in terms of \(s\). From the equation for \(t\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m t = s
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substitute \(t = s\) into the equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{v}(s) = \begin{pmatrix} 1 + s \\ 3s \\ 1 - s \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now solve for \(s\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m s = 1 + s \implies s - s = 1 \implies 0 = 1 \quad \text{(This is a contradiction, so we need to reconsider)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We should correctly express the solution:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m t = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substitute \(t = 1\) back into the parametric equation for \(v\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{v}(1) = \begin{pmatrix} 1 + 1 \\ 3(1) \\ 1 - 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the parametric equation for the line becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{v}(t) = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This clearly lies in the plane defined by \(x + y + cz = d\). From \(\mathbf{v}(t) = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}\), we can identify \(c\) and \(d\).
