[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the remainder when \(8 \cdot 10^{18} + 1^{18}\) is divided by 9, we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Calculate \(10^{18} \mod 9\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Observe that 10 is \(2 \cdot 5\), both of which are even numbers. Because of this, we can write \(10 \equiv 0 \mod 9\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    10^{18}/3 = 10^{18}/9 + 10^{-18}/3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Since \(10^{-18}/3\) is clearly an integer, and:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    10^{18} \div 9 \equiv 0 \mod 9
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Thus, \(10^{18}/9 \equiv 0 \mod 9\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Calculate \(1^{18} \mod 9\):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - \(1^1 \mod 9 = 1\), and any power of 1 is still 1:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    1^{18} \equiv 1 \mod 9
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Combine the results:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    8 \cdot 10^{18} + 1^{18} \equiv 8 \cdot 0 + 1 \equiv 1 \mod 9
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the remainder when \(8 \cdot 10^{18} + 1^{18}\) is divided by 9 is \(\boxed{1}\).<|endoftext|>
