[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A circle centered at $O$ has radius 1 and contains the point $A$. Segment $AB$ is tangent to the circle at $A$ and $\angle
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m AOB=\theta$. If point $C$ lies on $\overline{OA}$ and $\overline{BC}$ bisects $\angle ABO$, then express $OC$ in terms of $s$ and $c,$ where $s = \sin \theta$ and $c = \cos \theta.$
