[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m On a map, a 12-centimeter length represents 72 kilometers.  How many kilometers does a 17-centimeter length represent?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine how many kilometers a 17-centimeter length represents, we need to establish the relationship between centimeters and kilometers. We know that 12 centimeters represent 72 kilometers. We can use this information to set up a proportion to find out how many kilometers 17 centimeters would represent.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let \( x \) be the number of kilometers that 17 centimeters represents. The proportion can be set up as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{17 \text{ cm}}{72 \text{ km}} = \frac{17}{x \text{ km}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From this proportion, we can solve for \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 17x = 72 \times 17
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, calculate \( 72 \times 17 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 72 \times 17 = 72 \times (10 + 7) = 72 \times 10 + 72 \times 7
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 72 \times 10 = 720
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 72 \times 7 = 504
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 72 \times 17 = 1304
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, \( 72 \times 17 = 1304 \). Now, substitute this back into our proportion:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 17x = 1304
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve for \( x \), divide both sides of the equation by 17:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = \frac{1304}{17} = 76
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, a 17-centimeter length represents \( 76 \) kilometers. The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{76}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
