[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m If Alex gives Bob a penny, Bob will have three times as many pennies as Alex has. If Bob gives Alex a penny, Bob will have twice as many pennies as Alex has. How many pennies does Bob currently have?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve this problem, let's define the number of pennies Alex currently has as \( A \) and the number of pennies Bob currently has as \( R \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From the problem statement:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. If Bob gives Alex a penny, Bob will have three times as many pennies as Alex has. So we can write the equation: \( R + 1 = 3 \times A \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. If Bob gives Alex a penny, Bob will have twice as many pennies as Alex has. So we can write the equation: \( R + 2 = 2 \times A \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We now have a system of two linear equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m R + 1 = 3A \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m R + 2 = 2A
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve this system, we can subtract the first equation from the second to eliminate \( R \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (R + 2) - (R + 1) = 2A - 3A
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1 = -A
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A = -1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now substitute \( A = -1 \) into the first equation to find \( R \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m R + 1 = 3(-1)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m R + 1 = -3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m R = -3 - 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m R = -4
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, Bob currently has \( R = -4 \) pennies. The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{-4}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
