[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To evaluate \(\left\lceil {-\!\sqrt{23}}\right\rceil\), we need to determine the greatest integer that is less than or equal to \(-\!\sqrt{23}\). Here are the steps to find this value:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Identify the nature of infinity in mathematics:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Infinity is a concept used to describe something that has no end. If we consider \(-\!\sqrt{23}\), this is an unbounded minus the square root of 23, which is a very large number.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
