[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let $a$, $b$, and $c$ be three distinct one-digit numbers. What is the maximum value of the sum of the roots of the equation $(x-a)(x-b)+(x-b)(x-c)=0$?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the maximum value of the sum of the roots of the equation \((x-a)(x-b)+(x-b)(x-c)=0\), we start by analyzing the equation. This equation can be rewritten under a common factor:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (x-a)(x-b)+(x-b)(x-c) = 0 \implies (x-a)(x-b) + (x-b)(x-c) = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can factor out the terms that will come into play. First, combine like terms inside the parentheses:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (x-a)(x-b) + (x-b)(x-c) = (x-a)(x-c) + (x-b)(x-c)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, let's introduce new variables:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m p = x - a \implies x = p + a
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m q = x - b \implies x = b + q
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m r = x - c \implies x = c + r
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substitute these expressions into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ((p + a) - a)((b + q) - b) + ((b + q) - b)((c + r) - c) = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplify each term:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (p)(q) + (q)(r) = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m pq + qr = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can factor out \(-q\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -q(p + q) = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(q \neq 0\) (it is a root of the original equation), we can divide both sides by \(-q\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m p + q = 0 \implies p = -q
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This implies that \(p\) and \(-q\) are additive inverses of each other and have the same opposite sign. To maximize the sum of the roots, we choose \(p\) and \(-q\) in opposite directions. Let us choose \(p = 1\) and \(-q = -1\) (or vice versa) to satisfy the equation \(pq + qr = 0\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m p = 1, \quad q = -1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The roots of the equation will be:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = p + a = 1 + a
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = b + q = b - 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = c + r = c - 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The sum of the roots is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (1 + a) + (1 - 1) + (c - 1) = 1 + a + 0 + c - 1 = a + c
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the maximum value of the sum of the roots is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{0}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{33}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
