[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To calculate the greatest common factor (GCF) of 180 and 450, we can use the prime factorization method.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 1: Find the prime factors of the larger number (450).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The prime factors of 450 are 2, 3, 3, and 5.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 2: Find the prime factors of the smaller number (180).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The prime factors of 180 are 2, 2, 3, and 3.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 3: The common prime factors are the common prime factors of 450 and 180.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In this case, the only common prime factor is 2.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 4: To find the GCF, multiply the common prime factors and take the lowest exponent for each prime factor.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The GCF of 180 and 450 is 6 (2 used twice, 3 used once).
