[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 27 + 2x = 39 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find \( x \), we need to solve this equation. First, we'll eliminate the constant term by subtracting 27 from both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 2x = 39 - 27 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 2x = 12 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we'll divide both sides by 2 to isolate \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
