[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve for \( n \) in the range \(-90 < n < 90\) such that \(\tan n^\circ = \tan 252^\circ\), we start by using the property of the tangent function. The tangent function is periodic with a period of \(180^\circ\). This means that \(\tan(\theta) = \tan(\theta + 180^\circ k)\) for any integer \(k\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, note that \(252^\circ\) and \(660^\circ\) are within one full period of \(180^\circ\). The tangent values repeat every \(180^\circ\), so we can reduce \(252^\circ\) modulo \(180^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 252^\circ \div 180^\circ = 1 \text{ remainder } 72^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, \(252^\circ = 180^\circ + 72^\circ\). Since \(\tan \theta = \tan + 180^\circ k\) for any integer \(k\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \tan 252^\circ = \tan (180^\circ + 72^\circ) = \tan 72^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we need to find the value of \(\tan 72^\circ\). Using the known value of the tangent of \(72^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \tan 72^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{5} + 1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the integer \(n\) such that \(\tan n^\circ = \tan 252^\circ = \tan 72^\circ\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{72}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
