[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine the percentage of students who own cats, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Calculate the total number of students who own cats:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Total number of students = 300
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Number of students who own dogs = 60
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Therefore, number of students who own cats = Total number of students - Number of students who own dogs
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Number of students who own cats} = 300 - 60 = 240
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Calculate the percentage of students who own cats:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Number of students who own cats = 240
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Total number of students = 300
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Percentage of students who own cats = \(\left( \frac{\text{Number of students who own cats}}{\text{Total number of students}} \right) \times 100\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \left( \frac{240}{300} \right) \times 100 = 0.8 \times 100 = 80\%
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the percentage of students who own cats is \(\boxed{80}\).<|endoftext|>
