[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To convert the point \((5, \frac{3\pi}{2}, 4)\) from cylindrical coordinates \((r, \theta, z)\) to rectangular coordinates \((x, y, z)\), we need to use the following formulas:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. \( x = r \cos \theta \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. \( y = r \sin \theta \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. \( z = z \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \( r = 5 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \( \frac{3\pi}{2} \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's calculate \( \cos \left( \frac{3\pi}{2} \right) \) and \( \sin \left( \frac{3\pi}{2} \right) \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(\cos \left( \frac{3\pi}{2} \right) = 0\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(\sin \left( \frac{3\pi}{2} \right) = -1\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, substitute these values into the formulas:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. \( x = r \cos \theta \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ x = 5 \cdot 0 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. \( y = r \sin \theta \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ y = 5 \cdot (-1) = -5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. \( z = z \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ z = 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the rectangular coordinates are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \boxed{(x, y, z) = (0, -5, 4)} \]<|endoftext|>
