[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m An. 4 years. B. 5 years. C. 6 years. D. 7 years. E. 8 years. F. 9 years. G. 10 years.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please respond by writing a program in Python.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve this problem, we need to calculate the Projected value (PV) of the project for each period based on the given conditions. Here’s the step-by-step approach:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Determine the Projected value (PV) for each year:** Use the option pricing method with the given required rate of return (14.4%), the historical stock price (PV value) 22.20 per share, and the risk-free rate (0.7%) for 12.5-year duration.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Calculate the updated cost of equity after accounting for the dividend increment and the weighted average cost of capital (WACC) of 12.5% for 12.5-year duration:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here's the Python code to calculate the Projected value (PV):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Given data
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m PA_debt = 2000  # Projected value of the Mr. Diversified plan, in million dollars per year
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m PA_cost_2 = 13.5  # Cost of infinite holder's equity, in dollars per share per year
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m PA_cost_cb = 10.5  # Cost of current holder's equity, in dollars per share per year
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m PB = 0.70  # Yield on bonds over 12.5 years
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m CFC_6 = 12.50  # Beta for the Hereby-cited common stock and the CD instrument, in hundreds
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m CFC_5 = 9.50  # Beta for the CD instrument and the cost of debt, in hundreds
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m CFC_4 = 11.50  # Beta for the Hereby-cited common stock and the CD instrument, in hundreds
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A_00 = 9.20  # Projected value of the cane bar project
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m V_00 = 22.20  # Value of cane bar project for 8 years
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m C1 = -4110000  # Projected long term effect on investment value
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Option-pricing formula
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m def option_v(S0, R0_f, b):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     A = (PB - R0_f) / (b - 1)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     return A * S0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Calculate Projected long-term value at the end of year 5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A5 = option_v(V_00, PA_cost_2, CFC_6)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m PV_00 = A5 + A_00
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Total multi-years value
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Years = 5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m PV = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m for _ in range(Years):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     PeriodS0 = PA_cost_2 - PA_cost_cb
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     beta = CFC_5 / PeriodS0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     A = option_v(A_b/CFC_4, PA_cost_2, beta)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     PV += A / (CFC_5 + PeriodS0)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     AR_ER0_f = A / V_00
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m     AR_Yield = AR_ER0_f * C1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m print(PV)
