[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A freight train travels 1 mile in 1 minute 30 seconds. At this rate, how many miles will the train travel in 1 hour?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's break this down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we need to define the rate of the train:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - 1 mile is traveled in 1 minute 30 seconds.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we need to find out how many miles the train travels in 1 hour.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Convert 1 hour into minutes:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 1 \text{ hour} = 60 \text{ minutes} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Calculate the duration of the train's journey in minutes:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 60 \text{ minutes} = 1 \text{ hour} \times 60 \text{ minutes/hour} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{Duration} = 180 \text{ minutes} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Convert the duration from minutes to hours (since 1 mile is traveled in 180 minutes):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 180 \text{ minutes} = \frac{180}{60} \text{ hours} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{Duration} = 3 \text{ hours} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. Calculate the total length of the train's journey in miles:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{Distance} = \frac{\text{Duration}}{\text{Rate of one mile}} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{Distance} = \frac{3 \text{ hours}}{1 \text{ hour/mile}} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{Distance} = 3 \text{ miles} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the train will travel \(\boxed{3}\) miles in 1 hour.<|endoftext|>
