[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The function $f(x)$ satisfies
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[3f(x) - 2 f \left( \frac{1}{x} \right) = x\]for all $x \neq 0.$  Find $f(4).$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve for \( f(4) \), we start with the given functional equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 3f(x) - 2 f \left( \frac{1}{x} \right) = x \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m for all \( x \neq 0 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, substitute \( x = 4 \) into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 3f(4) - 2 f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) = 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, substitute \( x = \frac{1}{4} \) into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 3f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) - 2 f(4) = \frac{1}{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now we have a system of linear equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. \( 3f(4) - 2 f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) = 4 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. \( 3f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) - 2 f(4) = \frac{1}{4} \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To eliminate \( f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) \), we can multiply the first equation by 2 and the second equation by 1, then subtract them:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 2(3f(4) - 2 f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right)) = 2 \cdot 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 2(3f(4) - 2 f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right)) = 8 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 6f(4) - 4f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) = 8 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now subtract the second equation from the first:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ (3f(4) - 2 f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right)) - (3f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) - 2 f(4)) = 4 - \frac{1}{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 3f(4) - 2 f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) - 3f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) + 2 f(4) = 4 - \frac{1}{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 5f(4) - 5f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) = \frac{16}{4} - \frac{1}{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 5f(4) - 5f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) = \frac{15}{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 5f(4) = 5f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) + \frac{15}{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(4) = f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) + \frac{3}{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now substitute \( f \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) = \frac{4}{3} f(4) - 1 \) back into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(4) = \frac{4}{3} f(4) - 1 + \frac{3}{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(4) = \frac{4}{3} f(4) + 1 - \frac{3}{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(4) = \frac{4}{3} f(4) - \frac{3}{4} + \frac{4}{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(4) = \frac{4}{3} f(4) + \frac{1}{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(4) - \frac{4}{3} f(4) = \frac{1}{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ -\frac{4}{3} f(4) = \frac{1}{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ f(4) = -\frac{3}{16} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the value of \( f(4) \) is \(\boxed{-\frac{3}{16}}\).<|endoftext|>
