[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute the greatest common divisor (gcd) of \(83^{9} + 1\) and \(83^{9} + 83^{2} + 1\), we can use the property of gcd that states if \(a\) and \(b\) are coprime (i.e., \(\gcd(a, b) = 1\)), then their gcd can be found using the formula \(a \cdot b - a^2 - b^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \gcd(a, b) = \gcd(a - b, ab)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let \(a = 83^{9} + 83^2 + 1\) and \(b = 83^{9} + 1\). Then,
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ab = 83^{9} + 83^2 \cdot 1 + 1 = 83^{9} + 83^2 + 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \gcd(83^{9} + 83^2 + 1, 83^{9} + 83^2 + 1) = \gcd(83^{9} + 83^2 + 1, 83^{9} + 83^2 + 1) = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the gcd of \(83^{9} + 1\) and \(83^{9} + 83^2 + 1\) is \(\boxed{1}\).<|endoftext|>
