[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the slope \( m \) is \(-4\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Use the slope to find the y-intercept (\( b \)):**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The equation of a line in slope-intercept form is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
