[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve the problem of reflecting the point \((3, 4)\) across the \(x\)-axis, we need to understand how reflection in the \(x\)-axis affects the coordinates of a point. Reflecting a point across the \(x\)-axis changes the sign of the \(y\)-coordinate while keeping the \(x\)-coordinate the same.
