[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's identify the divisors of 50 and 15.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - The divisors of 50 are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \pm 1, \pm 2, \pm 5, \pm 10, \pm 25, \pm 50
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - The divisors of 15 are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \pm 1, \pm 3, \pm 5, \pm 15
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we find common divisors:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - The common divisors of 50 and 15 are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \pm 1, \pm 5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we denote $S_1$ as the sum of the divisors of 50 that are also divisors of 15:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m S_1 = 1 + 5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Calculating this:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m S_1 = 1 + 5 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To verify that there are no common divisors between 50 and 15 other than 1:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - The only divisors common to both 50 and 15 are 1 and 5.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since $S_1$ is one of the common divisors and there are no other common divisors, the only answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \Square
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the sum of all positive divisors of 50 that are also divisors of 15 is \boxed{6}.<|endoftext|>
