[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To expand the expression \( (x^{22} - 3x^{5} + x^{-2} - 7) \cdot (5x^4) \), we will use the distributive property. This means we will multiply each term in the first polynomial by each term in the second polynomial.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x^{22} \cdot 5x^4 - 3x^{5} \cdot 5x^4 + x^{-2} \cdot 5x^4 - 7 \cdot 5x^4
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, let's perform each multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. \( x^{22} \cdot 5x^4 = 5x^{26} \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. \( -3x^{5} \cdot 5x^4 = -15x^{9} \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. \( x^{-2} \cdot 5x^4 = 5x^{-2} \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. \( -7 \cdot 5x^4 = -35x^4 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Putting these results together, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5x^{26} - 15x^{9} + 5x^{-2} - 35x^4
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the expanded form of the expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{5x^{26} - 15x^{9} + 5x^{-2} - 35x^4}
