[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The numerical value of a particular square's area is equal to the numerical value of its perimeter. What is the length of a side of the square?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve this problem, let's start by understanding the relationship between the area and the perimeter of a square.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The area \( A \) of a square is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ A = \text{side}^2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The perimeter \( P \) of a square is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ P = 4 \times \text{side} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m According to the problem, the numerical value of the area and the numerical value of the perimeter are equal. Therefore, we can set up the following equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{side}^2 = 4 \times \text{side} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can simplify this equation by moving all terms to one side:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{side}^2 - 4 \times \text{side} = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we factor out the common term \(\text{side}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{side}(\text{side} - 4) = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This equation tells us that the side length \(\text{side}\) of the square could be either 0 or \(\text{side} - 4 = 0\). Solving for \(\text{side}\) in the second equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{side} = 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the length of a side of the square is \(\boxed{4}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4\text{ units}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
