[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Shirts: all available colors (tan, black, blue, gray, white, yellow)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Hats: all available colors (tan, black, blue, gray, white, yellow)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Calculate the total number of possible outfits without any restrictions:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - If we use all 6 shirts, we have \(6 \times 3\) outfits (since each shirt can be paired with any of the 3 pants). 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    6 \times 3 = 18
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - If we use all 4 pairs of pants, we have \(4 \times 2\) outfits (since each pair of pants can be paired with any of the 2 hats). 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    4 \times 2 = 8
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - If we use all 6 hats, we have \(6\) outfits (since each hat can be paired with any of the 6 shirts and 1 pair of pants, which can also be paired with itself. Therefore, we have \(6 \times 2 + 6 \times 1 = 12 + 6 = 18\) outfits. However, we have counted the outfits we already counted (6 outfits), so we subtract 6.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    8 - 6 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, without any restrictions, the total number of possible outfits is 2.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Subtract the number of restricted outfits from the total number of possible outfits:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - We need to ensure that all 3 items are the same color. If we use all 6 shirts and all 4 pairs of pants, we have 1 shirt and 4 pairs of pants with 4 hats, which is already including all 3 shirts and 8 pairs of pants.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    2 - 1 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the number of valid outfits is \(\boxed{1}\).
