[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In a certain amount of time, a plane traveling at a constant $250$ miles per hour traveled $20,\!000$ feet.  In this same amount of time, how many feet would a plane traveling at a constant $400$ miles per hour travel?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine how far a plane traveling at a constant \(400\) miles per hour would travel in the corresponding time, we can use the fact that both planes are traveling at the same speed, which we'll call \(v\). Here are the steps to solve the problem:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Convert the flight time from hours to minutes:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Flight time} = \frac{20,000 \text{ feet}}{250 \text{ miles}} = 80 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Determine the distance traveled by the plane at \(v\) miles per hour:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \text{Distance} = v \times \text{Flight time} = 400 \text{ miles per hour} \times 80 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Calculate the distance in miles and convert it to feet:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    400 \text{ miles per hour} \times 80 \text{ minutes} = 32,000 \text{ miles}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    32,000 \text{ miles} \times 5280 \text{ feet per mile} = 163,520,000 \text{ feet}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the plane traveling at a constant \(400\) miles per hour would travel approximately \(\boxed{163,520,000}\) feet in the corresponding time.<|endoftext|>
