[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m What is the area of the gray region, in square units, if the radius of the larger circle is four times the radius of the smaller circle and the diameter of the smaller circle is 2 units? Express your answer in terms of $\pi$. [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m size(150);
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m pair A, B;
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A=(0,0);
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m B=(-4,1);
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m fill(circle(A, 8), gray(.7));
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m fill(circle(B, 2), white);
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m draw(circle(A, 8));
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m draw(circle(B, 2));
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [/asy]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the area of the gray region, we need to calculate the areas of the two circles and find the area of the gray triangle that occupies the area between the two circles.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 1: Calculate the area of the larger circle.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The radius of the larger circle is four times the radius of the smaller circle. Since the smaller circle has a radius of 1 unit, the radius of the larger circle is \(4 \times 1 = 4\) units.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The area \(A_{\text{large}}\) of the larger circle is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ A_{\text{large}} = \pi r^2 = \pi (4)^2 = 16\pi \text{ square units} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 2: Calculate the area of the smaller circle.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The area of the smaller circle is \(\pi\) square units since it has a radius of 1 unit.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ A_{\text{small}} = \pi (1)^2 = \pi \text{ square units} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Step 3: Define the area of the gray triangle.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The gray region is the area between the two circles, which we can find by subtracting the area of the smaller circle from the area of the larger circle.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ A_{\text{gray}} = A_{\text{large}} - A_{\text{small}} = 16\pi - \pi = 15\pi \text{ square units} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the area of the gray region is \(15\pi\) square units.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 15\pi
