[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m How many distinct diagonals of a convex pentagon can be drawn?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the number of distinct diagonals in a convex pentagon, we can use the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Number of diagonals = n(n - 3)/2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m where n is the number of sides of the pentagon. In this case, n = 5.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Number of diagonals = 5(5 - 3)/2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Number of diagonals = 5(2)/2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Number of diagonals = 5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, there are 5 distinct diagonals in a convex pentagon.
