[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the matrix-vector product \( AB \), we compute each entry of the resulting matrix \( C \). The entry in the \( i \)-th row and \( j \)-th column of the matrix \( C \) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m C_{ij} = \sum_{k=1}^{3} A_{ik} B_k
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m where \( A_{ik} \) are the entries of the first row of \( A \) and \( B_k \) are the entries of the column \( k \) of the column vector \( B \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. For \( i = 1 \) and \( j = 1 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
