[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute the given sum \(\sum_{n=2}^{101} \frac{2 + n \cdot 6}{4^n}\), we start by simplifying the general term of the series. The general term is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{2 + n \cdot 6}{4^n} = \frac{2}{4^n} + \frac{n \cdot 6}{4^n} = \frac{2}{4^n} + \frac{6n}{4^n} = \frac{2}{4^n} (1 + 3n) = \frac{2}{4^n} \cdot \frac{1 + 3n}{1}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the sum becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \sum_{n=2}^{101} \frac{2}{4^n} (1 + 3n)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we expand the sum term by term:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{2}{4^2} \cdot (1 + 3 \cdot 2) + \frac{2}{4^3} \cdot (1 + 3 \cdot 3) + \frac{2}{4^4} \cdot (1 + 3 \cdot 4) + \cdots + \frac{2}{4^{101}} \cdot (1 + 3n)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{2}{16} \cdot (1 + 6) + \frac{2}{64} \cdot (1 + 9) + \frac{2}{256} \cdot (1 + 12) + \cdots + \frac{2}{4^{101}} \cdot (1 + 3n)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m which further simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{2}{16} \cdot 7 + \frac{2}{64} \cdot 10 + \frac{2}{256} \cdot 15 + \cdots + \frac{2}{4^{101}} \cdot (1 + 3n)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = \frac{1}{8} \cdot 7 + \frac{1}{32} \cdot 10 + \frac{3}{128} \cdot 15 + \cdots + \frac{2}{4^{101}} \cdot (1 + 3n)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = \sum_{k=0}^{101} \left( \frac{1}{8} \cdot 7 + \frac{1}{32} \cdot 10 + \frac{3}{128} \cdot 15 + \cdots + \frac{2}{4^{101}} \cdot (1 + 3k) \right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we need to find a pattern in the sum. Notice that:
