[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We are given that this expression equals \(1000x^3 + 27\) for all \(x\). Since the coefficients of \(x^3\), \(x^2\), and \(x\) must match, we can separate the coefficients of \(x^3\) and \(x^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ad = 1000 \quad \text{(1)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ae + bd = 0 \quad \text{(2)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m af + be + cd = 0 \quad \text{(3)}
