[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let $\mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ -3 & -1 \end{pmatrix}.$  There exist scalars $p$ and $q$ such that
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\mathbf{M}^2 = p \mathbf{M} + q \mathbf{I}.\]Enter the ordered pair $(p,q).$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve for the scalars \( p \) and \( q \) such that \(\mathbf{M}^2 = p \mathbf{M} + q \mathbf{I}\), we start by calculating \(\mathbf{M}^2\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ -3 & -1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we compute \(\mathbf{M}^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{M}^2 = \mathbf{M} \cdot \mathbf{M}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find \(\mathbf{M}^2\), we multiply each element of \(\mathbf{M}\) by each element of \(\mathbf{M}\) and sum the products:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{M}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ -3 & -1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ -3 & -1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Calculate each element of \(\mathbf{M}^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (2 \cdot 2) + (7 \cdot -3) = 4 - 21 = -17
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (2 \cdot 7) + (7 \cdot -1) = 14 - 7 = 7
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (-3 \cdot 2) + (-1 \cdot -3) = -6 + 3 = -3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (-3 \cdot 7) + (-1 \cdot -1) = -21 + 1 = -20
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{M}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} -17 & 7 \\ -3 & -20 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m It is given that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{M}^2 = p \mathbf{M} + q \mathbf{I}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(\mathbf{I}\) is the identity matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{M}^2 = p \mathbf{M} + q \mathbf{I}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, we equate the two expressions:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} -17 & 7 \\ -3 & -20 \end{pmatrix} = p \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ -3 & -1 \end{pmatrix} + q \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This gives us a system of linear equations by comparing corresponding elements:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. \( -17 = p \cdot 2 + q \cdot 1 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. \( 7 = p \cdot 7 + q \cdot 0 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. \( -3 = p \cdot -3 + q \cdot 0 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. \( -20 = p \cdot 1 + q \cdot 1 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplify each equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. \( -17 = 2p + q \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. \( 7 = 7p - 20 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. \( -3 = -3p \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. \( -20 = p + q \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Solve the third equation for \( p \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -3 = -3p \implies p = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substitute \( p = 1 \) into the first and fourth equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -17 = 2(1) + q \implies -17 = 2 + q \implies q = -19
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Finally, substitute \( p = 1 \) and \( q = -19 \) into the third equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -3 = -3(1) \implies -3 = -3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Both equations are satisfied, so the scalars are confirmed:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{(1, -19)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
