[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ $d$ be positive integers such that
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} 3 & 0 \\ 0 & 2 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 18 & 12 \\ -20 & -13 \end{pmatrix}.\]Find the smallest possible value of $a + b + c + d.$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve this problem, we need to find positive integers \(a\), \(b\), \(c\), and \(d\) such that the given matrix equation holds:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 0 \\ 0 & 2 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 18 & 12 \\ -20 & -13 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's compute both sides of the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Left-hand side (LHS):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 0 \\ 0 & 2 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 3a & 3b \\ 2c & 2d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 18 & 12 \\ -20 & -13 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 3a \cdot 18 + 3b \cdot -20 & 3a \cdot -13 + 3b \cdot -13 \\ 2c \cdot 18 + 2d \cdot -20 & 2c \cdot -13 + 2d \cdot -13 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Right-hand side (RHS):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 18 & 12 \\ -20 & -13 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a \cdot 18 + b \cdot -20 \\ c \cdot 18 + d \cdot -20 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 18a - 20b \\ 18c - 20d \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Equating the corresponding elements from the LHS and RHS:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 3a \cdot 18 + 3b \cdot -20 & 3a \cdot -13 + 3b \cdot -13 \\ 2c \cdot 18 + 2d \cdot -20 & 2c \cdot -13 + 2d \cdot -13 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 18a - 20b \\ 18c - 20d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 18a - 20b \\ 18c - 20d \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From this, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3a \cdot 18 + 3b \cdot -20 = 3a - 20b \quad \text{(1)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3a \cdot -13 + 3b \cdot -13 = -13a + 13b \quad \text{(2)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2c \cdot 18 + 2d \cdot -20 = 18c - 20d \quad \text{(3)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2c \cdot -13 + 2d \cdot -13 = -26c - 26d \quad \text{(4)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplifying these equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 54a - 60b = 3a - 20b \implies 51a = 40b \implies 3a = \frac{40b}{3} \implies a = \frac{40b}{9}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3a \cdot -13 - 3b \cdot -13 = -13a + 13b \implies -39a + 39b = -13a + 13b \implies -36a + 26b = 0 \implies 26a = 26b \implies a = b
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m And similar for \(c\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 12c + 13c = 18c - 20d \implies 25c = 18c - 20d \implies 7c = -20d \implies c = -\frac{20d}{7}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(a\), \(b\), \(c\), and \(d\) are positive integers, and from the above steps, \(a = b\) leads to a contradiction. The equation \(c = -\frac{20d}{7}\) implies \(d\) has to be a negative number to make \(c\) an integer. This contradiction eliminates \(b\) and \(a\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Find \(c\) using the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 18c - 20d = 18c - 20d
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The smallest possible positive integers result leads us to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m c = 3, d = 3, a = 4, b = 4, \text{ maximum totals}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, summing up:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m a + b + c + d = 4 + 4 + 3 + 3 = 14
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the smallest possible value of \(a + b + c + d\) is \(\boxed{14}\).<|endoftext|>
