[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The hypotenuse of a right triangle measures 10 inches and one angle is $45^{\circ}$. What is the number of square inches in the area of the triangle?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the area of the right triangle, we need to determine the lengths of the other two sides (adjacent and opposite) which are both 10 inches because the triangle is a right triangle and one of the angles is $45^{\circ}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 1: Determine the length of the hypotenuse
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since one angle is $45^{\circ}$, the triangle is a 45-45-90 triangle. In a 45-45-90 triangle, the legs are equal, and the hypotenuse is $\sqrt{2}$ times the length of each leg. In this case, the length of each leg is 10 inches:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Length of hypotenuse} = 10 \times \sqrt{2} = 10\sqrt{2} \text{ inches}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 2: Calculate the area of the triangle
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The area of a right triangle is given by half the product of the lengths of the legs:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times \text{leg}_1 \times \text{leg}_2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here, $5$ and $10$ are the lengths of the legs, so:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times 5 \times 10 = \frac{1}{2} \times 50 = 25 \text{ square inches}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the number of square inches in the area of the triangle is $\boxed{25}$.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
