[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the value of \( b \), we will solve the given system of linear equations step-by-step.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2a + 1 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m b - a = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we solve the first equation for \( a \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2a + 1 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Subtract 1 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2a = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Divide both sides by 2:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m a = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now that we have \( a = 0 \), we substitute this value into the second equation to find \( b \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m b - a = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
