[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve this problem, we need to consider all possible combinations of officers for the chairman, vice-chairman, treasurer, and morale officer from the 10 available members. We then multiply these combinations together since each selection can work for all 4 officers independently.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The number of ways to choose a president from 10 members is \(10\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The number of ways to choose a vice-chairman from the remaining 9 members is \(9\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The number of ways to choose a treasurer from the remaining 8 members is \(8\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The number of ways to choose a morale officer from the remaining 7 members is \(7\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the total number of possible combinations, we multiply these numbers together:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 10 \times 9 \times 8 \times 7 \]
