[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the area of the triangle formed by the points \(\mathbf{0}\), \(\mathbf{a}\), and \(\mathbf{b}\), we can use the determinant formula for the area of a triangle with vertices \((x_1, y_1)\), \((x_2, y_2)\), and \((x_3, y_3)\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
