[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve the equation \(\frac{9-4x}{x+6}=7\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Eliminate the denominator**: Multiply both sides of the equation by \(x+6\) to clear the fraction.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \frac{9-4x}{x+6} \cdot (x+6) = 7 \cdot (x+6)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    9 - 4x = 7(x + 6)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Distribute the 7**: Distribute 7 on the right-hand side of the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    9 - 4x = 7x + 42
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Isolate the variable \(x\)**: To do this, add \(4x\) to both sides of the equation to get all the \(x\) terms on one side.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    9 + 4x - 4x = 7x + 42 + 4x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Simplifying this, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    9 = 11x + 42
