[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve for the base \( b \) such that \( b \) base-34 numbers sum up to \( b \) base-b numbers, we need to understand the properties of base conversions. Specifically, in base \( b \), the number \( 34_b \) can be expressed in base \( b \) as \( b^2 + b + 4 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's denote the \( b \) base-34 numbers as \( a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_k \). These numbers can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ a_1 = 34_a \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ a_2 = 34_a = 3 \cdot 34_a \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ a_3 = 34_a = 3 \cdot 34_a = 3^3 \cdot 34_a \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \vdots \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ a_k = 34_a = 3^k \cdot 34_a \]
