[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The sum of these \( k \) numbers in base \( b \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \sum_{i=1}^k a_i = \sum_{i=1}^k (3^i \cdot 34_a) = 34_a \sum_{i=1}^k 3^i \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The sum of the powers of 3 from \( k+1 \) to \( 2k \) is an arithmetic series:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \sum_{i=1}^k 3^i = 3 + 3^2 + 3^3 + \cdots + 3^k = 3 \cdot \frac{3^k - 1}{3 - 1} = \frac{3(3^k - 1)}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the sum of all these \( k \) numbers is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \sum_{i=1}^k a_i = b^2 + b + 4 = \frac{3(3^k - 1)}{2} + b^2 + b + 4 \]
