[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine how many blueberry bushes Natalie needs to pick to have forty-eight zucchinis, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Calculate how many zucchinis one blueberry bush can yield.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Determine how many zucchinis are needed to make one zucchini (since each zucchini is made up of two zucchinis, one blueberry bush gives us four zucchinis).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Determine how many blueberry bushes are needed to get forty-eight zucchinis.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's break this down and calculate it step by step using Python code.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Step 1: Calculate how many zucchinis one blueberry bush can yield
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m containers_per_bush = 8
