[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m What is the largest value of $x$ such that $(4x+11)(2x-8)=x(2x+7)$? Express your answer as a fraction.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve the equation \((4x+11)(2x-8) = x(2x+7)\), we will first expand both sides of the equation. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Starting with the left-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (4x+11)(2x-8) = 4x \cdot 2x + 4x \cdot (-8) + 11 \cdot 2x + 11 \cdot (-8)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 8x^2 - 32x + 22x - 88
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 8x^2 - 10x - 88
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now for the right-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x(2x+7) = 2x^2 + 7x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 8x^2 - 10x - 88 = 2x^2 + 7x
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we move all terms to one side to set the equation to zero:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 8x^2 - 10x - 88 - 2x^2 - 7x = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6x^2 - 17x - 88 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now we have a standard quadratic equation in the form \(ax^2 + bx + c = 0\). Here, \(a = 6\), \(b = -17\), and \(c = -88\). We will solve this using the quadratic formula \(x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we calculate the discriminant:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m b^2 - 4ac = (-17)^2 - 4 \cdot 6 \cdot (-88)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 289 + 1792
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m = 2081
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we find the square root of the discriminant:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \sqrt{2081} = \sqrt{49 \cdot 41} = 7\sqrt{41}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now we apply the quadratic formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = \frac{-(-17) \pm 7\sqrt{41}}{2 \cdot 6}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = \frac{17 \pm 7\sqrt{41}}{12}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the solutions are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x_1 = \frac{17 + 7\sqrt{41}}{12}, \quad x_2 = \frac{17 - 7\sqrt{41}}{12}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can express these solutions in a simplified form without fractions:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x_1 = \frac{17 + 7\sqrt{41}}{12}, \quad x_2 = \frac{17 - 7\sqrt{41}}{12}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the largest value of \(x\), we compare \(\frac{17 + 7\sqrt{41}}{12}\) and \(\frac{17 - 7\sqrt{41}}{12}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{17 + 7\sqrt{41}}{12} \quad \text{and} \quad \frac{17 - 7\sqrt{41}}{12}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since squaring both sides does not change the order of the variables, we compare:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x_1 > x_2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the largest value of \(x\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\frac{17 + 7\sqrt{41}}{12}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
