[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine how many ounces of zinc are in Henri's brass trumpet, we need to understand the composition of the brass. Brass is made up of copper and zinc. The initial composition of the brass is 80% copper and 20% zinc. This means that the remaining percentage, which is the zinc content, is 20%.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we calculate the amount of zinc in the brass:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - The total percentage of copper in the brass is \(80\%\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Therefore, the percentage of zinc in the brass is \(100\% - 80\% = 20\%\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since the brass is 20% zinc, we can calculate the amount of zinc by multiplying the total amount of brass by the percentage of zinc:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{Amount of zinc} = \text{Total amount of brass} \times \text{Percentage of zinc} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{Amount of zinc} = 48 \text{ ounces} \times 20\% \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{Amount of zinc} = 48 \text{ ounces} \times 0.20 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{Amount of zinc} = 9.6 \text{ ounces} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the amount of zinc in Henri's brass trumpet is \(\boxed{9.6}\) ounces.
