[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To simplify \((7b^3)^2 \cdot (4b^2)^{-3}\), we will follow a step-by-step approach.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's simplify each part of the expression separately.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Simplify \((7b^3)^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    (7b^3)^2 = 7^2 \cdot (b^3)^2 = 49b^{12}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Simplify \((4b^2)^{-3}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    (4b^2)^{-3} = 4^{-3} \cdot (b^2)^{-3} = \frac{1}{4^3} \cdot \left(\frac{1}{b^2}\right)^3 = \frac{1}{64} \cdot \frac{1}{b^6} = \frac{1}{64b^6}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we combine the simplified parts:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 49b^{12} \cdot \frac{1}{64b^6} = 49 \cdot \frac{1}{64} \cdot b^{12 - 6} = \frac{49}{64} \cdot b^6 = \frac{49b^6}{64}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the simplified form of \((7b^3)^2 \cdot (4b^2)^{-3}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\frac{49b^6}{64}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
