[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find \(\cot \frac{3\pi}{2}\), we need to recognize the value of the cotangent function at this angle. The cotangent function is defined as the ratio of the cosine function to the sine function:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cot \theta = \frac{\cos \theta}{\sin \theta}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m For an angle \(\theta = \frac{3\pi}{2}\), we know that \(\frac{3\pi}{2}\) is an angle in the second quadrant (since sine is positive in this quadrant). In the second quadrant, the cosine is negative and the sine is positive. This will help us to determine the sign of the cotangent function.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The specific values of the trigonometric functions in the second quadrant are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \cos \frac{3\pi}{2} = 0 \quad \text{and} \quad \sin \frac{3\pi}{2} = -1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we can substitute these values into the cotangent function:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
