[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We have: $$54+(23^5\div 159)+130-200.$$ Let's square: $$54+23^{(5\div 159)}+130-200.$$ Let's change the order of operations: $$54+23^5\div159+130-200.$$ Let's take the fifth root of 54: $$\sqrt[5]{\left(54\right)^{1/4}}.$$ We have: $$\sqrt[5]{\left(54\right)^{1/4}}.$$ Now we see what it equals: $$54\div\left(54^4\div4\right)$$ which equals \boxed{\frac{1}{2}} (or $0.5$).<|endoftext|>
