[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Convert the point $(\rho,\theta,\phi) = \left( 3, \frac{5 \pi}{12}, 0 \right)$ in spherical coordinates to rectangular coordinates.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To convert the point \((\rho, \theta, \phi) = \left( 3, \frac{5\pi}{12}, 0 \right)\) from spherical coordinates \((\rho, \theta, \phi)\) to rectangular coordinates \((x, y, z)\), we can use the following formulas:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x = \rho \sin\phi \cos\theta
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m y = \rho \sin\phi \sin\theta
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m z = \rho \cos\phi
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m (\rho, \theta, \phi) = \left( 3, \frac{5\pi}{12}, 0 \right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's plug these values into each formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Calculate \(x\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Calculate \(y\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Calculate \(z\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here are the calculations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. \(x = \rho \sin\phi \cos\theta\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    x = 3 \sin(0) \cos\left(\frac{5\pi}{12}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Since \(\sin(0) = 0\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    x = 3 \cos\left(\frac{5\pi}{12}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Calculate \(y\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    y = \rho \sin\phi \sin\theta
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Since \(\sin(\phi) = \sin(0)\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    y = 3 \sin\left(\frac{5\pi}{12}\right) \sin\left(\frac{5\pi}{12}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Since \(\sin(0) = 0\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    y = 3 \sin^2\left(\frac{5\pi}{12}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Calculate \(z\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    z = \rho \cos\phi
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Since \(\cos(0) = 1\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    z = 3 \cos\left(\frac{5\pi}{12}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the rectangular coordinates are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{(3 \cos\left(\frac{5\pi}{12}\right) \sin^2\left(\frac{5\pi}{12}\right), 3 \cos\left(\frac{5\pi}{12}\right), 3 \sin\left(\frac{5\pi}{12}\right))}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
