[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m I'll compute the determinant of the given 3x3 matrix. The determinant of a 3x3 matrix \(\begin{bmatrix} a & b & c \\ d & e & f \\ g & h & i \end{bmatrix}\) is calculated using the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{det} = a(ei - fh) - b(di - fg) + c(dh - eg)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Plugging in the values from our problem:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{vmatrix} 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   1 & \cos (a - b) & \cos a \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \cos (a - b) & 1 & \cos b \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \cos a & \cos b & 1 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m =
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1 \cdot \left(1 \cdot 1 - \cos b \cdot \cos b\right) - \cos (a - b) \cdot \left(\cos (a - b) \cdot 1 - \cos a \cdot \cos a\right) + \cos a \cdot \left(\cos (a - b) \cdot \cos b - \cos a \cdot 1\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's simplify this expression step by step using Python to ensure accuracy:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{vmatrix} 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   1 & \cos (a - b) & \cos a \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \cos (a - b) & 1 & \cos b \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \cos a & \cos b & 1 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m =
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1 \cdot \left(1 - \cos^2 b\right) - \cos (a - b) \cdot \left(\cos (a - b) - \cos^2 a\right) + \cos a \cdot \left(\cos (a - b) \cos b - \cos a\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Which simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1 - \cos^2 b - \cos (a - b) \left(\cos (a - b) - \cos^2 a\right) + \cos a \left(\cos (a - b) \cos b - \cos a\right)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's compute it in Python.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m from sympy import symbols, cos, simplify, cos_to_representation
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Define the variables
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m a, b = symbols('a b')
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Define the matrix
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A = [[1, cos(a - b), cos(a)],
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      [cos(a - b), 1, cos(b)],
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      [cos(a), cos(b), 1]])
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m # Expand the determinant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m det = A[0, 0] * (A[1, 1] * A[2, 2] - A[1, 2] * A[2, 1]) - \
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m       A[0, 1] * (A[1, 0] * A[2, 2] - A[1, 2] * A[2, 0]) + \
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m       A[0, 2] * (A[1, 0] * A[2, 1] - A[1, 1] * A[2, 0])
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m det = simplify(det)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m print(det)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ```
