[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Sure! We have the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \dfrac{1}{2} + \dfrac{1}{x} = \dfrac{5}{6}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's isolate $\dfrac{1}{x}$ by subtracting $\dfrac{1}{2}$ from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \dfrac{1}{x} = \dfrac{5}{6} - \dfrac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To subtract the fractions, we need a common denominator. The common denominator for 6 and 2 is 6, so we rewrite $\dfrac{1}{2}$ as $\dfrac{3}{6}$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
