[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m What is the units digit of $19^{19}+99^{99}$?
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine the units digit of \(19^{19} + 99^{99}\), we need to analyze the units digit of each term separately and then combine the results.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 1: Units Digit of \(19^{19}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, observe the units digit of \(19^{k}\) for different values of \(k\). The units digit of \(19\) is \(9\), and the units digit cycles in a pattern every 10 powers of 9:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 9^1 \equiv 9 \pmod{10}, \quad 9^2 \equiv 1 \pmod{10}, \quad 9^3 \equiv 9 \pmod{10}, \quad 9^4 \equiv 1 \pmod{10}, \quad \text{and so on.}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the units digit of \(19^{19}\) will be the same as the units digit of \(9^{19}\). Since \(19 \div 10 = 1\) with a remainder of \(9\) (because \(19\) is not divisible by \(10\)), the units digit of \(9^{19}\) is \(9\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 2: Units Digit of \(99^{99}\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, observe the units digit of \(99\). The units digit of \(99\) is \(9\). When we raise a number whose units digit is \(9\) to any higher power, the units digit remains \(9\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 9^{10} \equiv 1 \pmod{10}, \quad 9^{11} \equiv 9 \pmod{10}, \quad 9^{12} \equiv 1 \pmod{10}, \quad 9^{13} \equiv 9 \pmod{10}, \quad \text{and so on.}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the units digit of \(99^{99}\) is \(9\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m ### Step 3: Combining the Results
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we add the units digits of \(19^{19}\) and \(99^{99}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 9 + 9 = 18
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The units digit of \(18\) is \(8\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the units digit of \(19^{19} + 99^{99}\) is \(\boxed{8}\).<|endoftext|>
