[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Two concentric circles are centered at point P. The sides of a 45 degree angle at P form an arc on the smaller circle that is the same length as an arc on the larger circle formed by the sides of a 36  degree angle at P. What is the ratio of the area of the smaller circle to the area of the larger circle? Express your answer as a common fraction.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the ratio of the areas of the smaller circle to the larger circle, we start by defining their radii. Let's denote the larger circle as \(O_1\) and its center as \(P_1\). The smaller circle will be \(O_2\) and will circumscribe \(O_1\), so the centers of both circles will be \(P\) and \(O_2\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - The arc length of the 45-degree angle at \(P\) in the smaller circle corresponds to the arc length of the 36-degree angle at \(P\) in the larger circle. Since the two angles are in the ratio of \(\frac{36}{45}\), the ratio of the angles is \(\frac{4}{3}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The arc length of a quarter circle passing through a point is \(\frac{360^\circ}{4} = 90^\circ\) of that full circle. This is equivalent to three 45-degree arcs. Therefore, the arc length of the smaller circle is three times the angle of the smaller circle in that same ratio, which means the smaller circle has arc length that is three times the smaller circle’s radius. The radius \(r_1\) of the smaller circle is also just the radius of the larger circle because it divides the larger circle into two equal parts.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let the radius of the larger circle be \(R_1\). Then, the radius of the smaller circle \(r_2\) is also \(R_1\), and the angle of the smaller circle in the standard circle system is \(\frac{4}{3}\) of the angle of the larger circle in degrees. Therefore, the angle of the smaller circle in the standard circle system is \(\frac{4}{3} \times 360^\circ = 480^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The perimeter of the smaller circle (which is equal to the ratio of its circumference to \(\pi\)) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{Perimeter of smaller circle} = \frac{480^\circ}{\pi} \times \text{radius of smaller circle} = \frac{480^\circ}{\pi} \times R_1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The circumference of a circle is given by \(2\pi R_1\), so the circumference of the larger circle is \(2\pi R_1\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{Perimeter of larger circle} = 2\pi R_1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \frac{480^\circ}{\pi} \times R_1 = 2\pi R_1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m By canceling \(\pi\) from both sides, we find:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \frac{480^\circ}{R_1} = 2 R_1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 480^\circ = 2 R_1^2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ R_1^2 = 240^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ R_1 = \sqrt{240} = 4\sqrt{15} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the radius of the larger circle \(R_1\) is \(4\sqrt{15}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The area of the larger circle is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{Area of larger circle} = \pi R_1^2 = \pi (4\sqrt{15})^2 = 120\pi \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The area of the smaller circle is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{Area of smaller circle} = (4\sqrt{15})^2\pi = 120\pi \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the ratio of the area of the smaller circle to the area of the larger circle is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \text{Ratio} = \frac{\text{Area of smaller circle}}{\text{Area of larger circle}} = \frac{120\pi}{120\pi} = 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the ratio of the area of the smaller circle to the area of the larger circle is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \boxed{1} \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
