[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the coefficient of \(x^3\) in the product of \((24x^4 + 6x^3 + 4x^2 - 7x - 5)(6x^3 + 3x^2 + 3x + 4)\), we need to identify the terms in each polynomial that, when multiplied together, result in an \(x^3\) term and then sum their coefficients.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The polynomial we are working with is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[P(x) = 24x^4 + 6x^3 + 4x^2 - 7x - 5\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m and
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[Q(x) = 6x^3 + 3x^2 + 3x + 4.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the coefficient of \(x^3\) in the product \(P(x) \cdot Q(x)\), we look at the terms in each polynomial that include \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(x^4\) in \(Q(x)\) multiplied by \(x\) in \(P(x)\) gives \(x^5\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(x^3\) in \(P(x)\) multiplied by \(x\) in \(Q(x)\) gives \(x^4\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(x^2\) in \(P(x)\) multiplied by \(x\) in \(Q(x)\) gives \(0x^3\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(x^2\) in \(P(x)\) multiplied by \(Q(x)\) gives \(-7x^2\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(x^2\) in \(P(x)\) multiplied by \(Q(x)\) gives \(3x^2\cdot4x = 12x^3\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(x\) in \(P(x)\) multiplied by \(Q(x)\) gives \(-7x^2\cdot4 = -28x^2\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(x^1\) in \(P(x)\) multiplied by \(Q(x)\) gives \(-7x\cdot4 = -28x\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(x^0\) in \(Q(x)\) multiplied by \(P(x)\) gives \(-5\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m When we combine all these terms, we look at the contributions to the \(x^3\) term:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(x^5\) from \(x^5\) * \(x\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(x^4\) from \(x^4\) * \(x\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(0x^3\) from \(x^3\) * \(x^3\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(-7x^2\) from \(x^2\) * \(x^2\), so this is \(-7x^4\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(-28x^2\) from \(x^2\) * \(Q(x)\), so this is \(-28x^4\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(-28x\) from \(x^2\) * \(Q(x)\), so this is \(-28x^3\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(-28x\) from \(x\) * \(Q(x)\), so this is \(-28x^3\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - \(0x^2\) from \(x^2\) * \(P(x)\), so this is \(-28x^2\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Adding these contributions together, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[x^5 + x^4 + 0x^3 - 7x^4 - 28x^4 - 28x^3 - 28x^2 - 28x^2.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplifying, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[x^5 - 8x^4 - 56x^3 - 56x^2.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the coefficient of \(x^3\) in the product is \(-56\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[\boxed{-56}.\]<|endoftext|>
