[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve this expression \(3 \times (7 - 5) - 5\), we will follow the order of operations, often remembered by the acronym PEMDAS (Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), Addition and Subtraction (from left to right)).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Evaluate the expression inside the parentheses:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    7 - 5 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    So the expression now becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    3 \times (2) - 5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Perform the multiplication:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    3 \times 2 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    So the expression now becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    6 - 5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Perform the subtraction:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    6 - 5 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the value of the expression \(3 \times (7 - 5) - 5\) is \(\boxed{1}\).<|endoftext|>
