[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Sure, let's proceed step by step to find the absolute value of the difference between \(18A\) and \(18B\), given \(A = \frac{1}{4}\) and \(B = -\frac{1}{2}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, calculate \(18A\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 18A = 18 \left(\frac{1}{4}\right) = \frac{18}{4} = 4.5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, calculate \(18B\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 18B = 18 \left(-\frac{1}{2}\right) = -9
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, find the difference between \(18A\) and \(18B\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 18A - 18B = 4.5 - (-9) = 4.5 + 9 = 13.5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The absolute value of \(13.5\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m |13.5| = 13.5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the absolute value of the difference is \(\boxed{13.5}\).<|endoftext|>
