[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Evaluate $i^{11} + i^{111}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To evaluate \( i^{11} + i^{111} \), we need to understand the properties of the imaginary unit \( i \), where \( i = \sqrt{-1} \). The powers of \( i \) cycle every four terms as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^1 = i, \quad i^2 = -1, \quad i^3 = -i, \quad i^4 = 1, \quad i^5 = i, \quad \text{and so on.}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This cyclic pattern implies:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^n = i^{n \mod 4}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m where \( n \) is any integer.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We start by calculating the first few powers of \( i \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^1 = i, \quad i^2 = -1, \quad i^3 = -i, \quad i^4 = 1, \quad i^5 = i, \quad i^6 = -1, \quad \text{and so on.}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we observe the pattern in the exponents:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 11 = 3 \times 3 + 2, \quad 111 = 3 \times 33 + 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using these observations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - For \( i^{11} \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   11 \mod 4 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   So, \( i^{11} = i^3 = -i \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - For \( i^{111} \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   111 \mod 4 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   So, \( i^{111} = i^3 = -i \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we add these results together:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m i^{11} + i^{111} = (-i) + (-i) = -2i
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(-2i\) is purely real, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{-2i}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -2i
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
