[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To evaluate \(\log_{\sqrt[3]{5}}125\), we use the change of base formula for logarithms. The change of base formula is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \log_b a = \frac{\log_c a}{\log_c b}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In this case, we can use base 10 or base \(e\) (the base of the natural logarithm), but for simplicity, we will use base 10. So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \log_{\sqrt[3]{5}}125 = \frac{\log_{10} 125}{\log_{10} \sqrt[3]{5}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we need to evaluate \(\log_{10} 125\). We know that \(125 = 5^3\), so:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \log_{10} 125 = \log_{10} (5^3) = 3 \log_{10} 5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we need to evaluate \(\log_{10} \sqrt[3]{5}\). We can rewrite \(\sqrt[3]{5}\) as \(5^{1/3}\), so:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \log_{10} \sqrt[3]{5} = \log_{10} (5^{1/3}) = \frac{1}{3} \log_{10} 5
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Putting these together, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \log_{\sqrt[3]{5}} 125 = \frac{3 \log_{10} 5}{\frac{1}{3} \log_{10} 5} = \frac{3 \log_{10} 5}{\frac{1}{3} \log_{10} 5} = \frac{3 \log_{10} 5}{\log_{10} 5} = 3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{3}
