[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the amount of zinc in Henri's brass trumpet, we need to determine the total amount of zinc in the alloy.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. First, we know that the alloy consists of $80\%$ copper and $20\%$ zinc. Since Henri's trumpet contains 48 ounces of copper, we can calculate the amount of zinc using the following equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Zinc} = \text{Total Copper} \times \text{Percentage of Zinc}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Zinc} = 48 \, \text{ounces} \times 20\%
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. To perform the multiplication, we use the relationship $a \times b = (a \times c) \times (b \times c)$, where $c = 100\%$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Zinc} = 48 \times \frac{20}{100} \times 100 \times 100
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Simplifying this expression:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Zinc} = 48 \times 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. Further simplifying:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Zinc} = 96 \, \text{ounces}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the clarinet contains $96$ ounces of zinc.
