[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Find the matrix $\mathbf{M}$ if it satisfies $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{i} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ -8 \end{pmatrix},$ $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{j} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix},$ and $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{k} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}.$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Certainly! Let's solve for the matrix $\mathbf{M}$ using the given equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{i} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ -8 \end{pmatrix}$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{j} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{k} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To compute $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{i}$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{M} \mathbf{i} = \begin{pmatrix} m_{11} & m_{12} & m_{13} \\ m_{21} & m_{22} & m_{23} \\ m_{31} & m_{32} & m_{33} \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} m_{11} \\ m_{21} \\ m_{31} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, we can set up the matrix equation as:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} m_{11} & m_{12} & m_{13} \\ m_{21} & m_{22} & m_{23} \\ m_{31} & m_{32} & m_{33} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This gives us the following system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{11} = 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{21} = 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{31} = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, the matrix equation for $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{j} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$ can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} m_{11} & m_{12} & m_{13} \\ m_{21} & m_{22} & m_{23} \\ m_{31} & m_{32} & m_{33} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This gives us the following system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{11} = 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{21} = 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{31} = -2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Finally, the matrix equation for $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{k} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}$ can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} m_{11} & m_{12} & m_{13} \\ m_{21} & m_{22} & m_{23} \\ m_{31} & m_{32} & m_{33} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This gives us the following system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{11} = 7 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{21} = -1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m_{31} = 4
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From the above matrix equations, we can deduce the following non-trivial solution:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} m_{11} \\ m_{21} \\ m_{31} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} + u \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplifying this, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mu + t(u + 1) = 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 7 \mu + t(-1 - 1) + u(4 + 2) = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{and}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mu + t(7 + 1) = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From the linear equations, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mu = 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Substituting $\mu = 2$ into the other linear equations, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m u(7 + 1) + 7t = 0 \implies 8t = -u \implies u = -8t
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 7u + 7t + 11t = 0 \implies 18t = 0 \implies t = 0
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{and}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2 + 1 - 8t = 0 \implies 3 = 8t \implies t = \frac{3}{8}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From these calculations, we see that a non-trivial solution exists if $t = \frac{3}{8}$. Thus, the matrix $\mathbf{M}$ can be constructed as:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{M} = t \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} + u \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} = \frac{3}{8} \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} + \frac{3}{8} \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We can thus write the final matrix as:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m M = \frac{3}{8} \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} + \frac{3}{8} \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{3}{8} \cdot 0 \\ \frac{3}{8} \cdot 5 \\ \frac{3}{8} \cdot -2 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} \frac{3}{8} \cdot 7 \\ \frac{3}{8} \cdot -1 \\ \frac{3}{8} \cdot 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{3}{8} \\ \frac{15}{8} \\ -\frac{6}{8} \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} \frac{21}{8} \\ -\frac{3}{8} \\ \frac{3}{2} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Finally, we combine the components:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{3}{8} \\ \frac{15}{8} \\ -\frac{6}{8} \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} \frac{21}{8} \\ -\frac{3}{8} \\ \frac{3}{2} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{3}{8} + \frac{21}{8} \\ \frac{15}{8} - \frac{3}{8} \\ -\frac{6}{8} + \frac{3}{2} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{24}{8} \\ \frac{12}{8} \\ \frac{-6 + 12}{8} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ \frac{3}{2} \\ \frac{6}{8} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ \frac{3}{2} \\ \frac{3}{4} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the matrix $\mathbf{M}$ is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m M = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ \frac{3}{2} \\ \frac{3}{4} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
