[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the area of the triangle given by the points \((-8, 0)\) and \((0, 8)\) in the coordinate plane, we can use the formula for the area of a triangle with vertices given by \((x_1, y_1)\), \((x_2, y_2)\), and \((x_3, y_3)\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Here, the vertices are \((-8, 0)\), \((0, 8)\), and \((x, y)\). We will use the coordinates \((-8, 0)\) and \((0, 8)\) as \((x_1, y_1)\) and \((0, y_2)\) respectively.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| -8(8 - y) + 0(y - 0) + x(0 - 8) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplify the expression inside the absolute value:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| -8(8 - y) - 8x \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Expand and simplify further:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| -64 + 8y - 8x \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Combine like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| 8y - 8x - 64 \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Factor out the -8 from the expression inside the absolute value:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| 8(y - x - 8) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The expression inside the absolute value is always non-negative, so the absolute value simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area} = \left| 8(y - x - 8) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Determine the sign of the expression inside the absolute value:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m y - x - 8 \geq 0 \quad \text{for the triangle to be valid}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the area is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Area} = 8(y - x - 8)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the area of the triangle is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
