[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To simplify the fraction \(\frac{84}{144}\), we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of the numerator (84) and the denominator (144).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we find the prime factorization of each number:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - The prime factorization of 84 is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   84 = 2 \times 2 \times 3 \times 7
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - The prime factorization of 144 is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   144 = 2 \times 2 \times 2 \times 2 \times 3 \times 3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we identify the common prime factors. The common factors of 84 and 144 are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - 2
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - 3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - 7
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The greatest common factor (GCF) is the product of these common prime factors:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{GCF} = 2 \times 2 \times 3 \times 7 = 84
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we divide both the numerator and the denominator of the fraction \(\frac{84}{144}\) by their GCF (84):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{84 \div 84}{144 \div 84} = \frac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the simplified form of \(\frac{84}{144}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{\frac{1}{2}}
