[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To evaluate $\lfloor 6.7 \rfloor + \lfloor -6.7 \rfloor$, we need to understand the concept of the floor function. The floor function $\lfloor x \rfloor$ gives the greatest integer less than or equal to $x$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. Calculate $\lfloor 6.7 \rfloor$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The greatest integer less than or equal to 6.7 is 6.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \lfloor 6.7 \rfloor = 6
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Calculate $\lfloor -6.7 \rfloor$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - The greatest integer less than or equal to -6.7 is -7.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \lfloor -6.7 \rfloor = -7
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Add the results from steps 1 and 2.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \lfloor 6.7 \rfloor + \lfloor -6.7 \rfloor = 6 + (-7) = 6 - 7 = -1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
