[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    First, compute \(\left(\frac{9}{4}\right)^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \left(\frac{9}{4}\right)^2 = \left(\frac{9}{4}\right) \times \left(\frac{9}{4}\right) = \frac{81}{16}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Now, apply the ceiling function to \(\frac{81}{16}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \frac{81}{16} \approx 5.0625
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    The ceiling function \(\left\lceil x \right\rceil\) gives the smallest integer greater than or equal to \(x\). Since \(5.0625\) is already an integer, \(\left\lceil 5.0625 \right\rceil = 5\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, sum the results:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \left\lceil\sqrt{\frac{9}{4}}\right\rceil + \left\lceil\frac{9}{4}\right\rceil + \left\lceil\left(\frac{9}{4}\right)^2\right\rceil = 2 + 3 + 5 = 10
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{10}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
