[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{array}{|c|c|c|}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \hline
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 25 & z & 8 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \hline
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 21 & x & w \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \hline
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 18 & 24 & y \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \hline
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This means that the sum of each row, column, or diagonal is equal. Therefore, the sum of each row is also equal to \( 25 + 21 + 18 \). Let's calculate this value first:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 25 + 21 + 18 = 64
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since there are 3 rows (or columns, or diagonals), the sum of all the numbers in the square must be:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3 \times 64 = 192
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, let's calculate the sum of each row sum from the left to the right:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 25 + z + 8 = 113
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m w + x + 21 = 113
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m y + z + 8 = 113
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x + z + 24 = 113
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We already know three of these sums:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x + z + 21 = 113 \implies x + z = 92
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m z + 8 = 113 \implies z = 105
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m y + z + 8 = 113 \implies y + 0 = 95 \implies y = 95
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m However, since the sum \( x + z = 92 \), we can verify by substituting back. If \( x = 92 \) and \( z = 105 \), then we need to check if the sum \( x + z = 92 \) holds true:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m x + z = 92
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now let's solve for \( w \) using the same logic. If \( z = 105 \), then the sum of the other rows would be:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 25 + 105 + 8 = 138
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m w + x + 21 = 138 \implies w + 105 = 138 \implies w = 33
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m y + 105 + 8 = 138 \implies y + 113 = 138 \implies y = 25
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
