[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we need to determine all the numbers that divide 91 without leaving a remainder.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. First, we check if 91 is a prime number or not:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 91 is not divisible by 2 (since it's odd).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Divide 91 by 3:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m      91 ÷ 3 = 30 ... remainder: 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - Test 91 can be divided by 5 (since \(91 \div 5 = 18.2\) and 5 is not an integer).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 91 is not divisible by either 5 or 2.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. Since 91 is a prime number, it has no divisors other than 1 and itself.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. Therefore, the only positive divisor of 91 is 1.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4. To verify, we should see if all numbers up to 101 (since the divisors of 91 are all less than or equal to 101) divide 91 without remainder.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's test this:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - 91 ÷ 1 = 91 (remainder: 0)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - 91 ÷ 10 = 9.1 ... remainder: 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - 91 ÷ 11 = 8.3 ... remainder: 3
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - 91 ÷ 12 = 7 ... not divisible
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - Check higher numbers...
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m When we check divisors higher than 10, we will find that each of 1 up to 10 satisfy the condition that 91 is a divisor. However, 10 and more than 11 cannot evenly divide 91.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the sum of all positive divisors of 91 is only 1.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
