[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{1}{206} = 0.0495495495495\ldots
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The digit that appears in the 205th position after the decimal point is the same as the digit in the \(205\)th position in the repeating sequence. Therefore, we need to find the digit in the repeating block.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To do this, we note that the first digit after the decimal point is 4. The next digit is 9, the next is a 4, the next is 9, and so on. We see that the pattern repeats every 2 digits. So, the 205th digit is the same as the 15th digit in the repeating sequence "49". The 15th digit in the sequence "49" is 9.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the 205th digit after the decimal point in the decimal representation of \(\frac{1}{206}\) is \(\boxed{9}\).
