[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the equation of the line in the form \(y = mx + b\), we need to determine the slope \(m\) and the y-intercept \(b\). The given parametric equations are:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's identify the slope \(m\). The slope \(m\) is the coefficient of \(t\) in the second component of the parametric equations. From the parametric equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - For \(x\), the coefficient of \(t\) gives the slope: \(m = -7\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m - For \(y\), the coefficient of \(t\) gives the slope: \(m = -2\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, both slopes are \(-7\), but since there is a different sign in the second component, we have two correct slopes: \(-7\) and \(7\). But we only need the one represented directly in the problem, so we choose the positive value for the slope:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m m = 7
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we need to find the y-intercept \(b\). We can determine \(b\) by substituting a specific value of \(t\) into the parametric equations and solving for \(y\). Let's use \(t = 0\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix} + 7 \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 49 \\ -14 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 46 \\ -20 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
