[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m we need to decompose the given rational function into partial fractions. 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's set up the decomposition as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{4x^3 - 20x^2 + 37x - 25}{(x-2)^3(x-1)} = \frac{A}{x-1} + \frac{B}{(x-2)^3} + \frac{C}{(x-2)^2} + \frac{D}{x-2}.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we combine the right-hand side over a common denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \frac{A}{x-1} + \frac{B}{(x-2)^3} + \frac{C}{(x-2)^2} + \frac{D}{x-2} = \frac{A(x-2)(x-1) + B(x-1)}{(x-1)(x-2)^3} + \frac{C(x-2)^3}{(x-1)(x-2)^3} + \frac{D(x-2)^2}{(x-1)(x-2)^3} + \frac{D}{(x-2)^2}.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Combine the numerators:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4x^3 - 20x^2 + 37x - 25 = A(x-2)(x-1) + B(x-2)^2 + C(x-1)(x-2) + D.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we expand each term:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m A(x-2)(x-1) = A(x^2 - x - 2),
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m B(x-2)^2 = B(x^2 - 4x + 4),
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m C(x-1)(x-2) = C(x^2 - 3x + 2),
