[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 0.2x = \text{number of students who selected milk} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We know that this number is 72:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 0.2x = 72 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find \( x \), we divide both sides of the equation by 0.2:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ x = \frac{72}{0.2} = 360 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
