[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the smallest value of \( x \) that satisfies the equation \( |3x + 7| = 26 \), we need to consider the properties of absolute values. The equation \( |3x + 7| = 26 \) can be split into two separate equations because of the absolute value:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. \( 3x + 7 = 26 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. \( 3x + 7 = -26 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We will solve each equation separately.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m **Solving the first equation:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 3x + 7 = 26 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Subtract 7 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 3x = 26 - 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 3x = 19 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Divide both sides by 3:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ x = \frac{19}{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, one solution is \( x = \frac{19}{3} \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m **Solving the second equation:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 3x + 7 = -26 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Subtract 7 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 3x = -26 - 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 3x = -33 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Divide both sides by 3:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ x = -11 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the other solution is \( x = -11 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine which of these solutions is smaller, we compare \( \frac{19}{3} \) and \( -11 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, calculate \( \frac{19}{3} \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \frac{19}{3} \approx 6.3333 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, consider \( -11 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ -11 \approx -11 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \( 6.3333 < -11 \), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ x = \frac{19}{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the smallest value of \( x \) that satisfies the equation \( |3x + 7| = 26 \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \boxed{\frac{19}{3}} \]<|endoftext|>
