[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the value of the sum $-1 + 2 - 3 + 4 - 5 + 6 - 7 + \dots + 10,000$, let's first understand the pattern.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Each term in the series can be expressed as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Term} = \begin{cases} 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -1 & \text{if } n \text{ is odd} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1 & \text{if } n \text{ is even}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This means we can pair the terms in a way that they cancel each other out. Specifically, we can pair up the odd-numbered terms and the even-numbered terms.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Let's analyze the first few terms:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6 + 7
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Each pair sums to 10:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -1 + 2 \quad = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1 + 3 \quad = 4
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 4 + 5 \quad = 9
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 9 + 6 \quad = 15
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 15 + 7 \quad = 22
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the first half of the terms (first 5 terms) sum to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1 + 4 + 9 + 15 + 22 = 41
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m The last term is 10,000. We can pair the next few terms:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 10000 / 2 = 5000
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{Even number, } 5000
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we put the pairs together:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 10,000 = 41 - 42 \text{ (this pair is repeated)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 41 + 42 = 83
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, the first half of the series up to 10,000 sum to:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 41 + 83 = 124
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We need to find the total sum from the first half:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \text{First half sum} = 41 \text{ (odd sum pairs)} + 83 \text{ (even sum pairs)} = 124
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We need to add the sequence up to 10,000:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 124 - 10,000 = -9,876
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
