[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine the smallest abundant number, we need to find a number \( n \) (where \( n = d_1 \times d_2 \cdots d_k \)) such that \( d_1 + d_2 + \cdots + d_k < n \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m We start by listing the smallest abundant numbers and checking their sum of divisors.
