[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 5. **6**: Deficient (since \( d_1 = 6 \) and \( d_2 = 1 \) where \( 1 = 1 \) and \( 6 = 2 \times 3 \)) with sum of divisors \( 1 + 3 + 2 = 6 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 6. **12**: Deficient (since \( d_1 = 6 \) and \( d_2 = 2 \) where \( 6 = 2 \times 3 \) and \( 2 = 2 \times 1 \)) with sum of divisors \( 1 + 2 + 3 = 6 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 7. **18**: Abundant (since \( d_1 = 18 \) and \( d_2 = 3 \), where \( 18 = 2 \times 3 \times 3 \) and \( 3 = 3 \)) with sum of divisors \( 1 + 2 + 3 + 6 = 13 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 8. **20**: Deficient (since \( d_1 = 20 \) and \( d_2 = 2 \) where \( 20 = 2 \times 2 \times 5 \)) with sum of divisors \( 1 + 2 + 4 + 5 = 12 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 9. **21**: Deficient (since \( d_1 = 21 \) and \( d_2 = 3 \) where \( 21 = 3 \times 7 \)) with sum of divisors \( 1 + 3 + 7 = 11 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 10. **24**: Deficient (since \( d_1 = 24 \) and \( d_2 = 3 \) where \( 24 = 2 \times 3 \times 4 \)) with sum of divisors \( 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 11. **24**: Deficient (since \( d_1 = 24 \) and \( d_2 = 3 \) where \( 24 = 3 \times 8 \)) with sum of divisors \( 1 + 3 + 4 + 8 = 16 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 12. **28**: Abundant (since \( d_1 = 28 \) and \( d_2 = 2 \) where \( 28 = 2 \times 2 \times 7 \) and \( 2 = 2 \times 1 \)) with sum of divisors \( 1 + 2 + 4 + 7 = 14 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 13. **30**: Abundant (since \( d_1 = 30 \) and \( d_2 = 5 \) where \( 30 = 2 \times 3 \times 5 \) and \( 5 = 5 \)) with sum of divisors \( 1 + 2 + 3 + 5 = 11 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 14. **30**: Abundant (since \( d_1 = 30 \) and \( d_2 = 5 \) where \( 30 = 2 \times 3 \times 5 \) and \( 5 = 5 \)) with sum of divisors \( 1 + 2 + 3 + 5 = 11 \).
