[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m If $a \star b = \dfrac{\left(\dfrac{1}{b} - \dfrac{1}{a}\right)}{(a - b)}$, express $3 \star 11$ as a common fraction.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To express \(3 \star 11\) as a common fraction, we start with the given operation:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m a \star b = \dfrac{\left(\dfrac{1}{b} - \dfrac{1}{a}\right)}{(a - b)}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we need to simplify the expression inside the parentheses:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \dfrac{1}{b} - \dfrac{1}{a} = \dfrac{a - b}{ab}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So the expression for \(3 \star 11\) becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3 \star 11 = \dfrac{\dfrac{a - b}{ab}}{11 - a} = \dfrac{a - b}{11a - ab^{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we need to evaluate this expression at \(a = 3\) and \(b = 11\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3 \star 11 = \dfrac{3 - 11}{11 \cdot 3 - 3^2} = \dfrac{-8}{33 - 9} = \dfrac{-8}{24} = \dfrac{-2}{6} = -\dfrac{1}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \boxed{-\dfrac{1}{3}}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
