[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 1: \(1\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 2: \(2\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 3: \(3\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 4: \(2^2\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 5: \(5\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 6: \(2 \times 3\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 7: \(7\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 8: \(2^3\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 9: \(3^2\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 10: \(2 \times 5\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 11: \(11\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 12: \(2^2 \times 3\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 13: \(13\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 14: \(2 \times 7\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 15: \(3 \times 5\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 16: \(2^4\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 17: \(17\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 18: \(2 \times 3^2\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - 19: \(19\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m From the above list, the number with the maximum number of distinct positive integer factors is 12, as it has exactly three prime factors (2, 3, and 5), 14, as it has four prime factors (2, 7), and 18, as it has six prime factors (2, 3, 3, 2, 3). The greatest number of distinct positive integer factors is 16 (for 12), 18 (for 18), and 12 (for 12).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, let's mark the answer for the greatest number of distinct positive integer factors. The answer is:
