[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the value of the sum \(10 e^{2 \pi i/11} + 10 e^{15 \pi i/22}\), we need to use Euler's formula, which states that \(e^{i\theta} = \cos(\theta) + i\sin(\theta)\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's express \(e^{2 \pi i/11}\) and \(e^{15 \pi i/22}\) using Euler's formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ e^{2 \pi i/11} = \cos\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) + i \sin\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ e^{15 \pi i/22} = \cos\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) + i \sin\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now, we add these two expressions together:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 10 e^{2 \pi i/11} + 10 e^{15 \pi i/22} = 10 \left( \cos\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) + i \sin\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) \right) + 10 \left( \cos\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) + i \sin\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) \right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Distribute the 10:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ = 10 \cos\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) + 10 \cos\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) + 10 i \sin\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) + 10 i \sin\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Combine the real and imaginary parts:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ = 10 \left( \cos\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) + \cos\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) \right) + 10 i \left( \sin\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) + i \sin\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) \right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using the angle addition formulas for sine and cosine:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \cos\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) + \cos\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) = 2 \cos\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11} + \frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) \cos\left(\frac{3 \pi}{22}\right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \sin\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) + i \sin\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) = \sin\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) - i \cos\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ = 10 \left( 2 \cos\left(\frac{3 \pi}{22}\right) \cos\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) \right) + 10 i \left( \sin\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) - i \cos\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) \right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ = 20 \cos\left(\frac{3 \pi}{22}\right) \cos\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) + 10 \sin^2\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) + 10 \cos^2\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Using the tangent addition formula for sine and cosine:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 10 \cos^2\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) = 10 \left(1 - \tan^2\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right)\right) = 10 \tan^2\left(\frac{\pi}{11}\right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 20 \cos\left(\frac{3 \pi}{22}\right) \cos\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) + 10 \tan^2\left(\frac{\pi}{11}\right) + 10 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Combining the terms with \(\tan^2\left(\frac{\pi}{11}\right)\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ = 10 \left(2 \cos\left(\frac{3 \pi}{22}\right) \cos\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) + \tan^2\left(\frac{\pi}{11}\right)\right) + 10 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Since \(\sin\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) = \cos\left(\frac{9 \pi}{22}\right)\), we can use the double-angle identity:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ 2 \cos\left(\frac{3 \pi}{22}\right) \cos\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) + \tan^2\left(\frac{\pi}{11}\right) = 1 + \cos\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) \sqrt{\sin^2\left(\frac{16 \pi}{22}\right)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Simplifying further, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ = 1 + \cos\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) \sqrt{\sin^2\left(\pi + \frac{3 \pi}{22}\right)} + \cos\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) \sqrt{\sin^2\left(\frac{7 \pi}{22}\right)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ = 1 + \cos\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) \cdot 0 + \cos\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) \cdot \cos\left(\frac{5 \pi}{11}\right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ = 1 + \cos\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) \cdot \cos\left(\frac{5 \pi}{11}\right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Thus, the sum is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ = 20 e^{i \frac{\pi}{11}} + 10 \cos\left(\frac{3 \pi}{22}\right) \cos\left(\frac{15 \pi}{22}\right) + 10 \sin^2\left(\frac{2 \pi}{11}\right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Therefore, the ordered pair \((r, \theta)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[ \boxed{\left( 20, \frac{5 \pi}{11} \right)} \]<|endoftext|>
