[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's evaluate the given problem, so we'll start by working with simple values of the base, such as $i$.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m  Well, we have the following basic values:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m  $i^1 = i$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m  $i^2 = -1$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m  $i^3 = -i$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m  $i^4 = 1$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m By explicitly examining our basic values, we should be able to make a formula of this.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m  Let's notice that, by the definition of the complex number $i$, the exponents of $i$ follow a geometric sequence that has an exponent of 4 below the $i$ symbol. That is, this geometric series will end at $i^4$:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m  $i^1$  $i^2$  $i^3$  $i^4$ --> $i$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Now we need to add all its current values, which means elevating every number beyond the $i$ symbol:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $ (i^1) + (i^2) + (i^3) + (i^4)$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $ = (i) + (-1) + (-i) + 1$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $ = (i - i - 1 + 1) + (-1)$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $ = -1$
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Well, that solved everything! That is the final result. Putting in the final answer as asked, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m $\boxed{ -1 }$
