[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To determine how many two-digit positive integers have at least one 7 as a digit, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 1. **Identify the range of two-digit positive integers:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Two-digit positive integers range from 10 to 99.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 2. **Count the total number of two-digit positive integers:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    The total number of two-digit positive integers is 99.
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 3. **Count the number of two-digit positive integers that do not contain the digit 7:**
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    We need to count these integers from 10 to 69 (since 70 is outside this range).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - From 10 to 19: There are 9 numbers (10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - From 20 to 29: There are 9 numbers (20, 21, 22, ..., 29).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - From 30 to 39: There are 9 numbers (30, 31, 32, ..., 39).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    - From 40 to 49: There are 9 numbers (40, 41, 42, ..., 49).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    Adding these together, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m    \[
