[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Find the integer $n$, $0 \le n \le 7$, such that \[n \equiv -3737 \pmod{8}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To find the integer \( n \) such that \( n \equiv -3737 \pmod{8} \), we need to compute the remainder when \(-3737\) is divided by \(8\). We can do this by finding the sum of the digits of \(-3737\) and dividing it by \(8\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, we calculate the sum of the digits of \(-3737\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -3737 = -3737, \quad 3 + 7 + 3 + 7 = 20
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Next, we divide \(20\) by \(8\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 20 \div 8 = 2 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 4
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m This tells us that:
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m -3737 \equiv 4 \pmod{8}
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m Hence, the integer \( n \) that satisfies the condition \( n \equiv -3737 \pmod{8} \) is \( n = 4 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
