[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m To solve for \( n \) such that \( n \equiv -3737 \pmod{8} \), we need to determine the remainder when \(-3737\) is divided by \(8\).
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m First, let's consider the general property of modular arithmetic. Specifically, for any integer \( k \) and \( m \) where \( \gcd(k, m) = 1 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \|k \mod m\| = \frac{|k|}{m} \cdot \gcd((-|k|), m)\|
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m In this case, \( n \equiv -3737 \pmod{8} \). Since \(-3737\) is negative, we can convert it to a positive equivalent by adding \(10\):
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \|(-3737) \mod 8\| = \frac{|-3737|}{8} \cdot \gcd(3737, 8)\)
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2326006)[0m \(\gcd(-3737, 8) = \gcd(3737, 8)\) because \(-3737\) is divisible by 8 (since \(3737 \div 8\) is an integer).
